{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9LEyr89ftL6dqT54a6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AtrkZ6M2wAY8xWU5cmTc7R","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211953__xee4d12/work/_research/engine/engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js","limit":270},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3018,"cache_read_input_tokens":83833,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3018},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23de6e6b-3ae6-4bf5-9764-44b18bb5857c","uuid":"f1aae284-50e0-4003-9018-a7e846280044","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:24:08.217Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj9LEiUWpYt3bmAgbz4s","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01AtrkZ6M2wAY8xWU5cmTc7R":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211953__xee4d12/work/_research/engine/engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js","limit":270}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AtrkZ6M2wAY8xWU5cmTc7R","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/*!\n2\tmy-3D2dge 3D v0.88.0: real 3D worlds under my-3D2dge games (three.js r182 and Rapier 0.19.3)\n3\thttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\n4\t\n5\tA 3D world, its physics and its camera under a my-3D2dge game. The 2D engine (engine/my-3d2dge.js) still runs the game:\n6\tits exact fixed steps, scenes, input, pause menu, settings, touch buttons, sound, the rigs and their moves, the HUD. This\n7\tmodule simulates and draws the world under the game's clear canvas. Everything is drawn by code: levels written as text,\n8\ttextures pixel by pixel, characters by the 2D engine's rigs (as cards, or as 3D puppets on the same joints), props and\n9\tpickups from four shapes. No image, model or sound files.\n10\t\n11\tAGENTS: this header is the whole manual for the 3D side; the API card (API.md) covers the 2D side (E.Game, input, rigs,\n12\tmoves, E.font, E.ui, E.Menu, audio). Read the code below to debug it, or to change it (it is yours to change, in any\n13\tway you see fit): its sections start with \"/* ===\" and a number.\n14\t\n15\t## Host it (served: browsers load modules only over http; npx serve at the repository's root, or my-3d2dge.vercel.app)\n16\t<script type=\"importmap\">{ \"imports\": { \"three\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js\",\n17\t  \"three/webgpu\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js\", \"three/tsl\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.tsl.min.js\",\n18\t  \"@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat\": \"/vendor/rapier3d-simd-compat-0.19.3/rapier.js\" } }</script>\n19\t<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; overflow: hidden; background: #000 }</style>\n20\t<div id=\"stage\" style=\"position:relative;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:hidden\">\n21\t  <canvas id=\"view\"></canvas><canvas id=\"screen\" style=\"position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%\"></canvas></div>\n22\t<script src=\"/dist/my-3d2dge.js\"></script>                   the 2D engine, a classic script, first\n23\t<script type=\"module\" src=\"/dist/my-3d2dge-3d.js\"></script>  this file\n24\t<script type=\"module\" src=\"game.js\"></script>                your game, a module (const E = My3D2dge;)\n25\tInlined into a page's own script tag instead, this file ends the page at its first closing script tag (this header has\n26\tfour): write each with a backslash before its slash, as the build's single files do.\n27\t\n28\t## Mental model\n29\t- The 2D engine's units: x east, y south, z up; 16 units = 1 metre = 1 tile; speeds in units a second; angles in\n30\t  radians from +x toward +y (0 east, PI/2 south, -PI/2 north). The axes are left-handed (three.js's are right-handed):\n31\t  a mesh of your own built in engine units comes out mirrored, its winding and turns flipped; place it in three.js's\n32\t  (E.World3D.toThree(x, y, z): x, z, y over 16).\n33\t- new E.Game({ ..., bg: null }): its canvas is clear, and the HUD draws on it over the 3D picture (r.overlay, r.text,\n34\t  E.ui, E.font) in game pixels, r.W x r.H. res: 'ps1', expand: true as in the 2D games.\n35\t- await E.World3D.init(game) once (a boot step), then new E.World3D(game, { level, ... }) for each level. In a scene:\n36\t  update(dt) { your rules, then world.step(dt) } and draw(r) { world.draw(r), then your HUD }. Paused or frozen\n37\t  (game.freeze), update doesn't run, so the world holds still and still draws. A frame between steps draws the actors\n38\t  and the camera part way from the step before (game.alpha: even motion at 144 Hz); a pose set in onDraw is placed as set.\n39\t- Deterministic: the world steps in the game's fixed steps; gameplay randomness comes from E.rng(seed); the camera's\n40\t  pose is worked out in the steps. world.reset() then the same inputs give the same world.hash() on WebGPU, WebGL 2 and\n41\t  run again. Gameplay never reads the picture or the GPU: it reads actors, props and the level.\n42\t- The camera decides what \"up the stick\" means: move with world.camera.ground(game.input.move()).\n43\t\n44\t## Quick start: a complete game (collect the gems, mind the slimes)\n45\t```js quickstart\n46\tconst E = My3D2dge;\n47\tconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, bg: null, input: E.World3D.INPUT, menu: { settings: E.World3D.SETTINGS } });\n48\tconst LEVEL = { rows: [\n49\t  '################',\n50\t  '#t............t#',\n51\t  '#..g.....==..g.#',\n52\t  '#........==....#',\n53\t  '#..s.....^^....#',\n54\t  '#.............s#',\n55\t  '#..g...@....g..#',\n56\t  '#t............t#',\n57\t  '################'],\n58\t  legend: { '=': { floor: 16 }, '^': { stairs: 'n', floor: 16 }, g: { mark: 'gem' }, s: { mark: 'slime' }, '@': { mark: 'start' } } };\n59\tlet world, hero, slimes, gems, hp, done;\n60\tconst move = [0, 0];\n61\tconst play = {\n62\t  view: 'iso', views: ['iso', 'threequarter', 'topdown'], pausable: true, touch: ['jump'], camera: { zoom: [.6, 2] },\n63\t  enter() {\n64\t    world.reset(); const rnd = E.rng(1), s = world.marks.start[0];\n65\t    hero = world.hero({ x: s.x, y: s.y, rig: new E.Humanoid({ colors: { cloth: '#2f8f86' } }) });\n66\t    slimes = world.marks.slime.map(m => world.mob({ x: m.x, y: m.y, blob: new E.Blob({ R: 6 }) }));\n67\t    gems = world.marks.gem.map(m => world.thing('gem', m.x, m.y, m.z + 2, { spin: .5, bob: 3 }));\n68\t    world.camera.follow(hero); hp = 3; done = false;\n69\t    for (const e of slimes) e.data.t = rnd() * 2;\n70\t  },\n71\t  update(dt) {\n72\t    if (game.input.pressed('camera')) world.camera.set(world.camera.mode === 'view' ? 'chase' : 'view');\n73\t    world.camera.ground(game.input.move(), move);\n74\t    hero.vx = E.approach(hero.vx, move[0] * 90, 900 * dt); hero.vy = E.approach(hero.vy, move[1] * 90, 900 * dt);\n75\t    if (Math.hypot(move[0], move[1]) > .1) hero.facing = Math.atan2(move[1], move[0]);\n76\t    if (hero.grounded && game.input.pressed('jump')) hero.jump(170);\n77\t    for (const e of slimes) {   // hop at the hero now and then; touch one: a heart lost, knocked back\n78\t      if ((e.data.t -= dt) < 0 && e.grounded) { e.data.t = 1.2; const a = Math.atan2(hero.y - e.y, hero.x - e.x); e.vx = Math.cos(a) * 60; e.vy = Math.sin(a) * 60; e.vz = 140; e.facing = a; }\n79\t      if (Math.hypot(e.x - hero.x, e.y - hero.y) < 11 && Math.abs(e.z - hero.z) < 10 && !(hero.data.inv > 0)) { hp--; hero.data.inv = 1; hero.push((hero.x - e.x) * 12, (hero.y - e.y) * 12, 120); game.shake(3); }\n80\t    }\n81\t    hero.data.inv = (hero.data.inv || 0) - dt;\n82\t    for (const t of world.touching(hero, 'gem')) { world.remove(t); gems.splice(gems.indexOf(t), 1); game.particles.glints(t.x, t.y, t.z + 6, 8, '#bff8ff'); }\n83\t    if (!done && (!gems.length || hp <= 0)) { done = true; game.note(gems.length ? 'OUCH!' : 'ALL GEMS!', 2); game.after(2, () => game.go('play')); }\n84\t    world.step(dt);\n85\t  },\n86\t  draw(r) {\n87\t    world.draw(r);\n88\t    r.overlay(g => { E.ui.hearts(g, 6, 6, Math.max(0, hp), 3); E.font.text(g, 'GEMS ' + gems.length, 6, 18, '#bff8ff'); });\n89\t  }\n90\t};\n91\tgame.start({ scenes: { play }, scene: 'play', boot: { steps: [\n92\t  ['The 3D engine', () => E.World3D.init(game)],\n93\t  ['The level', () => { world = new E.World3D(game, { level: LEVEL }); world.prepare(); }]] } });\n94\t```\n95\t\n96\t## The level: text, one character per tile; row 0 is north\n97\tlevel: { rows, legend, ground, side, colors, bottom }. A legend entry says what its character is (the defaults: '#' wall\n98\t48, 'w' wall 12, 'P' pillar 56, '.' floor, ' ' pit, 't' brazier):\n99\t  { floor: h }        walkable at height h (0 the ground; above 0 a raised floor, solid to the ground)\n100\t  { wall: h }         a solid block h tall, cut low where it stands between a view camera and the level (cut: false)\n101\t  { pillar: h }       each block of these tiles is one pillar, cut to a stump when it hides the target\n102\t  { stairs: 'n'|'s'|'e'|'w', from: 0, floor: 16 }   rising toward that side, from height `from` to `floor`\n103\t  { platform: h, thick: 4 }   a slab in the air, its top at h (walk under it); add pit: true for nothing below\n104\t  { pit: true }       no floor: a body that falls in is lost (actor.fell)\n105\t  { torch: true }     a brazier with a flickering light (the lights go to the torches nearest the target)\n106\t  { mark: 'name' }    a spot: world.marks.name -> [{ x, y, z, cx, cy }] (the tile's centre, on its surface)\n107\t  { shape: 'bench', facing, scale, mats, solid }   a shape standing on the tile (world.shape), walked round when solid\n108\tand its look: ground ('flagstone' 'grass' 'dirt' 'sand' 'snow' 'planks' 'tiles' 'plain' 'water' 'lava', or (x, y) =>\n109\t[r, g, b]) with colors { base, dark, light }, side ('brick' 'block' 'earth' 'planks' 'metal') with color (and top, line).\n110\tThe level's ground is every tile's default; its side styles the floors' edges, its wallSide the walls ('brick'; a tile's\n111\town side wins). Add looks: E.World3D.GROUND.name, E.World3D.SIDE.name.\n112\t\n113\t## The world: new E.World3D(game, o)\n114\to: { level, look: 'card' | 'puppet', res: 'pixels' | 'balanced' | 'full', gravity: 480, sky: '#06050b' or [top,\n115\thorizon], fog: { color, near, far } (units past the target) or false, ambient: [sky, ground, intensity], sun: { color,\n116\tintensity, dir: [x, y, z] (it shines along it), area, shadow }, torchLights: 6, torchShadows: 1, torchPower: 30,\n117\tlights: 2 (your own), spots: 0 (flashlights), glowLights: 4, shadows, outlines, filter, camera: { mode, proj, fov, chase, ... }, terrain (an open\n118\tworld instead of the level: below), overlay: { fov } (first person: below), onDraw: (world, r) => {} (your own 3D drawing\n119\teach frame, whichever scene draws the world) }\n120\t  world.step(dt) / world.draw(r) / world.reset() / world.hash([your numbers]) / world.prepare() (build the shaders now)\n121\t  world.dispose(): frees a world (its physics, meshes and textures); dispose a level's world before making the next\n122\t  world.width, depth (units), mw, mh (tiles), bottom, marks, torches, actors, props, platforms, things, time, stats\n123\t  world.ground(x, y)   the ground's height (a wall's top on a wall; bottom over a pit)\n124\t  world.floorAt(x, y, z)   the surface a body at height z stands on or falls to (platforms too)\n125\t  world.topH(x, y)     the top of whatever stands there (shots stop below it)\n126\t  world.tile(cx, cy), spec(cx, cy), solidTile(cx, cy)   the level's character, its legend entry, walls and pillars\n127\t  world.flow() -> flow: flow.to(x, y) aims it; flow.dir(x, y, out) -> the way there ([x, y], or null: go straight);\n128\t      it climbs stairs and gentle slopes and drops off ledges, never jumps\n129\t  world.randomFloor(rnd, minDist, fx, fy) -> [x, y]; world.clear(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1) -> a clear line of sight?\n130\t  world.ray(x, y, z, dx, dy, dz, len, { skip: actor(s), level: true (sight lines), down }) -> the first hit { x, y, z, nx,\n131\t      ny, nz, dist, actor, prop, ground } or null: hitscan, ledges, feet on the ground\n132\t  world.block({ x, y, z, w, d, h, yaw } | { x, y, z, r, h }): an invisible fixed collider (walls you draw your own way;\n133\t      z its base, as for world.box, world.thing and world.shape)\n134\t  world.near(x, y, r, kind) -> actors within r; world.touching(actor, kind) -> things it touches\n135\t  world.project(x, y, z) -> [x, y] in game pixels for the HUD (null behind the camera)\n136\t  world.remove(actor | prop | platform | thing)\n137\t\n138\t## Actors: world.hero(o) and world.mob(o)\n139\thero: a kinematic capsule walked by Rapier's character controller: it slides along walls, climbs stairs and slopes,\n140\tsteps up curbs, rides moving platforms, pushes crates and shoves mobs. mob: a dynamic body; the crowd pushes and piles\n141\tup by itself, knockback is momentum. o: { x, y, z, rig: new E.Humanoid(...) | blob: new E.Blob(...) | orb: { color, r },\n142\tr, half (the capsule: radius, half its straight part; half 0 a ball), facing, fly (no gravity), mass, trail (a color for\n143\tthe rig's weapon trail), look ('card' | 'puppet' for this one), shadow, pose: false (you pose it yourself) }\n144\tEach step you set what it wants: a.vx, a.vy (units a second on the ground: E.approach toward a target speed), a.jump(v)\n145\tor a.vz, a.facing, a.anim (what its rig does: { attack: move.state, pose: 'cheer' | 'die' | 'cast', hurt, dash, expr };\n146\ta blob's { squash, look: [dx, dy], squint, flap }); world.step moves it, reads back a.x, a.y, a.z (its feet), a.vx,\n147\ta.vy, a.vz, a.grounded, a.landed (this step), a.fell (dropped below the level), and poses its rig.\n148\t  a.place(x, y, z), a.push(vx, vy, vz) (knockback), a.setSolid(false) (fallen: it stops blocking the others), a.remove(),\n149\t  a.resize(half) (a crouch, a slide: the capsule shorter, the feet kept; look up with world.ray before standing)\n150\t  a.flash (a hit flash while above 0: count it down yourself, a.flash -= dt), a.fade (0..1), a.sink (units drawn into the floor: spawning, sinking away), a.visible,\n151\t  a.data (yours). E.Attack, E.Combo and E.MOVES work as in 2D: attack.hits(list, e => E.inArc(a, a.facing, e, range,\n152\t  half), e => ...) on actors.\n153\t\n154\t## Props, platforms and things\n155\t  world.shape(id, x, y, z, { facing, scale, mats, flip, params, solid: true }): a shape (docs/ASSETS.md: an E.SHAPES id,\n156\t  a store set's 'SET:id' after E.addAssets, or an entry) in 3D, from the 2D engine's parts and materials, solid as\n157\t  map.solid's box. A reset takes yours away (the legend's stand again); world.shapes holds them; world.remove(s)\n158\t  world.crate(x, y, z, yaw), world.barrel(x, y, z): dynamic bodies (z their centre; left out, on the floor); world.knock(p, fromX, fromY, dv, up) throws one;\n159\t  world.box({ x, y, z, w, d, h, color, side, fixed, mass }); a prop has x, y, z, q (its rotation), data\n160\t  world.platform({ w, d, h, path: [[x, y, z], ...] (its top's points), speed, wait, loop, side, color }): a platform that\n161\t  moves (there and back, or round with loop); heroes on it ride it, bodies on it are carried\n162\t  world.thing(kind, x, y, z, o): drawn by code: coin gem heart key star potion chest door flag sign lever pad spring\n163\t  tree bush rock mushroom fence crystal trunk (an item box) typewriter (a save point); o: { yaw, spin (turns a second),\n164\t  bob, size, color, open (0..1), on, solid: true | [w, d, h] (a block where it stands: world.setSolid(t, false) opens\n165\t  it), data }. Add a kind:\n166\t  E.World3D.THINGS.lamp = (pen, t, time) => { pen.tube(0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 20, 1, '#555').glow(0, 0, 21, 2, '#ffd36a'); }\n167\t  A door: { w (32, across its local x), h (40), swing: true (leaves on hinges; else a gate that rises), locked: 'iron' (a\n168\t  key's id) }. world.reach(hero, 14, kinds) -> the thing in front of it within reach (what a check button acts on);\n169\t  world.unlock(door, inv) -> 'open' | 'unlocked' (the key taken from an E.RPG inventory) | 'locked';\n170\t  world.through(door, hero, { then }): the door opening between rooms (Resident Evil's): the camera goes through as it\n171\t  swings open, the hero comes out beyond it; while world.passing the world holds still: skip your rules\n172\t\n173\t## Drawing for one frame (in draw, before world.draw(r))\n174\t  world.arc(x, y, z, r0, r1, a0, a1, color, alpha): a flat arc on the ground (a telegraph)\n175\t  world.glow(x, y, z, r, color, { core, light: true }): a glowing ball (a bolt); the first four asked for light the scene\n176\t  world.pen.at(x, y, z, yaw, size, pitch, roll).box(x, y, z, w, d, h, color).ball(x, y, z, rx, ry, rz, color).tube(x0, y0, z0, x1,\n177\t      y1, z1, r, color).cone(...base to tip).bar(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, w, t, color).glow(x, y, z, r, color)\n178\t      .slab(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, ax, ay, az, w, t, color) (a box from one point to the other, w wide along a: any lean)\n179\t  world.light({ color, reach, power, flicker }) (made once, with the world): a light; set its x, y, z and on each frame\n180\t  world.flashlight(hero, { color, reach, angle, power, flicker: 0..1 (a failing bulb) }) (a world made with { spots: 1 }):\n181\t  a spot from its hand along its facing, every frame, casting shadows; .on\n182\t  game.particles (sparks, dust, bits, rings, glints, fire, text): drawn in 3D; they land on the level; text goes on the HUD\n183\t  game.shake(n), game.flash(color), game.freeze(s), game.note(text): as in 2D\n184\t\n185\t## The camera: world.camera\n186\t  modes: 'view' (the 2D engine's views as real 3D cameras following camera.target: game.view (game.nextView()),\n187\t  game.yaw (game.rotateView(45)): the starter's shell binds V and [ ] to them, the engine no key; game.zoom (the wheel,\n188\t  a pinch, Settings, where the scene's camera.zoom allows); proj 'persp' | 'ortho'; dist; walls in\n189\t  front cut low), 'chase' (behind the target; it swings round behind as the target moves; a click captures the mouse to\n190\t  turn it), 'first' (the target's eyes), 'fly', 'fixed' (camera.fixed = { x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, fov }: your own),\n191\t  'zones' (Resident Evil's: camera.zones = [{ box: [x0, y0, x1, y1], at: [x, y, z], look: [x, y, z] (fixed) | follow:\n192\t  true (turning after the target) | rail: [[x, y, z], [x, y, z]] (sliding level with it), fov (framed for 4:3: a taller\n193\t  screen widens it) }]: the target's zone is the camera, cut once it is camera.margin (8) units in (camera.zone,\n194\t  camera.cuts); across a cut ground() keeps the old way while the stick is held)\n195\t  camera: { capture: true (a click captures the mouse in any mode; camera.takeMouse(out) -> its [dx, dy] since the last\n196\t  call: turn your own camera), near, far (units) }; camera.target also sizes the outlines and centres the sun's shadow\n197\t  camera.set(mode), camera.follow(actor), camera.ground(move, out) -> the stick turned to the ground,\n198\t  camera.aim(actor) -> the angle the mouse (on the floor) or right stick points from it, or null; camera.heading,\n199\t  camera.pose, camera.chase = { pitch, dist, fov, height, auto }, camera.first = { pitch, fov }\n200\t  camera.steer(hero, move, dt, out) -> the way to go by the player's setting (game.settings.define(E.World3D.CONTROLS)):\n201\t  ground(), or tank controls (up forward along hero.facing, down back, left and right turn it: set facing yourself only\n202\t  when !camera.tank)\n203\t  Lock-on (Zelda's targeting): camera.lock(hero, mobs, { range: 160 }) -> the one in sight (alive, in range, a clear\n204\t  line) nearest where hero faces, or null; camera.cycle(mobs, 1 | -1) the next round the hero; camera.unlock();\n205\t  camera.lockOn. The chase and first cameras swing behind the hero to frame both, the view frames both, ground() strafes\n206\t  round it, a reticle marks it (camera.reticle: a color, false); it lets go when the target dies (alive = false), leaves\n207\t  or goes past 1.25 times the range. Turn the hero to it yourself\n208\t\n209\t## Open worlds: new E.World3D(game, { terrain: { height: (x, y) => z, ... } })\n210\tterrain: { size (32768: two kilometres), height, color: (x, y, z, nz, out) => [r, g, b] (0..255), cell (32), chunk (32\n211\tcells), far (draw distance), physics (heightfields this near an actor), detail (1.7), rock: { colors, band, slope: [s0,\n212\ts1] } (strata where it steepens), speckle, mottle, bottom }. Streamed: a chunk is sampled when first asked about, its\n213\tcollider made near actors (world.step), its meshes near the camera (world.draw: finer near). world.ground, floorAt, topH\n214\tand world.terrain.normal(x, y) read the triangles Rapier collides with; flow() goes straight. sky: { top, horizon, ground,\n215\tsun, haze } is a dome; fog: { color, near, far }. Keep height() fast: it runs per sample.\n216\t\n217\t## Vehicles, tracks, flight (the RACING and FLIGHT slices show them)\n218\tworld.vehicle({ kind: 'kart' | 'car' | 'hover', x, y, z, angle, rig (its driver, seated), color, and the drive module's\n219\tE.Car options over the kind's (top, accel, brake, turn, grip, drift, hop...), surfaces, ground: (x, y) => tag }): a ball\n220\tRapier rolls (walls, bumps, ramps, jumps) steered by E.Car's arcade handling; an actor. Each step v.update(dt, null,\n221\t{ steer, gas, brake, drift }) (or an input), then world.step; it reads speed, slide, angle, drifting, charge (a kart's\n222\tdrift boost), boostT, onGround, surface ('road', 'boost', a track's off, the level's ground: grass, sand... slow it),\n223\tbumped; v.boost(sec, power), v.spinOut(sec). E.Race (the drive module) races vehicles as it races E.Cars.\n224\tworld.track({ path: new E.Path(points [x, y, z], { closed: true, smooth: 'catmull' }), width: 96, bank: .25 (radians at\n225\tthe tightest bends), walls: true, kerb: 8, pads: [[d, across]] (boost pads), gaps: [[d0, d1, side]] (no wall: a\n226\tshortcut's way off), off (the surface beside it, 'grass'; null: the ground's own), surface: 'road' (a shortcut's\n227\t'dirt'), color, line }): the road and its walls, drawn\n228\tand solid (heights in the path: hills, a hump to jump; banked about the low edge); track.at(d) -> { x, y, z, angle, bank\n229\t}, track.where(x, y) -> { d, across, z }, track.surface(x, y). A terrain under it keeps below it (your height function).\n230\tworld.flyer({ x, y, z, yaw, speed: 300, min, max (brake, boost), turn, climb, bank, invert, low (least height), bounds:\n231\t[x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1] | rail: { path, speed, w, h } (Star Fox: the rail's point rides on, the ship moves about a w x h\n232\twindow across it) }): each step f.update(dt, { steer: [x, y], boost, brake, roll: -1 | 1 (a barrel roll: f.rolling),\n233\tloop }); f.x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, speed, frame (the rail's point), hitGround; f.seek(list, { cone, range }): what a\n234\tcharged shot locks on; f.at(): where to draw it this frame. world.pen.at(x, y, z, yaw, size, pitch, roll) tips the pen.\n235\tcamera 'behind': behind the target's heading (yaw, angle or facing) and pitch, swinging after it (camera.behind = { dist,\n236\theight, ahead, lag, fov, roll }): a kart's camera, a ship's (follow f.frame on a rail).\n237\tSplit screen: game.splitScreen(2) and world.addCamera(o): viewport i draws through world.cameras[i]; world.project\n238\tanswers in the viewport drawn last; no filter while split.\n239\t\n240\t## First person and third: a shooter (the starter's SHOOTER slice shows it all)\n241\tcamera 'fixed' with capture: each step turn by camera.takeMouse(), set camera.fixed (the eyes, or over the shoulder pulled\n242\tin by world.ray). overlay: { fov } makes world.overlay = { scene, camera, pen, on }: drawn after the world, its depth\n243\tcleared (the gun never sinks into a wall), lit like the world. overlay.pen is a pen in the eye's frame (engine units: x\n244\tahead, y right, z up): draw the arms and gun in onDraw; world.pen there draws bodies (the pens empty after each frame).\n245\t\n246\t## The look\n247\t  world.look = 'card' | 'puppet'; world.res = 'pixels' | 'balanced' | 'full'; world.shadows; world.outlines\n248\t  world.filter = { look: 'clean' | 'cel' (Comic cel: flat bands of light, ink) | 'pixel' (big dithered pixels), apply:\n249\t  'all' | 'objects' | 'env', bloom, fxaa, bands, ink, inkW, punch, px, levels, dither }\n250\t  E.World3D.SETTINGS in the game's menu lets the player pick the look, the picture, shadows and the filter.\n251\t  E.World3D.INPUT: WASD or arrows move, Space jumps, J or a click attacks, Shift dashes, E skill, Q lock, C camera.\n252\t\n253\t## Your own three.js\n254\tE.THREE (three/webgpu), E.TSL, E.RAPIER; world.scene, world.pw (Rapier's world), E.World3D.toThree(x, y, z) (engine\n255\tunits to three's metres, y up). The rules: WebGPURenderer and node materials only (MeshLambertNodeMaterial,\n256\tMeshToonNodeMaterial, MeshBasicNodeMaterial, TSL): never WebGLRenderer, ShaderMaterial, onBeforeCompile, EffectComposer or\n257\tthree/addons (not vendored); no compute shaders or storage buffers; nothing read back from the GPU. An InstancedMesh with\n258\tover 1,000 instances never uses DynamicDrawUsage (r182 drops its updates). Make meshes and lights when the world is made,\n259\tnot mid-game (a new material builds its shader: a stall).\n260\t\n261\t## Tests\n262\tHeadless Chromium runs it on WebGL 2 (?backend=webgl) and WebGPU (SwiftShader). world.hash() is the proof; game.advance(s)\n263\truns fixed steps at once; game.input.hold / tap script input. The kits expose window.__game.\n264\t*/\n265\timport * as THREE from 'three/webgpu';\n266\timport * as TSL from 'three/tsl';\n267\timport RAPIER from '@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat';\n268\t\n269\t/* =============================================================================\n270\t * 1. SETUP  units, helpers, collision groups, the page's renderer (World3D.init)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23de6e6b-3ae6-4bf5-9764-44b18bb5857c","uuid":"2191184d-d197-4f04-9e7f-9aa829200b2f","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:24:08.234Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211953__xee4d12/work/_research/engine/engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js","content":"/*!\nmy-3D2dge 3D v0.88.0: real 3D worlds under my-3D2dge games (three.js r182 and Rapier 0.19.3)\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\n\nA 3D world, its physics and its camera under a my-3D2dge game. The 2D engine (engine/my-3d2dge.js) still runs the game:\nits exact fixed steps, scenes, input, pause menu, settings, touch buttons, sound, the rigs and their moves, the HUD. This\nmodule simulates and draws the world under the game's clear canvas. Everything is drawn by code: levels written as text,\ntextures pixel by pixel, characters by the 2D engine's rigs (as cards, or as 3D puppets on the same joints), props and\npickups from four shapes. No image, model or sound files.\n\nAGENTS: this header is the whole manual for the 3D side; the API card (API.md) covers the 2D side (E.Game, input, rigs,\nmoves, E.font, E.ui, E.Menu, audio). Read the code below to debug it, or to change it (it is yours to change, in any\nway you see fit): its sections start with \"/* ===\" and a number.\n\n## Host it (served: browsers load modules only over http; npx serve at the repository's root, or my-3d2dge.vercel.app)\n<script type=\"importmap\">{ \"imports\": { \"three\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js\",\n  \"three/webgpu\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js\", \"three/tsl\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.tsl.min.js\",\n  \"@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat\": \"/vendor/rapier3d-simd-compat-0.19.3/rapier.js\" } }</script>\n<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; overflow: hidden; background: #000 }</style>\n<div id=\"stage\" style=\"position:relative;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:hidden\">\n  <canvas id=\"view\"></canvas><canvas id=\"screen\" style=\"position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%\"></canvas></div>\n<script src=\"/dist/my-3d2dge.js\"></script>                   the 2D engine, a classic script, first\n<script type=\"module\" src=\"/dist/my-3d2dge-3d.js\"></script>  this file\n<script type=\"module\" src=\"game.js\"></script>                your game, a module (const E = My3D2dge;)\nInlined into a page's own script tag instead, this file ends the page at its first closing script tag (this header has\nfour): write each with a backslash before its slash, as the build's single files do.\n\n## Mental model\n- The 2D engine's units: x east, y south, z up; 16 units = 1 metre = 1 tile; speeds in units a second; angles in\n  radians from +x toward +y (0 east, PI/2 south, -PI/2 north). The axes are left-handed (three.js's are right-handed):\n  a mesh of your own built in engine units comes out mirrored, its winding and turns flipped; place it in three.js's\n  (E.World3D.toThree(x, y, z): x, z, y over 16).\n- new E.Game({ ..., bg: null }): its canvas is clear, and the HUD draws on it over the 3D picture (r.overlay, r.text,\n  E.ui, E.font) in game pixels, r.W x r.H. res: 'ps1', expand: true as in the 2D games.\n- await E.World3D.init(game) once (a boot step), then new E.World3D(game, { level, ... }) for each level. In a scene:\n  update(dt) { your rules, then world.step(dt) } and draw(r) { world.draw(r), then your HUD }. Paused or frozen\n  (game.freeze), update doesn't run, so the world holds still and still draws. A frame between steps draws the actors\n  and the camera part way from the step before (game.alpha: even motion at 144 Hz); a pose set in onDraw is placed as set.\n- Deterministic: the world steps in the game's fixed steps; gameplay randomness comes from E.rng(seed); the camera's\n  pose is worked out in the steps. world.reset() then the same inputs give the same world.hash() on WebGPU, WebGL 2 and\n  run again. Gameplay never reads the picture or the GPU: it reads actors, props and the level.\n- The camera decides what \"up the stick\" means: move with world.camera.ground(game.input.move()).\n\n## Quick start: a complete game (collect the gems, mind the slimes)\n```js quickstart\nconst E = My3D2dge;\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, bg: null, input: E.World3D.INPUT, menu: { settings: E.World3D.SETTINGS } });\nconst LEVEL = { rows: [\n  '################',\n  '#t............t#',\n  '#..g.....==..g.#',\n  '#........==....#',\n  '#..s.....^^....#',\n  '#.............s#',\n  '#..g...@....g..#',\n  '#t............t#',\n  '################'],\n  legend: { '=': { floor: 16 }, '^': { stairs: 'n', floor: 16 }, g: { mark: 'gem' }, s: { mark: 'slime' }, '@': { mark: 'start' } } };\nlet world, hero, slimes, gems, hp, done;\nconst move = [0, 0];\nconst play = {\n  view: 'iso', views: ['iso', 'threequarter', 'topdown'], pausable: true, touch: ['jump'], camera: { zoom: [.6, 2] },\n  enter() {\n    world.reset(); const rnd = E.rng(1), s = world.marks.start[0];\n    hero = world.hero({ x: s.x, y: s.y, rig: new E.Humanoid({ colors: { cloth: '#2f8f86' } }) });\n    slimes = world.marks.slime.map(m => world.mob({ x: m.x, y: m.y, blob: new E.Blob({ R: 6 }) }));\n    gems = world.marks.gem.map(m => world.thing('gem', m.x, m.y, m.z + 2, { spin: .5, bob: 3 }));\n    world.camera.follow(hero); hp = 3; done = false;\n    for (const e of slimes) e.data.t = rnd() * 2;\n  },\n  update(dt) {\n    if (game.input.pressed('camera')) world.camera.set(world.camera.mode === 'view' ? 'chase' : 'view');\n    world.camera.ground(game.input.move(), move);\n    hero.vx = E.approach(hero.vx, move[0] * 90, 900 * dt); hero.vy = E.approach(hero.vy, move[1] * 90, 900 * dt);\n    if (Math.hypot(move[0], move[1]) > .1) hero.facing = Math.atan2(move[1], move[0]);\n    if (hero.grounded && game.input.pressed('jump')) hero.jump(170);\n    for (const e of slimes) {   // hop at the hero now and then; touch one: a heart lost, knocked back\n      if ((e.data.t -= dt) < 0 && e.grounded) { e.data.t = 1.2; const a = Math.atan2(hero.y - e.y, hero.x - e.x); e.vx = Math.cos(a) * 60; e.vy = Math.sin(a) * 60; e.vz = 140; e.facing = a; }\n      if (Math.hypot(e.x - hero.x, e.y - hero.y) < 11 && Math.abs(e.z - hero.z) < 10 && !(hero.data.inv > 0)) { hp--; hero.data.inv = 1; hero.push((hero.x - e.x) * 12, (hero.y - e.y) * 12, 120); game.shake(3); }\n    }\n    hero.data.inv = (hero.data.inv || 0) - dt;\n    for (const t of world.touching(hero, 'gem')) { world.remove(t); gems.splice(gems.indexOf(t), 1); game.particles.glints(t.x, t.y, t.z + 6, 8, '#bff8ff'); }\n    if (!done && (!gems.length || hp <= 0)) { done = true; game.note(gems.length ? 'OUCH!' : 'ALL GEMS!', 2); game.after(2, () => game.go('play')); }\n    world.step(dt);\n  },\n  draw(r) {\n    world.draw(r);\n    r.overlay(g => { E.ui.hearts(g, 6, 6, Math.max(0, hp), 3); E.font.text(g, 'GEMS ' + gems.length, 6, 18, '#bff8ff'); });\n  }\n};\ngame.start({ scenes: { play }, scene: 'play', boot: { steps: [\n  ['The 3D engine', () => E.World3D.init(game)],\n  ['The level', () => { world = new E.World3D(game, { level: LEVEL }); world.prepare(); }]] } });\n```\n\n## The level: text, one character per tile; row 0 is north\nlevel: { rows, legend, ground, side, colors, bottom }. A legend entry says what its character is (the defaults: '#' wall\n48, 'w' wall 12, 'P' pillar 56, '.' floor, ' ' pit, 't' brazier):\n  { floor: h }        walkable at height h (0 the ground; above 0 a raised floor, solid to the ground)\n  { wall: h }         a solid block h tall, cut low where it stands between a view camera and the level (cut: false)\n  { pillar: h }       each block of these tiles is one pillar, cut to a stump when it hides the target\n  { stairs: 'n'|'s'|'e'|'w', from: 0, floor: 16 }   rising toward that side, from height `from` to `floor`\n  { platform: h, thick: 4 }   a slab in the air, its top at h (walk under it); add pit: true for nothing below\n  { pit: true }       no floor: a body that falls in is lost (actor.fell)\n  { torch: true }     a brazier with a flickering light (the lights go to the torches nearest the target)\n  { mark: 'name' }    a spot: world.marks.name -> [{ x, y, z, cx, cy }] (the tile's centre, on its surface)\n  { shape: 'bench', facing, scale, mats, solid }   a shape standing on the tile (world.shape), walked round when solid\nand its look: ground ('flagstone' 'grass' 'dirt' 'sand' 'snow' 'planks' 'tiles' 'plain' 'water' 'lava', or (x, y) =>\n[r, g, b]) with colors { base, dark, light }, side ('brick' 'block' 'earth' 'planks' 'metal') with color (and top, line).\nThe level's ground is every tile's default; its side styles the floors' edges, its wallSide the walls ('brick'; a tile's\nown side wins). Add looks: E.World3D.GROUND.name, E.World3D.SIDE.name.\n\n## The world: new E.World3D(game, o)\no: { level, look: 'card' | 'puppet', res: 'pixels' | 'balanced' | 'full', gravity: 480, sky: '#06050b' or [top,\nhorizon], fog: { color, near, far } (units past the target) or false, ambient: [sky, ground, intensity], sun: { color,\nintensity, dir: [x, y, z] (it shines along it), area, shadow }, torchLights: 6, torchShadows: 1, torchPower: 30,\nlights: 2 (your own), spots: 0 (flashlights), glowLights: 4, shadows, outlines, filter, camera: { mode, proj, fov, chase, ... }, terrain (an open\nworld instead of the level: below), overlay: { fov } (first person: below), onDraw: (world, r) => {} (your own 3D drawing\neach frame, whichever scene draws the world) }\n  world.step(dt) / world.draw(r) / world.reset() / world.hash([your numbers]) / world.prepare() (build the shaders now)\n  world.dispose(): frees a world (its physics, meshes and textures); dispose a level's world before making the next\n  world.width, depth (units), mw, mh (tiles), bottom, marks, torches, actors, props, platforms, things, time, stats\n  world.ground(x, y)   the ground's height (a wall's top on a wall; bottom over a pit)\n  world.floorAt(x, y, z)   the surface a body at height z stands on or falls to (platforms too)\n  world.topH(x, y)     the top of whatever stands there (shots stop below it)\n  world.tile(cx, cy), spec(cx, cy), solidTile(cx, cy)   the level's character, its legend entry, walls and pillars\n  world.flow() -> flow: flow.to(x, y) aims it; flow.dir(x, y, out) -> the way there ([x, y], or null: go straight);\n      it climbs stairs and gentle slopes and drops off ledges, never jumps\n  world.randomFloor(rnd, minDist, fx, fy) -> [x, y]; world.clear(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1) -> a clear line of sight?\n  world.ray(x, y, z, dx, dy, dz, len, { skip: actor(s), level: true (sight lines), down }) -> the first hit { x, y, z, nx,\n      ny, nz, dist, actor, prop, ground } or null: hitscan, ledges, feet on the ground\n  world.block({ x, y, z, w, d, h, yaw } | { x, y, z, r, h }): an invisible fixed collider (walls you draw your own way;\n      z its base, as for world.box, world.thing and world.shape)\n  world.near(x, y, r, kind) -> actors within r; world.touching(actor, kind) -> things it touches\n  world.project(x, y, z) -> [x, y] in game pixels for the HUD (null behind the camera)\n  world.remove(actor | prop | platform | thing)\n\n## Actors: world.hero(o) and world.mob(o)\nhero: a kinematic capsule walked by Rapier's character controller: it slides along walls, climbs stairs and slopes,\nsteps up curbs, rides moving platforms, pushes crates and shoves mobs. mob: a dynamic body; the crowd pushes and piles\nup by itself, knockback is momentum. o: { x, y, z, rig: new E.Humanoid(...) | blob: new E.Blob(...) | orb: { color, r },\nr, half (the capsule: radius, half its straight part; half 0 a ball), facing, fly (no gravity), mass, trail (a color for\nthe rig's weapon trail), look ('card' | 'puppet' for this one), shadow, pose: false (you pose it yourself) }\nEach step you set what it wants: a.vx, a.vy (units a second on the ground: E.approach toward a target speed), a.jump(v)\nor a.vz, a.facing, a.anim (what its rig does: { attack: move.state, pose: 'cheer' | 'die' | 'cast', hurt, dash, expr };\na blob's { squash, look: [dx, dy], squint, flap }); world.step moves it, reads back a.x, a.y, a.z (its feet), a.vx,\na.vy, a.vz, a.grounded, a.landed (this step), a.fell (dropped below the level), and poses its rig.\n  a.place(x, y, z), a.push(vx, vy, vz) (knockback), a.setSolid(false) (fallen: it stops blocking the others), a.remove(),\n  a.resize(half) (a crouch, a slide: the capsule shorter, the feet kept; look up with world.ray before standing)\n  a.flash (a hit flash while above 0: count it down yourself, a.flash -= dt), a.fade (0..1), a.sink (units drawn into the floor: spawning, sinking away), a.visible,\n  a.data (yours). E.Attack, E.Combo and E.MOVES work as in 2D: attack.hits(list, e => E.inArc(a, a.facing, e, range,\n  half), e => ...) on actors.\n\n## Props, platforms and things\n  world.shape(id, x, y, z, { facing, scale, mats, flip, params, solid: true }): a shape (docs/ASSETS.md: an E.SHAPES id,\n  a store set's 'SET:id' after E.addAssets, or an entry) in 3D, from the 2D engine's parts and materials, solid as\n  map.solid's box. A reset takes yours away (the legend's stand again); world.shapes holds them; world.remove(s)\n  world.crate(x, y, z, yaw), world.barrel(x, y, z): dynamic bodies (z their centre; left out, on the floor); world.knock(p, fromX, fromY, dv, up) throws one;\n  world.box({ x, y, z, w, d, h, color, side, fixed, mass }); a prop has x, y, z, q (its rotation), data\n  world.platform({ w, d, h, path: [[x, y, z], ...] (its top's points), speed, wait, loop, side, color }): a platform that\n  moves (there and back, or round with loop); heroes on it ride it, bodies on it are carried\n  world.thing(kind, x, y, z, o): drawn by code: coin gem heart key star potion chest door flag sign lever pad spring\n  tree bush rock mushroom fence crystal trunk (an item box) typewriter (a save point); o: { yaw, spin (turns a second),\n  bob, size, color, open (0..1), on, solid: true | [w, d, h] (a block where it stands: world.setSolid(t, false) opens\n  it), data }. Add a kind:\n  E.World3D.THINGS.lamp = (pen, t, time) => { pen.tube(0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 20, 1, '#555').glow(0, 0, 21, 2, '#ffd36a'); }\n  A door: { w (32, across its local x), h (40), swing: true (leaves on hinges; else a gate that rises), locked: 'iron' (a\n  key's id) }. world.reach(hero, 14, kinds) -> the thing in front of it within reach (what a check button acts on);\n  world.unlock(door, inv) -> 'open' | 'unlocked' (the key taken from an E.RPG inventory) | 'locked';\n  world.through(door, hero, { then }): the door opening between rooms (Resident Evil's): the camera goes through as it\n  swings open, the hero comes out beyond it; while world.passing the world holds still: skip your rules\n\n## Drawing for one frame (in draw, before world.draw(r))\n  world.arc(x, y, z, r0, r1, a0, a1, color, alpha): a flat arc on the ground (a telegraph)\n  world.glow(x, y, z, r, color, { core, light: true }): a glowing ball (a bolt); the first four asked for light the scene\n  world.pen.at(x, y, z, yaw, size, pitch, roll).box(x, y, z, w, d, h, color).ball(x, y, z, rx, ry, rz, color).tube(x0, y0, z0, x1,\n      y1, z1, r, color).cone(...base to tip).bar(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, w, t, color).glow(x, y, z, r, color)\n      .slab(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, ax, ay, az, w, t, color) (a box from one point to the other, w wide along a: any lean)\n  world.light({ color, reach, power, flicker }) (made once, with the world): a light; set its x, y, z and on each frame\n  world.flashlight(hero, { color, reach, angle, power, flicker: 0..1 (a failing bulb) }) (a world made with { spots: 1 }):\n  a spot from its hand along its facing, every frame, casting shadows; .on\n  game.particles (sparks, dust, bits, rings, glints, fire, text): drawn in 3D; they land on the level; text goes on the HUD\n  game.shake(n), game.flash(color), game.freeze(s), game.note(text): as in 2D\n\n## The camera: world.camera\n  modes: 'view' (the 2D engine's views as real 3D cameras following camera.target: game.view (game.nextView()),\n  game.yaw (game.rotateView(45)): the starter's shell binds V and [ ] to them, the engine no key; game.zoom (the wheel,\n  a pinch, Settings, where the scene's camera.zoom allows); proj 'persp' | 'ortho'; dist; walls in\n  front cut low), 'chase' (behind the target; it swings round behind as the target moves; a click captures the mouse to\n  turn it), 'first' (the target's eyes), 'fly', 'fixed' (camera.fixed = { x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, fov }: your own),\n  'zones' (Resident Evil's: camera.zones = [{ box: [x0, y0, x1, y1], at: [x, y, z], look: [x, y, z] (fixed) | follow:\n  true (turning after the target) | rail: [[x, y, z], [x, y, z]] (sliding level with it), fov (framed for 4:3: a taller\n  screen widens it) }]: the target's zone is the camera, cut once it is camera.margin (8) units in (camera.zone,\n  camera.cuts); across a cut ground() keeps the old way while the stick is held)\n  camera: { capture: true (a click captures the mouse in any mode; camera.takeMouse(out) -> its [dx, dy] since the last\n  call: turn your own camera), near, far (units) }; camera.target also sizes the outlines and centres the sun's shadow\n  camera.set(mode), camera.follow(actor), camera.ground(move, out) -> the stick turned to the ground,\n  camera.aim(actor) -> the angle the mouse (on the floor) or right stick points from it, or null; camera.heading,\n  camera.pose, camera.chase = { pitch, dist, fov, height, auto }, camera.first = { pitch, fov }\n  camera.steer(hero, move, dt, out) -> the way to go by the player's setting (game.settings.define(E.World3D.CONTROLS)):\n  ground(), or tank controls (up forward along hero.facing, down back, left and right turn it: set facing yourself only\n  when !camera.tank)\n  Lock-on (Zelda's targeting): camera.lock(hero, mobs, { range: 160 }) -> the one in sight (alive, in range, a clear\n  line) nearest where hero faces, or null; camera.cycle(mobs, 1 | -1) the next round the hero; camera.unlock();\n  camera.lockOn. The chase and first cameras swing behind the hero to frame both, the view frames both, ground() strafes\n  round it, a reticle marks it (camera.reticle: a color, false); it lets go when the target dies (alive = false), leaves\n  or goes past 1.25 times the range. Turn the hero to it yourself\n\n## Open worlds: new E.World3D(game, { terrain: { height: (x, y) => z, ... } })\nterrain: { size (32768: two kilometres), height, color: (x, y, z, nz, out) => [r, g, b] (0..255), cell (32), chunk (32\ncells), far (draw distance), physics (heightfields this near an actor), detail (1.7), rock: { colors, band, slope: [s0,\ns1] } (strata where it steepens), speckle, mottle, bottom }. Streamed: a chunk is sampled when first asked about, its\ncollider made near actors (world.step), its meshes near the camera (world.draw: finer near). world.ground, floorAt, topH\nand world.terrain.normal(x, y) read the triangles Rapier collides with; flow() goes straight. sky: { top, horizon, ground,\nsun, haze } is a dome; fog: { color, near, far }. Keep height() fast: it runs per sample.\n\n## Vehicles, tracks, flight (the RACING and FLIGHT slices show them)\nworld.vehicle({ kind: 'kart' | 'car' | 'hover', x, y, z, angle, rig (its driver, seated), color, and the drive module's\nE.Car options over the kind's (top, accel, brake, turn, grip, drift, hop...), surfaces, ground: (x, y) => tag }): a ball\nRapier rolls (walls, bumps, ramps, jumps) steered by E.Car's arcade handling; an actor. Each step v.update(dt, null,\n{ steer, gas, brake, drift }) (or an input), then world.step; it reads speed, slide, angle, drifting, charge (a kart's\ndrift boost), boostT, onGround, surface ('road', 'boost', a track's off, the level's ground: grass, sand... slow it),\nbumped; v.boost(sec, power), v.spinOut(sec). E.Race (the drive module) races vehicles as it races E.Cars.\nworld.track({ path: new E.Path(points [x, y, z], { closed: true, smooth: 'catmull' }), width: 96, bank: .25 (radians at\nthe tightest bends), walls: true, kerb: 8, pads: [[d, across]] (boost pads), gaps: [[d0, d1, side]] (no wall: a\nshortcut's way off), off (the surface beside it, 'grass'; null: the ground's own), surface: 'road' (a shortcut's\n'dirt'), color, line }): the road and its walls, drawn\nand solid (heights in the path: hills, a hump to jump; banked about the low edge); track.at(d) -> { x, y, z, angle, bank\n}, track.where(x, y) -> { d, across, z }, track.surface(x, y). A terrain under it keeps below it (your height function).\nworld.flyer({ x, y, z, yaw, speed: 300, min, max (brake, boost), turn, climb, bank, invert, low (least height), bounds:\n[x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1] | rail: { path, speed, w, h } (Star Fox: the rail's point rides on, the ship moves about a w x h\nwindow across it) }): each step f.update(dt, { steer: [x, y], boost, brake, roll: -1 | 1 (a barrel roll: f.rolling),\nloop }); f.x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, speed, frame (the rail's point), hitGround; f.seek(list, { cone, range }): what a\ncharged shot locks on; f.at(): where to draw it this frame. world.pen.at(x, y, z, yaw, size, pitch, roll) tips the pen.\ncamera 'behind': behind the target's heading (yaw, angle or facing) and pitch, swinging after it (camera.behind = { dist,\nheight, ahead, lag, fov, roll }): a kart's camera, a ship's (follow f.frame on a rail).\nSplit screen: game.splitScreen(2) and world.addCamera(o): viewport i draws through world.cameras[i]; world.project\nanswers in the viewport drawn last; no filter while split.\n\n## First person and third: a shooter (the starter's SHOOTER slice shows it all)\ncamera 'fixed' with capture: each step turn by camera.takeMouse(), set camera.fixed (the eyes, or over the shoulder pulled\nin by world.ray). overlay: { fov } makes world.overlay = { scene, camera, pen, on }: drawn after the world, its depth\ncleared (the gun never sinks into a wall), lit like the world. overlay.pen is a pen in the eye's frame (engine units: x\nahead, y right, z up): draw the arms and gun in onDraw; world.pen there draws bodies (the pens empty after each frame).\n\n## The look\n  world.look = 'card' | 'puppet'; world.res = 'pixels' | 'balanced' | 'full'; world.shadows; world.outlines\n  world.filter = { look: 'clean' | 'cel' (Comic cel: flat bands of light, ink) | 'pixel' (big dithered pixels), apply:\n  'all' | 'objects' | 'env', bloom, fxaa, bands, ink, inkW, punch, px, levels, dither }\n  E.World3D.SETTINGS in the game's menu lets the player pick the look, the picture, shadows and the filter.\n  E.World3D.INPUT: WASD or arrows move, Space jumps, J or a click attacks, Shift dashes, E skill, Q lock, C camera.\n\n## Your own three.js\nE.THREE (three/webgpu), E.TSL, E.RAPIER; world.scene, world.pw (Rapier's world), E.World3D.toThree(x, y, z) (engine\nunits to three's metres, y up). The rules: WebGPURenderer and node materials only (MeshLambertNodeMaterial,\nMeshToonNodeMaterial, MeshBasicNodeMaterial, TSL): never WebGLRenderer, ShaderMaterial, onBeforeCompile, EffectComposer or\nthree/addons (not vendored); no compute shaders or storage buffers; nothing read back from the GPU. An InstancedMesh with\nover 1,000 instances never uses DynamicDrawUsage (r182 drops its updates). Make meshes and lights when the world is made,\nnot mid-game (a new material builds its shader: a stall).\n\n## Tests\nHeadless Chromium runs it on WebGL 2 (?backend=webgl) and WebGPU (SwiftShader). world.hash() is the proof; game.advance(s)\nruns fixed steps at once; game.input.hold / tap script input. The kits expose window.__game.\n*/\nimport * as THREE from 'three/webgpu';\nimport * as TSL from 'three/tsl';\nimport RAPIER from '@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat';\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * 1. SETUP  units, helpers, collision groups, the page's renderer (World3D.init)","numLines":270,"startLine":1,"totalLines":3311}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AtrkZ6M2wAY8xWU5cmTc7R","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9LEyr89ftL6dqT54a6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019sPnFS8fHmLPS4n8ouDHba","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211953__xee4d12/work/_research/engine/src/starter3d/40-horror.js","allow_large":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3018,"cache_read_input_tokens":83833,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3018},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23de6e6b-3ae6-4bf5-9764-44b18bb5857c","uuid":"1aa0ef43-6464-4169-8e86-f6afcff09ac3","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:24:09.905Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj9LEiUWpYt3bmAgbz4s","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019sPnFS8fHmLPS4n8ouDHba":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211953__xee4d12/work/_research/engine/src/starter3d/40-horror.js","allow_large":true}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019sPnFS8fHmLPS4n8ouDHba","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/* =====================================================================================\n2\t * SLICE 4  HORROR  (Resident Evil, Alone in the Dark, Silent Hill). @modules rpg\n3\t * A mansion's east and west wings by flashlight, each room under its own fixed camera (a cut as you walk on, the stick\n4\t * keeping its way across it). Hold K (or a right click) to aim the pistol: it locks on the nearest thing in front, up and\n5\t * down aim high and low (a dog is low), left and right pick another; J fires, or slashes with the knife (Q swaps).\n6\t * J alone checks what is in front: doors (the door opens between rooms), things to take, the item box, the typewriter\n7\t * (a save, in the 2D engine's slots). Shift runs; I opens the items: herbs heal, green and green or green and red mix.\n8\t * Zombies shamble and grab (tap J to shake free), dogs run and leap; two keys and a crank open the way to what waits\n9\t * in the gallery. Few bullets: walk round what you can. Settings, Tank controls: up walks the way you face, left and\n10\t * right turn you. THE 3D: camera zones (world.camera.zones: fixed, one that turns after you, one on a rail), lock-on\n11\t * (camera.lock, cycle), tank steering (camera.steer), the door between rooms (world.through), a flashlight with a\n12\t * failing bulb (world.flashlight), fog. HORROR.run(n): a scripted walk's hash (the proof); HORROR.bot(): to the boss\n13\t * ===================================================================================== */\n14\tconst HORROR = (() => {\n15\t  const T = 16, PI = Math.PI;\n16\t  /* ---- THE WING: one character per 1-metre tile. Rooms: the foyer (the start, the typewriter and the item box), the\n17\t   * west hall, the kitchen, the dining room, the east hall, the library (the crank's socket, the grille over the brass\n18\t   * key) and the gallery. Marks: @ the start, z zombies, d D dogs, G what waits, g r herbs, a A bullets, i the iron key,\n19\t   * q the brass key, c the crank, X the typewriter, Y the item box, O the crank's socket ---- */\n20\t  const LEVEL = {\n21\t    rows: [\n22\t      '####################..########################',\n23\t      '#.i.........#.................#..........#...#',\n24\t      '#.........g.#.t.............t.#..........#.q.#',\n25\t      '#..z........#.................#.KKK..KKK.#...#',\n26\t      '#...h.h.h...#........G........#..........##..#',\n27\t      '#...T.T.T...#...PP.......PP...#.....a........#',\n28\t      '#...j.j.j...#...PP.......PP...#.........O...t#',\n29\t      '#...........#.................#.KKK..KKK.....#',\n30\t      '#.t......z..#.................#..............#',\n31\t      '#..........a#.................#..z.........r.#',\n32\t      '#####..######.................#..............#',\n33\t      '#,SS,,,,SS,,#.................######..########',\n34\t      '#,,,,,,,,,k,#.................#####....#######',\n35\t      '#,,D,,c,,,,,########..#############....#######',\n36\t      '#,,,,,,,,,,,#,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,#####...a#######',\n37\t      '#B,,,,,,,,B,#,t,,,,,,,,,,,,,t,#####....#######',\n38\t      '#,A,,,,,,,,,#,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,#####..z.#######',\n39\t      '#####..######,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,#####....#######',\n40\t      '####....#####,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,#####....#######',\n41\t      '####..g.#####,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,#####....#######',\n42\t      '####....#####,,,b,,,,,,,,,b,,,#####....#######',\n43\t      '####........#,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,#.......t#######',\n44\t      '####..z......,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,......d..#######',\n45\t      '####.........,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,.g.......#######',\n46\t      '####........#,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,#........#######',\n47\t      '#############,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,################',\n48\t      '#############,,,X,,,,@,,,,Y,,,################',\n49\t      '#############,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,################',\n50\t      '#############,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,################',\n51\t      '##############################################'],\n52\t    ground: 'planks', colors: { base: '#4e3324', dark: '#3e281c', line: '#22140e' }, side: 'block', color: '#4a4248',\n53\t    legend: (() => {\n54\t      const tiles = { ground: 'tiles', colors: { a: '#6e665e', b: '#2e2a28', size: 8 } }, on = (sp, o) => Object.assign({}, sp, o);\n55\t      return { ',': tiles, P: { pillar: 56 }, t: { torch: true }, T: { shape: 'table' }, h: { shape: 'chair', facing: PI / 2 }, j: { shape: 'chair', facing: -PI / 2 },\n56\t        S: on(tiles, { shape: 'shelf', facing: PI / 2 }), B: on(tiles, { shape: 'barrel' }), k: on(tiles, { shape: 'stool' }), K: { shape: 'bookcase', facing: PI / 2 }, b: on(tiles, { shape: 'bench' }),\n57\t        '@': on(tiles, { mark: 'start' }), X: on(tiles, { mark: 'typewriter' }), Y: on(tiles, { mark: 'trunk' }), D: on(tiles, { mark: 'dog' }), c: on(tiles, { mark: 'crank' }), A: on(tiles, { mark: 'ammo' }),\n58\t        z: { mark: 'zombie' }, d: { mark: 'dog' }, G: { mark: 'boss' }, g: { mark: 'herbG' }, r: { mark: 'herbR' }, a: { mark: 'ammo' }, i: { mark: 'ironkey' }, q: { mark: 'brasskey' }, O: { mark: 'socket' } };\n59\t    })()\n60\t  };\n61\t  // the rooms (boxes in units, to the middle of their walls) and the camera of each part of them: a fixed one (at, look),\n62\t  // one that turns after you (follow), one that slides along a rail level with you (rail)\n63\t  const R = (x0, y0, x1, y1) => [x0 * T, y0 * T, x1 * T, y1 * T];\n64\t  const ROOMS = { foyer: R(12.5, 13.5, 30.5, 29.5), west: R(3.5, 17.5, 12.5, 25.5), kitchen: R(0, 10.5, 12.5, 17.5), dining: R(0, 0, 12.5, 10.5), east: R(30, 11.5, 39.5, 25.5), library: R(30.5, 0, 46, 11.5), gallery: R(12.5, 0, 30.5, 13.5) };\n65\t  const ZONES = [\n66\t    { room: 'foyer', box: R(12.5, 24, 30.5, 29.5), at: [468, 458, 64], look: [324, 352, 0], fov: 52 },\n67\t    { room: 'foyer', box: R(12.5, 13.5, 30.5, 24), at: [216, 228, 62], look: [380, 364, 0], fov: 52 },\n68\t    { room: 'west', box: R(3.5, 21, 12.5, 25.5), rail: [[196, 342, 52], [74, 342, 52]], fov: 56 },\n69\t    { room: 'west', box: R(3.5, 17.5, 8.5, 21), at: [122, 396, 50], look: [96, 292, 0], fov: 56 },\n70\t    { room: 'kitchen', box: R(0, 10.5, 12.5, 17.5), at: [184, 268, 58], look: [70, 196, 0], fov: 56 },\n71\t    { room: 'dining', box: R(0, 0, 12.5, 10.5), at: [184, 22, 62], follow: true, fov: 56 },\n72\t    { room: 'east', box: R(30, 20.5, 35, 25.5), at: [490, 396, 50], look: [604, 360, 0], fov: 56 },\n73\t    { room: 'east', box: R(35, 11.5, 39.5, 25.5), at: [592, 398, 58], follow: true, fov: 52 },\n74\t    { room: 'library', box: R(30.5, 0, 37.5, 11.5), at: [504, 170, 62], look: [584, 52, 0], fov: 56 },\n75\t    { room: 'library', box: R(37.5, 0, 46, 11.5), at: [716, 172, 62], look: [646, 60, 0], fov: 56 },\n76\t    { room: 'gallery', box: R(12.5, 0, 30.5, 13.5), rail: [[226, 206, 104], [446, 206, 104]], height: 26, fov: 58 }\n77\t  ];\n78\t  const roomAt = (x, y) => { for (const k in ROOMS) { const b = ROOMS[k]; if (x >= b[0] && x <= b[2] && y >= b[1] && y <= b[3]) return k; } return null; };\n79\t  // the doors (2 tiles wide in their gaps: yaw 0 spans x, PI / 2 spans y); the grille over the brass key rises\n80\t  const DOORS = [\n81\t    { id: 'west', x: 200, y: 368, yaw: PI / 2 }, { id: 'kitchen', x: 96, y: 280 }, { id: 'dining', x: 96, y: 168 },\n82\t    { id: 'east', x: 488, y: 368, yaw: PI / 2, locked: 'ironkey' }, { id: 'library', x: 592, y: 184 },\n83\t    { id: 'gallery', x: 336, y: 216, locked: 'brasskey' }, { id: 'exit', x: 336, y: 8, locked: 'sealed' }];\n84\t\n85\t  /* ---- ITEMS: the rpg module's items and a Resident Evil inventory of six slots; the item box holds the rest ---- */\n86\t  const rpg = new E.RPG({ items: {\n87\t    herbG: { name: 'Green herb', kind: 'use', heal: 30, info: 'A medicinal plant. Mix it to make it stronger.' },\n88\t    herbR: { name: 'Red herb', kind: 'use', info: 'Useless alone. Mixed with a green herb, it heals completely.' },\n89\t    herbGG: { name: 'Mixed herbs (G+G)', kind: 'use', heal: 60, info: 'Two green herbs, ground together.' },\n90\t    herbGR: { name: 'Mixed herbs (G+R)', kind: 'use', heal: 100, info: 'Green and red: it heals every wound.' },\n91\t    ammo: { name: 'Handgun bullets', kind: 'use', stack: 60, info: 'Bullets for the handgun.' },\n92\t    ironkey: { name: 'Iron key', kind: 'key', info: 'A heavy key. An iron lock is cast on its bow.' },\n93\t    brasskey: { name: 'Brass key', kind: 'key', info: 'A polished key with a brass lock engraved on it.' },\n94\t    crank: { name: 'Crank', kind: 'key', info: 'A square-ended crank handle. It fits some mechanism.' } } });\n95\t  const MIX = { 'herbG+herbG': 'herbGG', 'herbG+herbR': 'herbGR', 'herbR+herbG': 'herbGR' };\n96\t  const KEY_LOOK = { ironkey: '#8a8c98', brasskey: '#e0b048' };\n97\t  // the items' icons on the items screen (pixel sprites, drawn at twice their size)\n98\t  const leaf = c => E.sprite(['...gg....', '..gGg..g.', '.gGgg.gG.', '.gg.ggGg.', '..g.gGg..', '...ggg...', '..bbbbb..', '..bBBBb..', '...bbb...'], { g: c, G: E.shade(c, .3), b: '#7a5a40', B: '#9a7a5a' });\n99\t  const ICONS = { herbG: leaf('#4aa04a'), herbR: leaf('#c04040'), herbGG: leaf('#6ac05a'), herbGR: leaf('#c0a040'),\n100\t    ammo: E.sprite(['.y.y.y...', '.Y.Y.Y...', '.c.c.c...', '.c.c.c...', 'ooooooo..', 'oOOOOOo..', 'oOOOOOo..', 'ooooooo..'], { y: '#ffe090', Y: '#d8b048', c: '#b88a30', o: '#3a4628', O: '#5a6a3a' }),\n101\t    ironkey: E.sprite(['.kkk.....', 'k...k....', 'k...k....', '.kkkkkkkk', '.....k.k.', '.....k...'], { k: KEY_LOOK.ironkey }), brasskey: E.sprite(['.kkk.....', 'k...k....', 'k...k....', '.kkkkkkkk', '.....k.k.', '.....k...'], { k: KEY_LOOK.brasskey }),\n102\t    crank: E.sprite(['mm.......', 'mm.......', '.m.......', '.mmmmmm..', '......m..', '......mww', '.......ww'], { m: '#8a8a94', w: '#6a4a30' }) };\n103\t  // things drawn by code for this slice (the engine's kinds are in its manual): a potted herb, a box of bullets, the\n104\t  // crank, its socket in the library\n105\t  W3.THINGS.herb = (p, t) => { const c = t.color || '#4aa04a'; p.box(0, 0, 2.2, 6, 6, 4.4, '#7a5a40').box(0, 0, 4.6, 6.4, 6.4, .8, '#5a3e2a'); for (let k = 0; k < 6; k++) { const a = k * TAU / 6; p.cone(Math.cos(a) * .6, Math.sin(a) * .6, 4.6, Math.cos(a) * 3.4, Math.sin(a) * 3.4, 10 + (k & 1) * 2, 1.6, E.shade(c, (k & 1) * .15)); } };\n106\t  W3.THINGS.ammo = (p) => { p.box(0, 0, 1.8, 7, 5, 3.6, '#5a6a3a').box(0, 0, 3.7, 7.2, 5.2, .4, '#3a4628').box(-1, -2.6, 2, 3, .3, 1.4, '#e8d890'); for (let k = 0; k < 3; k++) p.tube(-2 + k * 2, 3, 3.6, -2 + k * 2, 3, 5.4, .55, '#d8b048'); };\n107\t  W3.THINGS.crank = (p) => { p.tube(-4, 0, 1, 3, 0, 1, .7, '#6a6a74').tube(3, 0, 1, 3, 0, 5, .7, '#6a6a74').tube(3, 0, 5, 6, 0, 5, .9, '#4a3020').box(-4.4, 0, 1, 1.4, 1.4, 1.4, '#3a3a42'); };\n108\t  W3.THINGS.socket = (p, t) => {   // a cast plate on a post, a square hole; with the crank in it, the handle turns\n109\t    p.box(0, 0, 6, 3, 3, 12, '#3a3640').box(0, 0, 13, 9, 3, 9, '#5a5664').ball(0, -1.6, 13, 1.8, .6, 1.8, '#18161c');\n110\t    if (t.on) { const a = t.turn || 0; p.tube(0, -1.8, 13, 0, -5, 13, .6, '#6a6a74').tube(0, -5, 13, Math.cos(a) * 4, -5, 13 + Math.sin(a) * 4, .6, '#6a6a74').ball(Math.cos(a) * 4, -6, 13 + Math.sin(a) * 4, 1, 1, 1, '#4a3020'); }\n111\t  };\n112\t\n113\t  /* ---- THE CAST: the hero, the dead of the house, its dogs, and what waits in the gallery ---- */\n114\t  const HERO_COLORS = { cloth: '#3a4e6a', pants: '#2a2c36', boot: '#1e1c22', belt: '#4a3a2a', hair: '#3a2418', skin: '#e0b090', glove: '#2a2a30', metal: '#4a4c56', metalDk: '#2a2a30', hilt: '#3a3a40' };\n115\t  const ZOMBIE_COLORS = [\n116\t    { skin: '#8a9a7e', hair: '#2e2a26', cloth: '#5a4a52', pants: '#33302e', boot: '#262220', belt: '#4a3a2a' },\n117\t    { skin: '#9a9488', hair: '#4a3e30', cloth: '#6a5a44', pants: '#2e2e34', boot: '#24221e', belt: '#3a3026' },\n118\t    { skin: '#7e8a7a', hair: '#1e1c1a', cloth: '#3e4a5a', pants: '#2a2826', boot: '#201e1c', belt: '#3a3026' }];\n119\t  const BOSS_COLORS = { skin: '#b8a090', hair: '#2a2024', cloth: '#5a1e22', pants: '#2a2228', boot: '#1e1a1c', belt: '#3a2a22', eye: '#ff3a2a' };\n120\t  const WALK = 26, RUN = 58, HP = 100, CLIP = 12, GUN_DMG = 10, HEAD_DMG = 26, KNIFE_DMG = 7, AIM_A = [-.42, 0, .42];\n121\t  const KIND = {\n122\t    zombie: { hp: 46, speed: [12, 17], r: 5, half: 8, head: 27 },\n123\t    dog: { hp: 24, speed: [84, 92], r: 4.5, half: 0, head: 11 },\n124\t    boss: { hp: 260, speed: [22, 22], r: 9, half: 15, head: 48 }\n125\t  };\n126\t\n127\t  /* ---- SOUNDS AND MUSIC (the step sequencer's format: original songs) ---- */\n128\t  const SOUNDS = {\n129\t    gun: [{ wave: 'noise', freq: 2400, to: 300, dur: .16, vol: .5 }, { wave: 'square', freq: 220, to: 70, dur: .1, vol: .3 }],\n130\t    dry: { wave: 'square', freq: 1800, dur: .02, vol: .12 }, reload: [{ wave: 'square', freq: 900, dur: .03, vol: .14 }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 3000, dur: .05, vol: .12, delay: .12 }],\n131\t    moan: { wave: 'saw', freq: 92, to: 70, dur: .9, vol: .1, vib: [5, .08], filter: 'lowpass' }, bark: [{ wave: 'saw', freq: 420, to: 240, dur: .09, vol: .18 }, { wave: 'saw', freq: 400, to: 200, dur: .1, vol: .16, delay: .14 }],\n132\t    bite: [{ wave: 'noise', freq: 1200, to: 300, dur: .14, vol: .4 }, { wave: 'square', freq: 160, to: 60, dur: .12, vol: .25 }],\n133\t    crank: { wave: 'square', freq: 300, arp: [0, 0, 0, 0], step: .09, dur: .36, vol: .12, filter: 'lowpass' }, stab: { wave: 'noise', freq: 3200, to: 900, dur: .09, vol: .22 },\n134\t    roar: [{ wave: 'saw', freq: 120, to: 50, dur: 1.2, vol: .22, vib: [8, .15] }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 400, to: 100, dur: 1, vol: .2, filter: 'lowpass' }]\n135\t  };\n136\t  const HALL = { bpm: 56, steps: 4, tracks: [   // the halls: a low drone, a slow minor figure, a heartbeat\n137\t    { wave: 'triangle', vol: .3, notes: 'D2 - - - - - - - | D2 - - - - - - - | Bb1 - - - - - - - | A1 - - - - - - -' },\n138\t    { wave: 'pulse25', vol: .05, notes: '. . D4 . . F4 . . | E4 . . . . . . . | . . D4 . . Bb3 . . | A3 . . . C#4 . . .' },\n139\t    { wave: 'sine', vol: .06, notes: '. . . . . . A4 . | . . . . . . . . | . . . . . . G4 . | . . . . F4 . E4 .' },\n140\t    { wave: 'drums', vol: .05, notes: 'k k . . . . . . | k k . . . . . .' }] };\n141\t  const SAFE = { bpm: 64, steps: 3, tracks: [   // the foyer: the typewriter's quiet, a waltz in the dark\n142\t    { wave: 'triangle', vol: .24, notes: 'F2 C3 A3 | F2 C3 A3 | D2 A2 F3 | D2 A2 F3 | Bb1 F2 D3 | Bb1 F2 D3 | C2 G2 E3 | C2 G2 E3' },\n143\t    { wave: 'sine', vol: .1, notes: 'A4 - C5 | F5 - E5 | D5 - - | A4 - - | Bb4 - D5 | F5 - G5 | E5 - - | - - -' }] };\n144\t  const DREAD = { bpm: 118, steps: 4, tracks: [   // the gallery's fight\n145\t    { wave: 'saw', vol: .06, notes: 'D3 D3 . D3 Eb3 . D3 . | D3 D3 . D3 C3 . Bb2 . | D3 D3 . D3 Eb3 . F3 . | Eb3 . D3 . C#3 . . .' },\n146\t    { wave: 'triangle', vol: .3, notes: 'D2 . D2 . D2 . D2 . | Bb1 . Bb1 . Bb1 . Bb1 . | G1 . G1 . G1 . G1 . | A1 . A1 . A1 . A1 .' },\n147\t    { wave: 'drums', vol: .1, notes: 'k . . k s . . . | k . k . s . . h' }] };\n148\t\n149\t  /* ---- THE STATE ---- */\n150\t  let world = null, flow = null, hero = null, H = null, lamp = null, muzzle = null, rnd = Math.random;\n151\t  let enemies = [], items = [], doors = {}, gate = null, socket = null, inv = null, box = null, flags = null, mode = 'play', menu = null, msg = null, song = null, ended = 0, scripted = false;\n152\t  const shots = [];\n153\t  BOOT.push(['The mansion', () => {\n154\t    for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(SOUNDS)) A.define(k, v);\n155\t    world = new W3(game, { level: LEVEL, torchLights: 4, torchShadows: 0, torchPower: 22, torchReach: 140, torchColor: '#ffb070', lights: 1, spots: 1,\n156\t      ambient: ['#3a3e56', '#141018', 1.6], fog: { color: '#040406', near: 40, far: 250 }, sky: '#020203', camera: { mode: 'zones', zones: ZONES, reticle: '#ff5a3a', lockRange: 170 },\n157\t      onDraw: () => { for (const e of enemies) if (e.type === 'dog') drawDog(e); for (const s of shots) world.pen.bar(s.x, s.y, s.z, s.x1, s.y1, s.z1, .5, .5, '#ffe8a8'); } });   // (the dogs and the shots' streaks, whichever scene draws the world)\n158\t    flow = world.flow();\n159\t  }]);\n160\t\n161\t  /** a fresh game, or the one a save holds (s: its data): the wing as it stood, the hero where it saved */\n162\t  function reset(seed = 1, s = null) {\n163\t    world.reset(); rnd = E.rng(seed); flow = world.flow();\n164\t    flags = s ? JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(s.flags)) : { taken: [], dead: [], open: [], crank: false, boss: false };\n165\t    const st = world.marks.start[0], at = s ? s.at : [st.x, st.y, -PI / 2];\n166\t    hero = world.hero({ x: at[0], y: at[1], r: 4.5, rig: new E.Humanoid({ weapon: s && !s.gun ? 'sword' : 'gun', bladeLen: 5, hair: 'long', colors: HERO_COLORS, speedRef: 60 }) }); hero.facing = at[2];\n167\t    H = { hp: s ? s.hp : HP, clip: s ? s.clip : CLIP, gun: s ? s.gun : true, aim: false, aimLv: 0, cool: 0, fireT: 0, reloadT: 0, hurtT: 0, grabbed: null, grabT: 0, shake: 0, stun: 0, crankT: 0, dead: false, deadT: 0, inv: 0, knife: null, room: roomAt(at[0], at[1]) || 'foyer', shots: 0 };\n168\t    inv = rpg.inventory({ slots: 6 }); box = rpg.inventory({ slots: 40 });\n169\t    for (const [id, n] of (s ? s.inv : [['ammo', 18], ['herbG', 1]])) inv.add(id, n);\n170\t    for (const [id, n] of (s ? s.box : [])) box.add(id, n);\n171\t    if (!lamp) { lamp = world.flashlight(hero, { power: 46, reach: 300, angle: .46, flicker: .35 }); muzzle = world.light({ color: '#ffd090', reach: 160, power: 0 }); }\n172\t    lamp.actor = hero; lamp.on = true;\n173\t    // the doors, the grille, the socket, the save room's things, what is left to take, and who is still about\n174\t    doors = {}; for (const d of DOORS) doors[d.id] = world.thing('door', d.x, d.y, 0, { yaw: d.yaw || 0, w: 30, h: 40, swing: true, color: '#4a2c1c', frame: '#3a3036', locked: flags.open.includes(d.id) ? null : d.locked || null, solid: true, data: { id: d.id } });\n175\t    if (flags.boss) doors.exit.locked = null;\n176\t    gate = world.thing('door', 44 * T, 4.5 * T, 0, { w: 30, h: 36, color: '#3a3a44', frame: '#3a3036', solid: !flags.crank, open: flags.crank ? 1 : 0, data: { id: 'gate' } });\n177\t    const sk = world.marks.socket[0]; socket = world.thing('socket', sk.x, sk.y, 0, { yaw: PI / 2, on: flags.crank, turn: 0, solid: [8, 6, 16] });\n178\t    world.thing('typewriter', world.marks.typewriter[0].x, world.marks.typewriter[0].y, 0, { yaw: PI / 2, solid: [22, 13, 16] });\n179\t    world.thing('trunk', world.marks.trunk[0].x, world.marks.trunk[0].y, 0, { yaw: -PI / 2, solid: [24, 12, 12] });\n180\t    items = [];\n181\t    const item = (mark, id, n, kind, o = {}) => (world.marks[mark] || []).forEach((m, i) => {\n182\t      const key = mark + i; if (flags.taken.includes(key)) return;\n183\t      items.push(world.thing(kind, m.x, m.y, m.z, Object.assign({ data: { key, item: id, n } }, o)));\n184\t    });\n185\t    item('herbG', 'herbG', 1, 'herb'); item('herbR', 'herbR', 1, 'herb', { color: '#c04040' }); item('ammo', 'ammo', 10, 'ammo'); item('crank', 'crank', 1, 'crank', { yaw: .6 });\n186\t    item('ironkey', 'ironkey', 1, 'key', { color: KEY_LOOK.ironkey, spin: .3, bob: 1, z: 3 }); item('brasskey', 'brasskey', 1, 'key', { color: KEY_LOOK.brasskey, spin: .3, bob: 1, z: 3 });\n187\t    enemies = [];\n188\t    const spawn = (type, m, i) => {\n189\t      const id = type + i; if (flags.dead.includes(id)) return; const k = KIND[type];\n190\t      const e = type === 'dog' ? world.mob({ x: m.x, y: m.y, r: k.r, half: 0, mass: 1.2, visible: false, pose: false })\n191\t        : world.mob({ x: m.x, y: m.y, r: k.r, half: k.half, mass: type === 'boss' ? 8 : 1.4, rig: type === 'boss' ? new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.8, build: 'bulky', weapon: null, hunch: .35, lean: .15, hair: 'long', sleeves: 'long', colors: BOSS_COLORS, eyeGlow: '#ff3a2a', speedRef: 40 })\n192\t          : new E.Humanoid({ weapon: null, hunch: .3 + rnd() * .2, lean: .12, stride: 5, speedRef: 30, colors: ZOMBIE_COLORS[(rnd() * ZOMBIE_COLORS.length) | 0], eyeGlow: '#d8e0a0' }) });\n193\t      Object.assign(e, { id, type, k, hp: k.hp, max: k.hp, room: roomAt(m.x, m.y), state: 'idle', t: rnd() * 2, stun: 0, speed: k.speed[0] + rnd() * (k.speed[1] - k.speed[0]), facing: rnd() * TAU, head: k.head, phase: rnd() * TAU, px: m.x, py: m.y, moan: 2 + rnd() * 6, atk: null });\n194\t      enemies.push(e);\n195\t    };\n196\t    for (const t of ['zombie', 'dog', 'boss']) (world.marks[t] || []).forEach((m, i) => spawn(t, m, i));\n197\t    shots.length = 0; mode = 'play'; menu = null; msg = null; ended = 0; song = null;\n198\t    world.camera.set('view'); world.camera.set('zones'); world.camera.follow(hero);\n199\t  }\n200\t  const say = (text, t = 2.6) => { msg = { text, t }; };\n201\t  const alive = () => enemies.filter(e => e.alive && e.hp > 0);\n202\t  const awake = () => alive().filter(e => e.room === H.room);\n203\t\n204\t  /* ---- THE HERO: the controls (ctl: move, the buttons this step), then what it does ---- */\n205\t  function heroStep(dt, ctl) {\n206\t    const h = hero, S = H;\n207\t    S.cool -= dt; S.fireT -= dt; S.hurtT -= dt; S.inv -= dt; h.flash -= dt;\n208\t    S.room = roomAt(h.x, h.y) || S.room;\n209\t    if (S.dead) { S.deadT += dt; h.vx = h.vy = 0; h.anim = { pose: 'die' }; return; }\n210\t    if (S.grabbed) {   // held by the dead: tap the button to shake free; a bite halfway\n211\t      const z = S.grabbed; S.grabT -= dt * (ctl.pressed('act') ? 6 : 1); h.vx = h.vy = 0; h.facing = Math.atan2(z.y - h.y, z.x - h.x);\n212\t      if (!z.bit && S.grabT < .55) { z.bit = true; hurtHero(z.type === 'boss' ? 30 : 16, h.facing + PI, true); A.sfx('bite'); }\n213\t      if (S.grabT <= 0 || !z.alive) { S.grabbed = null; const a = Math.atan2(h.y - z.y, h.x - z.x); h.push(Math.cos(a) * 140, Math.sin(a) * 140); z.push(-Math.cos(a) * 90, -Math.sin(a) * 90); z.state = 'recoil'; z.t = 1; }\n214\t      h.anim = { hurt: true, expr: 'wince', point: false };\n215\t      return;\n216\t    }\n217\t    if (S.crankT > 0) {   // turning the crank: the grille rises\n218\t      S.crankT -= dt; socket.turn = (socket.turn || 0) + dt * 6; gate.open = clamp(1 - S.crankT / 2.2, 0, 1); h.vx = h.vy = 0; h.anim = { pose: 'cast' };\n219\t      if (S.crankT <= 0) { world.setSolid(gate, false); flags.crank = true; say('The grille rose. Something gleams behind it.'); A.sfx('secret'); }\n220\t      return;\n221\t    }\n222\t    if (S.hurtT > 0) { h.vx = approach(h.vx, 0, 400 * dt); h.vy = approach(h.vy, 0, 400 * dt); h.anim = { hurt: true, expr: 'wince' }; return; }\n223\t    // aim: held, it stands still and locks on what is in front; up and down aim high and low, left and right pick another\n224\t    const wasAim = S.aim; S.aim = ctl.down('aim') && S.reloadT <= 0;\n225\t    const cam = world.camera, targets = awake();\n226\t    if (S.aim && !wasAim) { S.aimLv = 0; const t = cam.lock(h, targets); if (t && t.type === 'dog') S.aimLv = -1; }\n227\t    if (!S.aim && wasAim) cam.unlock();\n228\t    if (S.reloadT > 0) { S.reloadT -= dt; if (S.reloadT <= 0) { const n = Math.min(CLIP - S.clip, inv.count('ammo')); inv.remove('ammo', n); S.clip += n; } }\n229\t    if (S.aim) {\n230\t      h.vx = approach(h.vx, 0, 600 * dt); h.vy = approach(h.vy, 0, 600 * dt);\n231\t      if (ctl.pressed('up')) S.aimLv = Math.min(1, S.aimLv + 1); if (ctl.pressed('down')) S.aimLv = Math.max(-1, S.aimLv - 1);\n232\t      const L = cam.lockOn;\n233\t      if (L) { if (ctl.pressed('left')) cam.cycle(targets, -1); if (ctl.pressed('right')) cam.cycle(targets, 1); const T2 = cam.lockOn; h.facing = E.approachAng(h.facing, Math.atan2(T2.y - h.y, T2.x - h.x), dt * 9); }\n234\t      else { if (!cam.lock(h, targets)) h.facing += (ctl.move[0] ? Math.sign(ctl.move[0]) : 0) * 2.6 * dt; }\n235\t      if (ctl.pressed('act') && S.fireT <= 0) { ctl.use('act'); S.gun ? fire() : slash(); }\n236\t    } else {\n237\t      // walk or run: the camera's way, or tank controls (Settings)\n238\t      const mv = ctl.move, ml = Math.hypot(mv[0], mv[1]), sp = (ctl.down('run') ? RUN : WALK) * (S.hp <= 33 ? .7 : 1), acc = 500 * dt;\n239\t      h.vx = approach(h.vx, mv[0] * sp, acc); h.vy = approach(h.vy, mv[1] * sp, acc);\n240\t      if (ml > .1 && !ctl.tank) h.facing = E.approachAng(h.facing, Math.atan2(mv[1], mv[0]), dt * 9);\n241\t      if (ctl.pressed('swap')) { ctl.use('swap'); S.gun = !S.gun; h.rig.o.weapon = S.gun ? 'gun' : 'sword'; h.rig.o.bladeLen = 5; A.sfx('select'); say(S.gun ? 'Handgun.' : 'Knife.', 1); }\n242\t      if (ctl.pressed('act')) { ctl.use('act'); check(); }\n243\t    }\n244\t    if (S.knife) { S.knife.update(dt); if (S.knife.state && S.knife.phase === 'active') S.knife.hits(targets, e => Math.abs(e.z - h.z) < 24 && E.inArc(h, h.facing, e, 22 + e.k.r, .9), e => hurt(e, KNIFE_DMG, h.facing, 50)); if (!S.knife.busy) S.knife = null; }\n245\t    h.anim = { point: S.aim && S.gun, aim: S.aim ? AIM_A[S.aimLv + 1] : 0, attack: S.knife && S.knife.state, hurt: false, crouch: S.aim && S.aimLv < 0 && !S.gun, expr: S.hp <= 33 ? 'wince' : null };\n246\t  }\n247\t  /** the handgun: a shot along the aim (world.ray), the first body it meets hurt; a high shot at a head hurts more */\n248\t  function fire() {\n249\t    const h = hero, S = H;\n250\t    if (S.clip <= 0) { if (inv.count('ammo') > 0) { S.reloadT = 1.1; S.aim = false; world.camera.unlock(); A.sfx('reload'); } else { A.sfx('dry'); say('Out of bullets.', 1.2); } S.fireT = .4; return; }\n251\t    S.clip--; S.fireT = .42; S.shots++; A.sfx('gun'); game.shake(1.5);\n252\t    const a = h.facing, va = AIM_A[S.aimLv + 1], ca = Math.cos(va), x = h.x + Math.cos(a) * 7, y = h.y + Math.sin(a) * 7, z = h.z + 19;\n253\t    const hit = world.ray(x, y, z, Math.cos(a) * ca, Math.sin(a) * ca, Math.sin(va), 300, { skip: h });\n254\t    shots.push({ x, y, z, x1: hit ? hit.x : x + Math.cos(a) * ca * 300, y1: hit ? hit.y : y + Math.sin(a) * ca * 300, z1: hit ? hit.z : z + Math.sin(va) * 300, t: .06 });\n255\t    muzzle.x = x; muzzle.y = y; muzzle.z = z; muzzle.power = 26; muzzle.on = true; P.sparks(x, y, z, 3, a, { color: '#ffe0a0' });\n256\t    if (!hit) return;\n257\t    const e = hit.actor && enemies.includes(hit.actor) ? hit.actor : null;\n258\t    if (e && e.alive) { const head = e.type !== 'dog' && hit.z > e.z + e.head * .8; hurt(e, head ? HEAD_DMG : GUN_DMG, a, e.type === 'boss' ? 20 : 70); if (head) P.bits(hit.x, hit.y, hit.z, 6, ['#6a1a1a', '#9a2a2a', '#c8b0a0']); }\n259\t    else { P.sparks(hit.x, hit.y, hit.z, 5, Math.atan2(hit.ny, hit.nx)); P.dust(hit.x, hit.y, hit.z, 2); }\n260\t  }\n261\t  function slash() { H.knife = new E.Attack('slash', { reach: 5 }); H.knife.start(); H.fireT = .45; A.sfx('stab'); }\n262\t  function hurtHero(dmg, ang, held = false) {\n263\t    const h = hero, S = H; if (S.dead || (S.inv > 0 && !held)) return false;\n264\t    S.hp -= dmg; S.inv = .6; h.flash = .08; if (!held) { S.hurtT = .35; h.push(Math.cos(ang) * 110, Math.sin(ang) * 110); }\n265\t    game.shake(3); game.flash('#7a0000', .12, .35); A.sfx('hurt'); P.bits(h.x, h.y, h.z + 16, 6, ['#7a1010', '#a02020']);\n266\t    world.camera.unlock(); S.aim = false;\n267\t    if (S.hp <= 0) { S.hp = 0; S.dead = true; S.deadT = 0; S.grabbed = null; A.music(null); A.sfx('die'); }\n268\t    return true;\n269\t  }\n270\t  function hurt(e, dmg, ang, kb) {\n271\t    e.hp -= dmg; e.flash = .06; e.stun = e.type === 'boss' ? (e.hp % 60 < dmg ? .7 : 0) : .35; e.push(Math.cos(ang) * kb, Math.sin(ang) * kb);\n272\t    if (e.state === 'lunge' || e.state === 'pounce') e.state = 'chase';\n273\t    P.bits(e.x, e.y, e.z + e.head * .6, 4, ['#5a1414', '#8a2020']); A.sfx('hit');\n274\t    if (e.hp > 0) return;\n275\t    e.alive = false; flags.dead.push(e.id); e.setSolid(false); e.deadT = 0; A.sfx(e.type === 'dog' ? 'bark' : 'moan');\n276\t    if (world.camera.lockOn === e) world.camera.unlock();\n277\t    if (e.type === 'boss') { flags.boss = true; doors.exit.locked = null; game.flash('#ffffff', .3, .5); A.sfx('roar'); say('It is over. The way out is open.', 4); }\n278\t  }\n279\t  /** J in front of something: a door, a thing to take, the item box, the typewriter, the socket */\n280\t  function check() {\n281\t    const t = world.reach(hero, 16); if (!t) return;\n282\t    const d = t.data || {};\n283\t    if (t.kind === 'door' && d.id === 'gate') { say(flags.crank ? 'The grille is up.' : 'An iron grille. A key gleams behind it, out of reach.'); return; }\n284\t    if (t.kind === 'door') {\n285\t      if (d.id === 'exit') { if (t.locked) { say('Sealed with heavy chains. Something holds them from the far side.'); return; } win(); return; }\n286\t      if (t.locked) {\n287\t        const was = t.locked, r = world.unlock(t, inv);\n288\t        if (r === 'locked') { say('It is locked. ' + (was === 'ironkey' ? 'An iron lock.' : 'A brass lock.')); A.sfx('bump'); return; }\n289\t        flags.open.push(d.id); say('You used the ' + rpg.items[was].name.toUpperCase() + '.'); A.sfx('key'); return;\n290\t      }\n291\t      if (world.through(t, hero, { then: () => { autosave(); } })) A.sfx('door');\n292\t      return;\n293\t    }\n294\t    if (d.item) {\n295\t      if (!inv.add(d.item, d.n)) { say('No room. Leave something in the item box.'); A.sfx('bump'); return; }\n296\t      flags.taken.push(d.key); world.remove(t); items.splice(items.indexOf(t), 1); A.sfx(d.item.endsWith('key') ? 'key' : 'pickup');\n297\t      say('Took the ' + rpg.items[d.item].name.toUpperCase() + (d.n > 1 ? ' x' + d.n : '') + '.'); return;\n298\t    }\n299\t    if (t.kind === 'trunk') { openBox(); return; }\n300\t    if (t.kind === 'typewriter') { saveGame(); return; }\n301\t    if (t === socket) {\n302\t      if (flags.crank) { say('The crank is fixed in place.'); return; }\n303\t      if (!inv.has('crank')) { say('A mechanism with a square socket. A crank would fit it.'); return; }\n304\t      inv.remove('crank'); socket.on = true; H.crankT = 2.2; A.sfx('crank'); return;\n305\t    }\n306\t  }\n307\t\n308\t  /* ---- THE DEAD, THE DOGS, WHAT WAITS: each wakes when you are in its room ---- */\n309\t  const _d = [0, 0];\n310\t  function towards(e, out) {   // straight at the hero when it sees it, else down the flow field (round the furniture)\n311\t    const dx = hero.x - e.x, dy = hero.y - e.y, d = Math.hypot(dx, dy) || 1;\n312\t    if (d < 60 || world.clear(e.x, e.y, e.z + 10, hero.x, hero.y, hero.z + 10)) { out[0] = dx / d; out[1] = dy / d; return out; }\n313\t    if (flow.dir(e.x, e.y, out)) return out; out[0] = dx / d; out[1] = dy / d; return out;\n314\t  }\n315\t  function zombie(e, dt) {\n316\t    const h = hero, dx = h.x - e.x, dy = h.y - e.y, d = Math.hypot(dx, dy), toH = Math.atan2(dy, dx), boss = e.type === 'boss';\n317\t    let mx = 0, my = 0, sp = e.speed * (boss && e.hp < e.max / 2 ? 1.35 : 1);\n318\t    e.t -= dt; e.moan -= dt;\n319\t    if (e.moan < 0 && !boss) { e.moan = 5 + rnd() * 6; A.sfx('moan'); }\n320\t    if (e.stun > 0) e.state = e.state === 'grab' ? 'grab' : 'chase';\n321\t    else if (e.state === 'idle') { if (H.room === e.room && !H.dead) e.state = 'chase'; }\n322\t    else if (e.state === 'chase') {\n323\t      towards(e, _d); mx = _d[0]; my = _d[1]; e.facing = E.approachAng(e.facing, Math.atan2(my, mx), dt * (boss ? 3 : 2));\n324\t      if (H.room !== e.room) e.state = 'idle';\n325\t      else if (boss && d > 70 && d < 170 && e.t < 0 && world.clear(e.x, e.y, e.z + 20, h.x, h.y, h.z + 10)) { e.state = 'wind'; e.t = .6; A.sfx('roar'); }\n326\t      else if (d < (boss ? 30 : 14) && e.t < 0 && !H.dead && !H.grabbed) { e.state = 'lunge'; e.t = boss ? .55 : .5; if (boss) { e.atk = new E.Attack('haymaker', { reach: 9, hold: .2 }); e.atk.start(); } }\n327\t    }\n328\t    else if (e.state === 'lunge') {   // arms out, a lean, then the grab (the boss: a swing)\n329\t      e.facing = E.approachAng(e.facing, toH, dt * 3); if (!boss) { mx = Math.cos(e.facing) * .6; my = Math.sin(e.facing) * .6; }\n330\t      if (e.atk) e.atk.update(dt);\n331\t      if (e.t <= 0) {\n332\t        const reach = boss ? 34 : 12, near = d < reach + 4 && Math.abs(h.z - e.z) < 12 && Math.abs(E.angDiff(e.facing, toH)) < 1;\n333\t        if (near && !H.dead && !H.grabbed && H.crankT <= 0 && !world.passing) { if (boss) { hurtHero(26, toH); h.push(Math.cos(toH) * 120, Math.sin(toH) * 120); } else { H.grabbed = e; H.grabT = 1.25; e.bit = false; e.state = 'grab'; } }\n334\t        if (e.state === 'lunge') { e.state = 'recoil'; e.t = boss ? .8 : .9; }\n335\t      }\n336\t    }\n337\t    else if (e.state === 'grab') { e.facing = toH; if (H.grabbed !== e) { e.state = 'recoil'; e.t = 1; } }\n338\t    else if (e.state === 'wind') { e.facing = E.approachAng(e.facing, toH, dt * 4); if (e.t <= 0) { e.state = 'rush'; e.t = .7; } }\n339\t    else if (e.state === 'rush') {   // the boss's charge: straight on, a blow to whatever is in the way\n340\t      mx = Math.cos(e.facing); my = Math.sin(e.facing); sp = 150;\n341\t      if (d < 22 && !H.dead && !world.passing) { hurtHero(30, e.facing); h.push(Math.cos(e.facing) * 160, Math.sin(e.facing) * 160); e.t = 0; }\n342\t      if (e.t <= 0) { e.state = 'recoil'; e.t = 1; }\n343\t    }\n344\t    else if (e.state === 'recoil') { if (e.t <= 0) { e.state = 'chase'; e.t = boss ? 2 + rnd() * 2 : .4 + rnd() * .6; e.atk = null; } }\n345\t    if (e.atk && !e.atk.busy) e.atk = null;\n346\t    const acc = (e.stun > 0 ? 200 : 260) * dt;\n347\t    e.vx = approach(e.vx, e.stun > 0 ? 0 : mx * sp, acc); e.vy = approach(e.vy, e.stun > 0 ? 0 : my * sp, acc);\n348\t    e.stun -= dt; e.flash -= dt;\n349\t    e.anim = { pose: e.state === 'chase' || e.state === 'lunge' || e.state === 'grab' ? (boss ? null : 'cast') : null, hurt: e.stun > 0, attack: e.atk && e.atk.state, expr: 'angry', dash: e.state === 'rush' };\n350\t  }\n351\t  function dog(e, dt) {\n352\t    const h = hero, dx = h.x - e.x, dy = h.y - e.y, d = Math.hypot(dx, dy) || 1, toH = Math.atan2(dy, dx);\n353\t    e.t -= dt; e.phase += dt * Math.hypot(e.vx, e.vy) * .16; e.px = e.x; e.py = e.y;\n354\t    let mx = 0, my = 0;\n355\t    if (e.state === 'idle') { if (H.room === e.room && !H.dead) { e.state = 'run'; A.sfx('bark'); } }\n356\t    else if (e.state === 'run') {   // in, weaving\n357\t      towards(e, _d); const w = Math.sin(world.time * 3 + e.phase) * .5; mx = _d[0] - _d[1] * w; my = _d[1] + _d[0] * w; e.facing = E.approachAng(e.facing, Math.atan2(my, mx), dt * 8);\n358\t      if (H.room !== e.room) e.state = 'idle';\n359\t      else if (d < 38 && e.grounded && e.t < 0 && !world.passing) { e.state = 'pounce'; e.t = .5; e.vz = 120; e.vx = dx / d * (d + 4) / .5; e.vy = dy / d * (d + 4) / .5; e.facing = toH; A.sfx('bark'); }\n360\t    }\n361\t    else if (e.state === 'pounce') {\n362\t      if (d < e.r + 7 && Math.abs(h.z - e.z) < 18 && !H.dead) { hurtHero(10, toH); e.state = 'off'; e.t = .9; e.vx = -dx / d * 70; e.vy = -dy / d * 70; A.sfx('bite'); }\n363\t      else if (e.t < .1 && e.grounded) { e.state = 'off'; e.t = .6; }\n364\t    }\n365\t    else if (e.state === 'off') { mx = -dx / d; my = -dy / d; const s = Math.sign(Math.sin(e.phase)) || 1; mx -= my * s; my += mx * s; e.facing = E.approachAng(e.facing, Math.atan2(my, mx), dt * 6); if (e.t <= 0) { e.state = 'run'; e.t = .3 + rnd() * .5; } }\n366\t    if (e.state !== 'pounce') { const acc = (e.stun > 0 ? 300 : 700) * dt; e.vx = approach(e.vx, e.stun > 0 ? 0 : mx * e.speed, acc); e.vy = approach(e.vy, e.stun > 0 ? 0 : my * e.speed, acc); }\n367\t    e.stun -= dt; e.flash -= dt;\n368\t  }\n369\t\n370\t  /* ---- ONE STEP: the rules, then the world ---- */\n371\t  function step(dt, ctl) {\n372\t    if (msg && (msg.t -= dt) <= 0) msg = null;\n373\t    if (world.passing) { world.step(dt); return; }   // (a door between rooms: everything waits)\n374\t    flow.to(hero.x, hero.y);\n375\t    heroStep(dt, ctl);\n376\t    for (const e of enemies) {\n377\t      if (!e.alive) { e.deadT += dt; e.vx = approach(e.vx, 0, 300 * dt); e.vy = approach(e.vy, 0, 300 * dt); e.anim = { pose: 'die' }; continue; }\n378\t      if (e.type === 'dog') dog(e, dt); else zombie(e, dt);\n379\t    }\n380\t    for (let i = shots.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) if ((shots[i].t -= dt) <= 0) shots.splice(i, 1);\n381\t    if (muzzle.on && (muzzle.power -= 400 * dt) <= 0) muzzle.on = false;\n382\t    if (H.dead && H.deadT > 2.4 && !ended) { ended = 1; game.go('over', { from: 'horror', world, lines: ['YOU DIED', flags.taken.length + ' THINGS FOUND   ' + flags.dead.length + ' OF ' + enemies.length + ' PUT DOWN'] }); }\n383\t    world.step(dt);\n384\t  }\n385\t  function win() {\n386\t    if (ended) return; ended = 1; if (scripted) return; A.music('victory');\n387\t    game.after(1.2, () => game.go('over', { from: 'horror', world, won: true, title: 'ESCAPED', lines: ['THE WING IS QUIET', flags.dead.length + ' PUT DOWN   ' + H.shots + ' SHOTS FIRED'] }));\n388\t  }\n389\t  /* ---- SAVES: the typewriter writes to the 2D engine's slots (game.saves); a door passed writes the autosave ---- */\n390\t  const state = () => ({ data: { at: [hero.x, hero.y, hero.facing], hp: H.hp, clip: H.clip, gun: H.gun, inv: inv.list().map(s => [s.id, s.n]), box: box.list().map(s => [s.id, s.n]), flags }, place: (H.room || 'foyer').toUpperCase(), level: null });\n391\t  function saveGame() { game.saves.write = state; game.saves.read = s => reset(1, s.data); if (!game.saves.show('save')) game.saves.save(0); }\n392\t  function autosave() { if (!H.dead && !scripted) { game.saves.write = state; game.saves.autosave(); } }   // (not in the proof or the bot)\n393\t\n394\t  /* ---- THE ITEMS SCREEN (I) and THE ITEM BOX: the world stands still while they are open ---- */\n395\t  const status = () => H.hp > 66 ? ['FINE', '#5ad070'] : H.hp > 33 ? ['CAUTION', '#e8c040'] : ['DANGER', '#e8483a'];\n396\t  function openItems() { mode = 'items'; menu = { i: 0, pick: null, sub: null }; A.sfx('select'); world.camera.unlock(); H.aim = false; }\n397\t  function openBox() { mode = 'box'; menu = { side: 0, i: 0 }; A.sfx('door'); }\n398\t  function useItem(id) {\n399\t    const it = rpg.items[id];\n400\t    if (it.heal) { if (H.hp >= HP) { say('You are fine.'); return; } inv.remove(id); H.hp = Math.min(HP, H.hp + it.heal); A.sfx('heal'); say('You feel better.'); return; }\n401\t    say(it.info);\n402\t  }\n403\t  function itemsStep() {\n404\t    const I = game.input, M = menu, list = inv.list(), n = 6;\n405\t    if (I.pressed('items') || I.pressed('cancel')) { I.consumeAll(); if (M.sub) M.sub = null; else { mode = 'play'; menu = null; } return; }\n406\t    if (M.sub) {   // USE, MIX, INFO\n407\t      if (I.pressed('up')) M.sub.i = (M.sub.i + 2) % 3; if (I.pressed('down')) M.sub.i = (M.sub.i + 1) % 3;\n408\t      if (I.pressed('act') || I.pressed('confirm')) { I.consumeAll(); const s = list[M.i], c = M.sub.i; M.sub = null; if (!s) return; if (c === 0) useItem(s.id); else if (c === 1) { M.pick = M.i; say('Mix it with what?', 2); } else say(s.item.info); A.sfx('confirm'); }\n409\t      return;\n410\t    }\n411\t    if (I.pressed('left')) M.i = (M.i + n - 1) % n; if (I.pressed('right')) M.i = (M.i + 1) % n;\n412\t    if (I.pressed('up') || I.pressed('down')) M.i = (M.i + 3) % n;\n413\t    if (I.pressed('act') || I.pressed('confirm')) {\n414\t      I.consumeAll(); const s = list[M.i]; if (!s) return;\n415\t      if (M.pick !== null) { const a = list[M.pick], r = a && M.pick !== M.i && MIX[a.id + '+' + s.id]; M.pick = null; if (!r) { say('They do not mix.'); A.sfx('bump'); return; } inv.remove(a.id); inv.remove(s.id); inv.add(r); A.sfx('heal'); say('Mixed: ' + rpg.items[r].name + '.'); return; }\n416\t      M.sub = { i: 0 }; A.sfx('select');\n417\t    }\n418\t  }\n419\t  function boxStep() {\n420\t    const I = game.input, M = menu, lists = [inv.list(), box.list()];\n421\t    if (I.pressed('cancel') || I.pressed('items')) { I.consumeAll(); mode = 'play'; menu = null; A.sfx('door'); return; }\n422\t    if (I.pressed('left') || I.pressed('right')) { M.side ^= 1; M.i = 0; A.sfx('select'); }\n423\t    const L = lists[M.side], cap = M.side ? Math.max(1, L.length) : 6;\n424\t    if (I.pressed('up')) M.i = (M.i + cap - 1) % cap; if (I.pressed('down')) M.i = (M.i + 1) % cap;\n425\t    if (I.pressed('act') || I.pressed('confirm')) {\n426\t      I.consumeAll(); const s = L[M.i]; if (!s) return;\n427\t      const from = M.side ? box : inv, to = M.side ? inv : box;\n428\t      if (!to.add(s.id, s.n)) { say('No room.'); A.sfx('bump'); return; }\n429\t      from.remove(s.id, s.n); A.sfx('pickup'); M.i = Math.max(0, Math.min(M.i, lists[M.side].length - 2));\n430\t    }\n431\t  }\n432\t\n433\t  /* ---- THE DOGS DRAWN WITH THE PEN: a body, a head, four legs at a gallop (part way between steps) ---- */\n434\t  function drawDog(e) {\n435\t    const k = game.paused ? 1 : clamp(game.alpha, 0, 1), x = lerp(e.px, e.x, k), y = lerp(e.py, e.y, k), z = e.z, pen = world.pen, run = Math.min(1, Math.hypot(e.vx, e.vy) / 60), ph = e.phase, dead = !e.alive;\n436\t    const c = '#4a3c36', dk = '#2e2622', raw = '#8a3a34';\n437\t    pen.at(x, y, z + (dead ? -3 : 0), e.facing); if (e.flash > 0) pen.flash = true;\n438\t    const bob = dead ? 0 : Math.abs(Math.sin(ph)) * 1.2 * run, tilt = dead ? 0 : Math.sin(ph) * .06 * run;\n439\t    pen.ball(0, 0, 9 + bob, 7.2, 3.2, 3.6, c).ball(3.2, 0, 10 + bob, 3.2, 3.4, 3.6, dk).ball(-1, 1.8, 9.6 + bob, 2.2, 1.2, 1.6, raw);\n440\t    const hz = 12.5 + bob + (dead ? -6 : 0) - tilt * 10;\n441\t    pen.ball(7.6, 0, hz, 2.8, 2.4, 2.4, c).cone(9.4, 0, hz - .6, 13, 0, hz - 1.4, 1.5, dk).cone(7, -1.4, hz + 1.4, 6.4, -1.8, hz + 4.4, .9, dk).cone(7, 1.4, hz + 1.4, 6.4, 1.8, hz + 4.4, .9, dk);\n442\t    pen.glow(9.2, -1.1, hz + .8, .45, '#ff3a2a').glow(9.2, 1.1, hz + .8, .45, '#ff3a2a');\n443\t    pen.tube(-6.6, 0, 10 + bob, -10, 0, 12 + bob + Math.sin(ph * 2) * 1.5, .8, dk);\n444\t    for (const [lx, ly, o] of [[4.6, -2, 0], [4.6, 2, PI], [-4.6, -2, PI * .6], [-4.6, 2, PI * 1.6]]) {\n445\t      const s = dead ? .4 : Math.sin(ph + o), fx = lx + s * 3.4 * run, fz = dead ? 2 : Math.max(0, Math.cos(ph + o)) * 2.4 * run;\n446\t      pen.tube(lx, ly, 8 + bob, (lx + fx) / 2 + 1, ly, 4 + fz, 1.1, c).tube((lx + fx) / 2 + 1, ly, 4 + fz, fx, ly, fz + .4, .8, dk);\n447\t    }\n448\t    pen.flash = false; pen.at();\n449\t  }\n450\t\n451\t  /* ---- THE HUD: little in play (as in the games it follows): a message, the gun when aiming, the status in a corner;\n452\t   * the items screen and the item box over the picture ---- */\n453\t  function ecg(g, x, y, w, color, t) {   // a heartbeat line, faster as it gets worse\n454\t    const rate = H.hp > 66 ? 1.2 : H.hp > 33 ? 1.8 : 2.6;\n455\t    for (let i = 0; i < w; i++) { const u = (i / w + t * rate * .5) % 1, v = u > .42 && u < .46 ? -6 : u > .46 && u < .5 ? 5 : u > .5 && u < .53 ? -2 : 0; E.px.rect(g, x + i, y + v, 1, 1, color); }\n456\t  }\n457\t  function hud(g, r) {\n458\t    const [word, col] = status();\n459\t    if (mode === 'play') {\n460\t      E.font.text(g, word, 6, 6, col, { outline: '#000', font: 'tiny' }); ecg(g, 6, 18, 40, col, game.real);\n461\t      if (H.aim) E.font.text(g, (H.gun ? 'HANDGUN ' + H.clip + ' / ' + inv.count('ammo') : 'KNIFE') + (H.aimLv ? H.aimLv > 0 ? '  HIGH' : '  LOW' : ''), r.W - 6, 6, '#e8e0d0', { align: 'right', outline: '#000', font: 'tiny' });\n462\t      if (H.reloadT > 0) E.font.text(g, 'RELOADING', r.W - 6, 6, '#e8c040', { align: 'right', outline: '#000', font: 'tiny' });\n463\t      if (H.grabbed) E.font.text(g, (touch() ? 'TAP ACT' : 'TAP ' + game.input.label('act')) + ' TO SHAKE FREE', r.W / 2, r.H / 2 + 30, '#ff8a7a', { align: 'center', outline: '#000' });\n464\t    }\n465\t    // (the message: above the touch buttons on a phone)\n466\t    if (msg) { const w = Math.min(r.W - 20, 300), ta = game.input.touchArea(), y = ta && ta.y0 < r.H - 24 ? Math.min(r.H - 46, ta.y0 - 28) : r.H - 46; E.ui.box(g, (r.W - w) / 2, y, w, 22, { bg: '#08060a', border: '#5a5060' }); E.font.text(g, msg.text, r.W / 2, y + 7, '#e8e0d0', { align: 'center', outline: false, font: msg.text.length * 6 > w - 12 ? 'tiny' : undefined }); }\n467\t    if (mode === 'items') {\n468\t      const M = menu, list = inv.list(), w = Math.min(r.W - 16, 330), x0 = (r.W - w) / 2, y0 = Math.max(8, r.H / 2 - 90);\n469\t      g.save(); g.fillStyle = '#000'; g.globalAlpha = .7; g.fillRect(0, 0, r.bw, r.bh); g.restore(); g._c = null;\n470\t      E.ui.box(g, x0, y0, w, 160, { bg: '#0c0a10', border: '#6a6070' });\n471\t      E.font.text(g, 'CONDITION', x0 + 10, y0 + 8, '#a8a0b0', { font: 'tiny', outline: false }); E.font.text(g, word, x0 + 10, y0 + 20, col, { outline: false }); ecg(g, x0 + 10, y0 + 40, 90, col, game.real);\n472\t      E.font.text(g, H.gun ? 'HANDGUN  ' + H.clip + ' / ' + inv.count('ammo') : 'KNIFE', x0 + 10, y0 + 54, '#e8e0d0', { font: 'tiny', outline: false });\n473\t      for (let i = 0; i < 6; i++) {\n474\t        const s = list[i], cx = x0 + w - 186 + (i % 3) * 60, cy = y0 + 10 + Math.floor(i / 3) * 52, sel = i === M.i, pk = M.pick === i;\n475\t        E.ui.box(g, cx, cy, 54, 46, { bg: sel ? '#2a2234' : '#16121c', border: pk ? '#e8c040' : sel ? '#e8e0d0' : '#4a4250' });\n476\t        if (s) { E.px.sprite(g, ICONS[s.id], cx + 17, cy + 7, { scale: 2 }); if (s.n > 1) E.font.text(g, String(s.n), cx + 50, cy + 34, '#e8e0d0', { align: 'right', font: 'tiny', outline: '#000' }); }\n477\t      }\n478\t      const s = list[M.i]; E.font.text(g, s ? s.item.name : '', x0 + 10, y0 + 120, '#ffe0a0', { outline: false }); E.font.text(g, s ? s.item.info : '', x0 + 10, y0 + 134, '#c8c0d0', { font: 'tiny', outline: false });\n479\t      if (M.sub) { const sx = x0 + w - 186 + (M.i % 3) * 60 + 30, sy = y0 + 10 + Math.floor(M.i / 3) * 52 + 26; E.ui.box(g, sx, sy, 50, 40, { bg: '#08060a', border: '#e8e0d0' }); ['USE', 'MIX', 'INFO'].forEach((t, k) => E.font.text(g, (k === M.sub.i ? '▸' : ' ') + t, sx + 5, sy + 5 + k * 11, k === M.sub.i ? '#ffd36a' : '#e8e0d0', { font: 'tiny', outline: false })); }\n480\t    }\n481\t    if (mode === 'box') {\n482\t      const M = menu, w = Math.min(r.W - 16, 330), x0 = (r.W - w) / 2, y0 = Math.max(8, r.H / 2 - 90), L = [inv.list(), box.list()];\n483\t      g.save(); g.fillStyle = '#000'; g.globalAlpha = .7; g.fillRect(0, 0, r.bw, r.bh); g.restore(); g._c = null;\n484\t      ['YOURS', 'THE ITEM BOX'].forEach((t, side) => {\n485\t        const x = x0 + side * (w / 2 + 2), ww = w / 2 - 2; E.ui.box(g, x, y0, ww, 170, { bg: '#0c0a10', border: M.side === side ? '#e8e0d0' : '#4a4250' });\n486\t        E.font.text(g, t, x + 8, y0 + 7, '#a8a0b0', { font: 'tiny', outline: false });\n487\t        const rows = side ? Math.max(1, L[1].length) : 6;\n488\t        for (let i = 0; i < Math.min(rows, 12); i++) { const s = L[side][i], sel = M.side === side && M.i === i; E.font.text(g, (sel ? '▸ ' : '  ') + (s ? s.item.name + (s.n > 1 ? ' x' + s.n : '') : '-'), x + 6, y0 + 20 + i * 12, sel ? '#ffd36a' : '#e8e0d0', { font: 'tiny', outline: false }); }\n489\t      });\n490\t    }\n491\t  }\n492\t\n493\t  /* ---- the controls this step: the stick by the player's setting (camera.steer), the buttons ---- */\n494\t  const KEYS = { up: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'Pad12'], down: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'Pad13'], left: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'Pad14'], right: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'Pad15'],\n495\t    act: ['KeyJ', 'Space', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0'], aim: ['KeyK', 'Mouse2', 'Pad6', 'Pad4'], run: ['ShiftLeft', 'ShiftRight', 'Pad1'], swap: ['KeyQ', 'Pad3'], items: ['KeyI', 'Tab', 'Pad2'],\n496\t    start: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Pad9'], pause: ['Escape', 'KeyP', 'Pad9'], confirm: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Pad0'], cancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'Pad1'] };\n497\t  const TOUCH = ['items', 'run', 'aim', 'act'], TOUCH_LABELS = { items: 'ITEMS', run: 'RUN', aim: 'AIM', act: 'ACT' };\n498\t  const ctl = { move: [0, 0], tank: false, down: a => game.input.down(a), pressed: a => game.input.pressed(a), use: a => game.input.consume(a) };\n499\t  function controls(dt) { ctl.tank = world.camera.tank; world.camera.steer(hero, game.input.move(), H.aim || H.grabbed || H.dead ? 0 : dt, ctl.move); if (H.aim) ctl.move[0] = game.input.move()[0]; return ctl; }\n500\t\n501\t  /** the proof: a scripted walk from the foyer, the stick held up across a cut (it keeps its way, as a player's does),\n502\t   *  to the west door (the door between rooms), then aim at the dead in the hall (the lock) and shoot; n steps of 1/120\n503\t   *  s. The world's hash with the camera's cuts and zone and the lock's target: the same on WebGPU, WebGL 2 and run\n504\t   *  again */\n505\t  function run(n = 600) {\n506\t    reset(3); scripted = true; const keys = new Set(), c = { move: [0, 0], tank: false, down: a => keys.has(a), pressed: a => keys.has('tap:' + a), use() {} }, door = doors.west;\n507\t    const toward = (x, y) => { const dx = x - hero.x, dy = y - hero.y, d = Math.hypot(dx, dy); c.move[0] = d > 3 ? dx / d : 0; c.move[1] = d > 3 ? dy / d : 0; return d; };\n508\t    let phase = 0;\n509\t    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n510\t      keys.clear(); keys.add('run'); c.move[0] = c.move[1] = 0;\n511\t      if (phase === 0) { world.camera.steer(hero, [0, -1], 1 / 120, c.move, { tank: false }); if (world.camera.cuts) phase = 1; }   // up, held across the foyer's cut\n512\t      else if (phase === 1) { if (toward(door.x + 15, door.y) < 4) { phase = 2; hero.facing = PI; } }\n513\t      else if (phase === 2) { keys.add('tap:act'); phase = 3; }\n514\t      else if (phase === 3) { if (!world.passing && H.room === 'west') phase = 4; }\n515\t      else { keys.add('aim'); if (i % 40 === 0) keys.add('tap:act'); }\n516\t      step(1 / 120, c);\n517\t    }\n518\t    scripted = false; const L = world.camera.lockOn, Z = world.camera.zone;\n519\t    return world.hash([H.hp, H.clip, world.camera.cuts, ZONES.indexOf(Z), L ? enemies.indexOf(L) : -1, phase, enemies.filter(e => !e.alive).length]);\n520\t  }\n521\t\n522\t  /** the bot: plays the wing through to what waits in the gallery and fights it, by the game's own rules (each step a\n523\t   *  stick and buttons, as a player gives them): walk the flow field to each thing it needs, opening (and unlocking)\n524\t   *  the doors in its way, fight what comes (aim, shoot, low at dogs; the knife when the gun is dry), heal, crank the\n525\t   *  grille. Returns what it did: { reached, boss, won, rooms, took, opened, killed, shots, hp, steps, errors } */\n526\t  function bot(max = 120 * 60 * 12) {\n527\t    reset(5); scripted = true; const seen = new Set(['foyer']), keys = new Set(), c = { move: [0, 0], tank: false, down: a => keys.has(a), pressed: a => keys.has('tap:' + a), use: a => keys.delete('tap:' + a) };\n528\t    const GOALS = [['take', 'herbG1'], ['take', 'crank0'], ['take', 'ammo3'], ['take', 'ironkey0'], ['take', 'herbG0'], ['take', 'ammo1'], ['take', 'ammo2'], ['take', 'herbG2'],\n529\t      ['take', 'ammo0'], ['use', 'socket'], ['take', 'brasskey0'], ['take', 'herbR0'], ['fight', 'boss'], ['door', 'exit']];\n530\t    let g = 0, steps = 0, errors = 0, stuck = 0, lastD = 1e9, saved = false; const f = world.flow(), dt = 1 / 120;\n531\t    const where = () => { const [k, id] = GOALS[g] || []; if (k === 'door') return doors[id]; if (k === 'take') return items.find(t => t.data.key === id); if (k === 'use') return flags.crank ? null : socket; if (k === 'fight') return enemies.find(e => e.type === 'boss' && e.alive); return null; };\n532\t    const face = a => { hero.facing = E.approachAng(hero.facing, a, dt * 12); return Math.abs(E.angDiff(hero.facing, a)) < .1; };\n533\t    try {\n534\t      for (; steps < max && g < GOALS.length && !ended && !H.dead; steps++) {\n535\t        keys.clear(); c.move[0] = c.move[1] = 0;\n536\t        if (world.passing || H.crankT > 0) { step(dt, c); continue; }\n537\t        if (H.grabbed) { if (steps % 6 === 0) keys.add('tap:act'); step(dt, c); continue; }\n538\t        if (H.hp < 50) { const herb = inv.list().find(s => rpg.items[s.id].heal); if (herb) useItem(herb.id); }\n539\t        seen.add(H.room);\n540\t        // a threat in sight: aim (low at a dog), shoot; the knife up close when the gun is dry\n541\t        const foes = awake().filter(e => Math.hypot(e.x - hero.x, e.y - hero.y) < (e.type === 'boss' ? 200 : 120) && world.clear(hero.x, hero.y, hero.z + 16, e.x, e.y, e.z + 10));\n542\t        if (foes.length) {\n543\t          const dry = H.clip === 0 && !inv.count('ammo'); if (H.gun === dry) keys.add('tap:swap');\n544\t          const L = world.camera.lockOn, d = L ? Math.hypot(L.x - hero.x, L.y - hero.y) : 0;\n545\t          if (!H.gun && L && d > 18) { const a = Math.atan2(L.y - hero.y, L.x - hero.x); c.move[0] = Math.cos(a); c.move[1] = Math.sin(a); }\n546\t          else { keys.add('aim'); if (L && L.type === 'dog' && H.aimLv > -1) keys.add('tap:down'); if (L && L.type !== 'dog' && H.aimLv < 0) keys.add('tap:up');\n547\t            if (L && Math.abs(E.angDiff(hero.facing, Math.atan2(L.y - hero.y, L.x - hero.x))) < .12 && H.fireT <= 0) keys.add('tap:act'); }\n548\t          step(dt, c); continue;\n549\t        }\n550\t        const goal = GOALS[g], tgt = where(); if (!tgt) { g++; continue; }\n551\t        const d = Math.hypot(tgt.x - hero.x, tgt.y - hero.y);\n552\t        // there: face it and check it (a door: open it; the exit: out)\n553\t        if (goal[0] !== 'fight' && d < (goal[0] === 'door' ? 22 : 18)) {\n554\t          if (face(Math.atan2(tgt.y - hero.y, tgt.x - hero.x))) { keys.add('tap:act'); step(dt, c); if (goal[0] !== 'door' && (!items.includes(tgt) || flags.crank || H.crankT > 0)) g++; } else step(dt, c);\n555\t          if (inv.has('brasskey') && !saved) saved = game.saves.save(2, state());   // (a save on the way, loaded back at the end)\n556\t          continue;\n557\t        }\n558\t        // on the way: the flow field; a closed door in the way is opened (unlocked first, with the key it takes)\n559\t        f.to(tgt.x, tgt.y); const dir = f.dir(hero.x, hero.y, [0, 0]) || [(tgt.x - hero.x) / (d || 1), (tgt.y - hero.y) / (d || 1)];\n560\t        const door = world.reach(hero, 10, ['door']);\n561\t        if (door && door !== tgt && door !== gate && (door.x - hero.x) * dir[0] + (door.y - hero.y) * dir[1] > 0) { if (face(Math.atan2(door.y - hero.y, door.x - hero.x) + (door.yaw ? 0 : 0))) keys.add('tap:act'); step(dt, c); continue; }\n562\t        c.move[0] = dir[0]; c.move[1] = dir[1]; keys.add('run');\n563\t        stuck = d < lastD - .01 ? 0 : stuck + 1; lastD = d; if (stuck > 240) { c.move[0] = -dir[1]; c.move[1] = dir[0]; if (stuck > 330) stuck = 0; }\n564\t        step(dt, c);\n565\t      }\n566\t    } catch (e) { errors++; console.error(e); }\n567\t    scripted = false; const boss = enemies.find(e => e.type === 'boss');\n568\t    const r = { reached: seen.has('gallery'), boss: !!boss && !boss.alive, won: ended === 1 && !H.dead, dead: H.dead, rooms: [...seen], took: flags.taken.length, opened: flags.open.slice(), killed: flags.dead.length, shots: H.shots, hp: H.hp, goal: g, of: GOALS.length, steps, errors, saved };\n569\t    // the save made on the way, loaded back: the wing as it stood then (the crank turned, the brass key in hand, in the library)\n570\t    game.saves.read = s => reset(1, s.data); const back = saved && game.saves.load(2);\n571\t    if (back) r.loaded = { room: roomAt(hero.x, hero.y), crank: flags.crank, brass: inv.has('brasskey'), dead: flags.dead.length, gate: !gate.solid };\n572\t    game.saves.erase(2); ended = 0; return r;\n573\t  }\n574\t\n575\t  return {\n576\t    view: 'iso', input: KEYS, pausable: true, touch: TOUCH, camera: { zoom: [.6, 2] },\n577\t    enter() {\n578\t      game.settings.define(W3.CONTROLS); reset(1); active = world; A.music(null); game.input.touchButtons(TOUCH, { labels: TOUCH_LABELS });\n579\t      game.saves.write = state; game.saves.read = s => reset(1, s.data);\n580\t      if (game.saves.any) { mode = 'intro'; menu = new E.Menu(game, ['CONTINUE', 'NEW GAME'], { y: 'center', onPick: i => { mode = 'play'; menu = null; if (i === 0) game.saves.load(game.saves.latest().slot); } }); }\n581\t      say('The east and west wings. Find a way out.', 3.5);\n582\t    },\n583\t    update(dt) {\n584\t      if (mode === 'intro') { menu.update(dt); world.step(0); return; }\n585\t      if (mode === 'items') { itemsStep(); world.step(0); return; }\n586\t      if (mode === 'box') { boxStep(); world.step(0); return; }\n587\t      if (game.input.pressed('items') && !H.dead && !world.passing && !H.grabbed) { openItems(); return; }\n588\t      step(dt, controls(dt));\n589\t      const want = H.room === 'gallery' && enemies.some(e => e.type === 'boss' && e.alive) ? DREAD : H.room === 'foyer' ? SAFE : HALL;\n590\t      if (want !== song && !ended && !H.dead) { song = want; A.music(want); }\n591\t      const inp = game.input; inp.touchSet('act', H.aim ? 'FIRE' : null, true);\n592\t    },\n593\t    draw(r) {\n594\t      world.draw(r);\n595\t      r.overlay(g => hud(g, r));\n596\t      if (mode === 'intro') menu.draw(r);\n597\t    },\n598\t    get world() { return world; }, get hero() { return hero; }, get state() { return H; }, get enemies() { return enemies; }, get inv() { return inv; }, get flags() { return flags; },\n599\t    get mode() { return mode; }, reset, run, bot, ZONES, ROOMS\n600\t  };\n601\t})();\n602\tscenes.horror = HORROR;\n603\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23de6e6b-3ae6-4bf5-9764-44b18bb5857c","uuid":"0a19aea9-91ba-4c54-ac86-63a03cfc4c45","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:24:10.065Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211953__xee4d12/work/_research/engine/src/starter3d/40-horror.js","content":"/* =====================================================================================\n * SLICE 4  HORROR  (Resident Evil, Alone in the Dark, Silent Hill). @modules rpg\n * A mansion's east and west wings by flashlight, each room under its own fixed camera (a cut as you walk on, the stick\n * keeping its way across it). Hold K (or a right click) to aim the pistol: it locks on the nearest thing in front, up and\n * down aim high and low (a dog is low), left and right pick another; J fires, or slashes with the knife (Q swaps).\n * J alone checks what is in front: doors (the door opens between rooms), things to take, the item box, the typewriter\n * (a save, in the 2D engine's slots). Shift runs; I opens the items: herbs heal, green and green or green and red mix.\n * Zombies shamble and grab (tap J to shake free), dogs run and leap; two keys and a crank open the way to what waits\n * in the gallery. Few bullets: walk round what you can. Settings, Tank controls: up walks the way you face, left and\n * right turn you. THE 3D: camera zones (world.camera.zones: fixed, one that turns after you, one on a rail), lock-on\n * (camera.lock, cycle), tank steering (camera.steer), the door between rooms (world.through), a flashlight with a\n * failing bulb (world.flashlight), fog. HORROR.run(n): a scripted walk's hash (the proof); HORROR.bot(): to the boss\n * ===================================================================================== */\nconst HORROR = (() => {\n  const T = 16, PI = Math.PI;\n  /* ---- THE WING: one character per 1-metre tile. Rooms: the foyer (the start, the typewriter and the item box), the\n   * west hall, the kitchen, the dining room, the east hall, the library (the crank's socket, the grille over the brass\n   * key) and the gallery. Marks: @ the start, z zombies, d D dogs, G what waits, g r herbs, a A bullets, i the iron key,\n   * q the brass key, c the crank, X the typewriter, Y the item box, O the crank's socket ---- */\n  const LEVEL = {\n    rows: [\n      '####################..########################',\n      '#.i.........#.................#..........#...#',\n      '#.........g.#.t.............t.#..........#.q.#',\n      '#..z........#.................#.KKK..KKK.#...#',\n      '#...h.h.h...#........G........#..........##..#',\n      '#...T.T.T...#...PP.......PP...#.....a........#',\n      '#...j.j.j...#...PP.......PP...#.........O...t#',\n      '#...........#.................#.KKK..KKK.....#',\n      '#.t......z..#.................#..............#',\n      '#..........a#.................#..z.........r.#',\n      '#####..######.................#..............#',\n      '#,SS,,,,SS,,#.................######..########',\n      '#,,,,,,,,,k,#.................#####....#######',\n      '#,,D,,c,,,,,########..#############....#######',\n      '#,,,,,,,,,,,#,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,#####...a#######',\n      '#B,,,,,,,,B,#,t,,,,,,,,,,,,,t,#####....#######',\n      '#,A,,,,,,,,,#,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,#####..z.#######',\n      '#####..######,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,#####....#######',\n      '####....#####,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,#####....#######',\n      '####..g.#####,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,#####....#######',\n      '####....#####,,,b,,,,,,,,,b,,,#####....#######',\n      '####........#,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,#.......t#######',\n      '####..z......,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,......d..#######',\n      '####.........,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,.g.......#######',\n      '####........#,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,#........#######',\n      '#############,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,################',\n      '#############,,,X,,,,@,,,,Y,,,################',\n      '#############,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,################',\n      '#############,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,################',\n      '##############################################'],\n    ground: 'planks', colors: { base: '#4e3324', dark: '#3e281c', line: '#22140e' }, side: 'block', color: '#4a4248',\n    legend: (() => {\n      const tiles = { ground: 'tiles', colors: { a: '#6e665e', b: '#2e2a28', size: 8 } }, on = (sp, o) => Object.assign({}, sp, o);\n      return { ',': tiles, P: { pillar: 56 }, t: { torch: true }, T: { shape: 'table' }, h: { shape: 'chair', facing: PI / 2 }, j: { shape: 'chair', facing: -PI / 2 },\n        S: on(tiles, { shape: 'shelf', facing: PI / 2 }), B: on(tiles, { shape: 'barrel' }), k: on(tiles, { shape: 'stool' }), K: { shape: 'bookcase', facing: PI / 2 }, b: on(tiles, { shape: 'bench' }),\n        '@': on(tiles, { mark: 'start' }), X: on(tiles, { mark: 'typewriter' }), Y: on(tiles, { mark: 'trunk' }), D: on(tiles, { mark: 'dog' }), c: on(tiles, { mark: 'crank' }), A: on(tiles, { mark: 'ammo' }),\n        z: { mark: 'zombie' }, d: { mark: 'dog' }, G: { mark: 'boss' }, g: { mark: 'herbG' }, r: { mark: 'herbR' }, a: { mark: 'ammo' }, i: { mark: 'ironkey' }, q: { mark: 'brasskey' }, O: { mark: 'socket' } };\n    })()\n  };\n  // the rooms (boxes in units, to the middle of their walls) and the camera of each part of them: a fixed one (at, look),\n  // one that turns after you (follow), one that slides along a rail level with you (rail)\n  const R = (x0, y0, x1, y1) => [x0 * T, y0 * T, x1 * T, y1 * T];\n  const ROOMS = { foyer: R(12.5, 13.5, 30.5, 29.5), west: R(3.5, 17.5, 12.5, 25.5), kitchen: R(0, 10.5, 12.5, 17.5), dining: R(0, 0, 12.5, 10.5), east: R(30, 11.5, 39.5, 25.5), library: R(30.5, 0, 46, 11.5), gallery: R(12.5, 0, 30.5, 13.5) };\n  const ZONES = [\n    { room: 'foyer', box: R(12.5, 24, 30.5, 29.5), at: [468, 458, 64], look: [324, 352, 0], fov: 52 },\n    { room: 'foyer', box: R(12.5, 13.5, 30.5, 24), at: [216, 228, 62], look: [380, 364, 0], fov: 52 },\n    { room: 'west', box: R(3.5, 21, 12.5, 25.5), rail: [[196, 342, 52], [74, 342, 52]], fov: 56 },\n    { room: 'west', box: R(3.5, 17.5, 8.5, 21), at: [122, 396, 50], look: [96, 292, 0], fov: 56 },\n    { room: 'kitchen', box: R(0, 10.5, 12.5, 17.5), at: [184, 268, 58], look: [70, 196, 0], fov: 56 },\n    { room: 'dining', box: R(0, 0, 12.5, 10.5), at: [184, 22, 62], follow: true, fov: 56 },\n    { room: 'east', box: R(30, 20.5, 35, 25.5), at: [490, 396, 50], look: [604, 360, 0], fov: 56 },\n    { room: 'east', box: R(35, 11.5, 39.5, 25.5), at: [592, 398, 58], follow: true, fov: 52 },\n    { room: 'library', box: R(30.5, 0, 37.5, 11.5), at: [504, 170, 62], look: [584, 52, 0], fov: 56 },\n    { room: 'library', box: R(37.5, 0, 46, 11.5), at: [716, 172, 62], look: [646, 60, 0], fov: 56 },\n    { room: 'gallery', box: R(12.5, 0, 30.5, 13.5), rail: [[226, 206, 104], [446, 206, 104]], height: 26, fov: 58 }\n  ];\n  const roomAt = (x, y) => { for (const k in ROOMS) { const b = ROOMS[k]; if (x >= b[0] && x <= b[2] && y >= b[1] && y <= b[3]) return k; } return null; };\n  // the doors (2 tiles wide in their gaps: yaw 0 spans x, PI / 2 spans y); the grille over the brass key rises\n  const DOORS = [\n    { id: 'west', x: 200, y: 368, yaw: PI / 2 }, { id: 'kitchen', x: 96, y: 280 }, { id: 'dining', x: 96, y: 168 },\n    { id: 'east', x: 488, y: 368, yaw: PI / 2, locked: 'ironkey' }, { id: 'library', x: 592, y: 184 },\n    { id: 'gallery', x: 336, y: 216, locked: 'brasskey' }, { id: 'exit', x: 336, y: 8, locked: 'sealed' }];\n\n  /* ---- ITEMS: the rpg module's items and a Resident Evil inventory of six slots; the item box holds the rest ---- */\n  const rpg = new E.RPG({ items: {\n    herbG: { name: 'Green herb', kind: 'use', heal: 30, info: 'A medicinal plant. Mix it to make it stronger.' },\n    herbR: { name: 'Red herb', kind: 'use', info: 'Useless alone. Mixed with a green herb, it heals completely.' },\n    herbGG: { name: 'Mixed herbs (G+G)', kind: 'use', heal: 60, info: 'Two green herbs, ground together.' },\n    herbGR: { name: 'Mixed herbs (G+R)', kind: 'use', heal: 100, info: 'Green and red: it heals every wound.' },\n    ammo: { name: 'Handgun bullets', kind: 'use', stack: 60, info: 'Bullets for the handgun.' },\n    ironkey: { name: 'Iron key', kind: 'key', info: 'A heavy key. An iron lock is cast on its bow.' },\n    brasskey: { name: 'Brass key', kind: 'key', info: 'A polished key with a brass lock engraved on it.' },\n    crank: { name: 'Crank', kind: 'key', info: 'A square-ended crank handle. It fits some mechanism.' } } });\n  const MIX = { 'herbG+herbG': 'herbGG', 'herbG+herbR': 'herbGR', 'herbR+herbG': 'herbGR' };\n  const KEY_LOOK = { ironkey: '#8a8c98', brasskey: '#e0b048' };\n  // the items' icons on the items screen (pixel sprites, drawn at twice their size)\n  const leaf = c => E.sprite(['...gg....', '..gGg..g.', '.gGgg.gG.', '.gg.ggGg.', '..g.gGg..', '...ggg...', '..bbbbb..', '..bBBBb..', '...bbb...'], { g: c, G: E.shade(c, .3), b: '#7a5a40', B: '#9a7a5a' });\n  const ICONS = { herbG: leaf('#4aa04a'), herbR: leaf('#c04040'), herbGG: leaf('#6ac05a'), herbGR: leaf('#c0a040'),\n    ammo: E.sprite(['.y.y.y...', '.Y.Y.Y...', '.c.c.c...', '.c.c.c...', 'ooooooo..', 'oOOOOOo..', 'oOOOOOo..', 'ooooooo..'], { y: '#ffe090', Y: '#d8b048', c: '#b88a30', o: '#3a4628', O: '#5a6a3a' }),\n    ironkey: E.sprite(['.kkk.....', 'k...k....', 'k...k....', '.kkkkkkkk', '.....k.k.', '.....k...'], { k: KEY_LOOK.ironkey }), brasskey: E.sprite(['.kkk.....', 'k...k....', 'k...k....', '.kkkkkkkk', '.....k.k.', '.....k...'], { k: KEY_LOOK.brasskey }),\n    crank: E.sprite(['mm.......', 'mm.......', '.m.......', '.mmmmmm..', '......m..', '......mww', '.......ww'], { m: '#8a8a94', w: '#6a4a30' }) };\n  // things drawn by code for this slice (the engine's kinds are in its manual): a potted herb, a box of bullets, the\n  // crank, its socket in the library\n  W3.THINGS.herb = (p, t) => { const c = t.color || '#4aa04a'; p.box(0, 0, 2.2, 6, 6, 4.4, '#7a5a40').box(0, 0, 4.6, 6.4, 6.4, .8, '#5a3e2a'); for (let k = 0; k < 6; k++) { const a = k * TAU / 6; p.cone(Math.cos(a) * .6, Math.sin(a) * .6, 4.6, Math.cos(a) * 3.4, Math.sin(a) * 3.4, 10 + (k & 1) * 2, 1.6, E.shade(c, (k & 1) * .15)); } };\n  W3.THINGS.ammo = (p) => { p.box(0, 0, 1.8, 7, 5, 3.6, '#5a6a3a').box(0, 0, 3.7, 7.2, 5.2, .4, '#3a4628').box(-1, -2.6, 2, 3, .3, 1.4, '#e8d890'); for (let k = 0; k < 3; k++) p.tube(-2 + k * 2, 3, 3.6, -2 + k * 2, 3, 5.4, .55, '#d8b048'); };\n  W3.THINGS.crank = (p) => { p.tube(-4, 0, 1, 3, 0, 1, .7, '#6a6a74').tube(3, 0, 1, 3, 0, 5, .7, '#6a6a74').tube(3, 0, 5, 6, 0, 5, .9, '#4a3020').box(-4.4, 0, 1, 1.4, 1.4, 1.4, '#3a3a42'); };\n  W3.THINGS.socket = (p, t) => {   // a cast plate on a post, a square hole; with the crank in it, the handle turns\n    p.box(0, 0, 6, 3, 3, 12, '#3a3640').box(0, 0, 13, 9, 3, 9, '#5a5664').ball(0, -1.6, 13, 1.8, .6, 1.8, '#18161c');\n    if (t.on) { const a = t.turn || 0; p.tube(0, -1.8, 13, 0, -5, 13, .6, '#6a6a74').tube(0, -5, 13, Math.cos(a) * 4, -5, 13 + Math.sin(a) * 4, .6, '#6a6a74').ball(Math.cos(a) * 4, -6, 13 + Math.sin(a) * 4, 1, 1, 1, '#4a3020'); }\n  };\n\n  /* ---- THE CAST: the hero, the dead of the house, its dogs, and what waits in the gallery ---- */\n  const HERO_COLORS = { cloth: '#3a4e6a', pants: '#2a2c36', boot: '#1e1c22', belt: '#4a3a2a', hair: '#3a2418', skin: '#e0b090', glove: '#2a2a30', metal: '#4a4c56', metalDk: '#2a2a30', hilt: '#3a3a40' };\n  const ZOMBIE_COLORS = [\n    { skin: '#8a9a7e', hair: '#2e2a26', cloth: '#5a4a52', pants: '#33302e', boot: '#262220', belt: '#4a3a2a' },\n    { skin: '#9a9488', hair: '#4a3e30', cloth: '#6a5a44', pants: '#2e2e34', boot: '#24221e', belt: '#3a3026' },\n    { skin: '#7e8a7a', hair: '#1e1c1a', cloth: '#3e4a5a', pants: '#2a2826', boot: '#201e1c', belt: '#3a3026' }];\n  const BOSS_COLORS = { skin: '#b8a090', hair: '#2a2024', cloth: '#5a1e22', pants: '#2a2228', boot: '#1e1a1c', belt: '#3a2a22', eye: '#ff3a2a' };\n  const WALK = 26, RUN = 58, HP = 100, CLIP = 12, GUN_DMG = 10, HEAD_DMG = 26, KNIFE_DMG = 7, AIM_A = [-.42, 0, .42];\n  const KIND = {\n    zombie: { hp: 46, speed: [12, 17], r: 5, half: 8, head: 27 },\n    dog: { hp: 24, speed: [84, 92], r: 4.5, half: 0, head: 11 },\n    boss: { hp: 260, speed: [22, 22], r: 9, half: 15, head: 48 }\n  };\n\n  /* ---- SOUNDS AND MUSIC (the step sequencer's format: original songs) ---- */\n  const SOUNDS = {\n    gun: [{ wave: 'noise', freq: 2400, to: 300, dur: .16, vol: .5 }, { wave: 'square', freq: 220, to: 70, dur: .1, vol: .3 }],\n    dry: { wave: 'square', freq: 1800, dur: .02, vol: .12 }, reload: [{ wave: 'square', freq: 900, dur: .03, vol: .14 }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 3000, dur: .05, vol: .12, delay: .12 }],\n    moan: { wave: 'saw', freq: 92, to: 70, dur: .9, vol: .1, vib: [5, .08], filter: 'lowpass' }, bark: [{ wave: 'saw', freq: 420, to: 240, dur: .09, vol: .18 }, { wave: 'saw', freq: 400, to: 200, dur: .1, vol: .16, delay: .14 }],\n    bite: [{ wave: 'noise', freq: 1200, to: 300, dur: .14, vol: .4 }, { wave: 'square', freq: 160, to: 60, dur: .12, vol: .25 }],\n    crank: { wave: 'square', freq: 300, arp: [0, 0, 0, 0], step: .09, dur: .36, vol: .12, filter: 'lowpass' }, stab: { wave: 'noise', freq: 3200, to: 900, dur: .09, vol: .22 },\n    roar: [{ wave: 'saw', freq: 120, to: 50, dur: 1.2, vol: .22, vib: [8, .15] }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 400, to: 100, dur: 1, vol: .2, filter: 'lowpass' }]\n  };\n  const HALL = { bpm: 56, steps: 4, tracks: [   // the halls: a low drone, a slow minor figure, a heartbeat\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: .3, notes: 'D2 - - - - - - - | D2 - - - - - - - | Bb1 - - - - - - - | A1 - - - - - - -' },\n    { wave: 'pulse25', vol: .05, notes: '. . D4 . . F4 . . | E4 . . . . . . . | . . D4 . . Bb3 . . | A3 . . . C#4 . . .' },\n    { wave: 'sine', vol: .06, notes: '. . . . . . A4 . | . . . . . . . . | . . . . . . G4 . | . . . . F4 . E4 .' },\n    { wave: 'drums', vol: .05, notes: 'k k . . . . . . | k k . . . . . .' }] };\n  const SAFE = { bpm: 64, steps: 3, tracks: [   // the foyer: the typewriter's quiet, a waltz in the dark\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: .24, notes: 'F2 C3 A3 | F2 C3 A3 | D2 A2 F3 | D2 A2 F3 | Bb1 F2 D3 | Bb1 F2 D3 | C2 G2 E3 | C2 G2 E3' },\n    { wave: 'sine', vol: .1, notes: 'A4 - C5 | F5 - E5 | D5 - - | A4 - - | Bb4 - D5 | F5 - G5 | E5 - - | - - -' }] };\n  const DREAD = { bpm: 118, steps: 4, tracks: [   // the gallery's fight\n    { wave: 'saw', vol: .06, notes: 'D3 D3 . D3 Eb3 . D3 . | D3 D3 . D3 C3 . Bb2 . | D3 D3 . D3 Eb3 . F3 . | Eb3 . D3 . C#3 . . .' },\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: .3, notes: 'D2 . D2 . D2 . D2 . | Bb1 . Bb1 . Bb1 . Bb1 . | G1 . G1 . G1 . G1 . | A1 . A1 . A1 . A1 .' },\n    { wave: 'drums', vol: .1, notes: 'k . . k s . . . | k . k . s . . h' }] };\n\n  /* ---- THE STATE ---- */\n  let world = null, flow = null, hero = null, H = null, lamp = null, muzzle = null, rnd = Math.random;\n  let enemies = [], items = [], doors = {}, gate = null, socket = null, inv = null, box = null, flags = null, mode = 'play', menu = null, msg = null, song = null, ended = 0, scripted = false;\n  const shots = [];\n  BOOT.push(['The mansion', () => {\n    for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(SOUNDS)) A.define(k, v);\n    world = new W3(game, { level: LEVEL, torchLights: 4, torchShadows: 0, torchPower: 22, torchReach: 140, torchColor: '#ffb070', lights: 1, spots: 1,\n      ambient: ['#3a3e56', '#141018', 1.6], fog: { color: '#040406', near: 40, far: 250 }, sky: '#020203', camera: { mode: 'zones', zones: ZONES, reticle: '#ff5a3a', lockRange: 170 },\n      onDraw: () => { for (const e of enemies) if (e.type === 'dog') drawDog(e); for (const s of shots) world.pen.bar(s.x, s.y, s.z, s.x1, s.y1, s.z1, .5, .5, '#ffe8a8'); } });   // (the dogs and the shots' streaks, whichever scene draws the world)\n    flow = world.flow();\n  }]);\n\n  /** a fresh game, or the one a save holds (s: its data): the wing as it stood, the hero where it saved */\n  function reset(seed = 1, s = null) {\n    world.reset(); rnd = E.rng(seed); flow = world.flow();\n    flags = s ? JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(s.flags)) : { taken: [], dead: [], open: [], crank: false, boss: false };\n    const st = world.marks.start[0], at = s ? s.at : [st.x, st.y, -PI / 2];\n    hero = world.hero({ x: at[0], y: at[1], r: 4.5, rig: new E.Humanoid({ weapon: s && !s.gun ? 'sword' : 'gun', bladeLen: 5, hair: 'long', colors: HERO_COLORS, speedRef: 60 }) }); hero.facing = at[2];\n    H = { hp: s ? s.hp : HP, clip: s ? s.clip : CLIP, gun: s ? s.gun : true, aim: false, aimLv: 0, cool: 0, fireT: 0, reloadT: 0, hurtT: 0, grabbed: null, grabT: 0, shake: 0, stun: 0, crankT: 0, dead: false, deadT: 0, inv: 0, knife: null, room: roomAt(at[0], at[1]) || 'foyer', shots: 0 };\n    inv = rpg.inventory({ slots: 6 }); box = rpg.inventory({ slots: 40 });\n    for (const [id, n] of (s ? s.inv : [['ammo', 18], ['herbG', 1]])) inv.add(id, n);\n    for (const [id, n] of (s ? s.box : [])) box.add(id, n);\n    if (!lamp) { lamp = world.flashlight(hero, { power: 46, reach: 300, angle: .46, flicker: .35 }); muzzle = world.light({ color: '#ffd090', reach: 160, power: 0 }); }\n    lamp.actor = hero; lamp.on = true;\n    // the doors, the grille, the socket, the save room's things, what is left to take, and who is still about\n    doors = {}; for (const d of DOORS) doors[d.id] = world.thing('door', d.x, d.y, 0, { yaw: d.yaw || 0, w: 30, h: 40, swing: true, color: '#4a2c1c', frame: '#3a3036', locked: flags.open.includes(d.id) ? null : d.locked || null, solid: true, data: { id: d.id } });\n    if (flags.boss) doors.exit.locked = null;\n    gate = world.thing('door', 44 * T, 4.5 * T, 0, { w: 30, h: 36, color: '#3a3a44', frame: '#3a3036', solid: !flags.crank, open: flags.crank ? 1 : 0, data: { id: 'gate' } });\n    const sk = world.marks.socket[0]; socket = world.thing('socket', sk.x, sk.y, 0, { yaw: PI / 2, on: flags.crank, turn: 0, solid: [8, 6, 16] });\n    world.thing('typewriter', world.marks.typewriter[0].x, world.marks.typewriter[0].y, 0, { yaw: PI / 2, solid: [22, 13, 16] });\n    world.thing('trunk', world.marks.trunk[0].x, world.marks.trunk[0].y, 0, { yaw: -PI / 2, solid: [24, 12, 12] });\n    items = [];\n    const item = (mark, id, n, kind, o = {}) => (world.marks[mark] || []).forEach((m, i) => {\n      const key = mark + i; if (flags.taken.includes(key)) return;\n      items.push(world.thing(kind, m.x, m.y, m.z, Object.assign({ data: { key, item: id, n } }, o)));\n    });\n    item('herbG', 'herbG', 1, 'herb'); item('herbR', 'herbR', 1, 'herb', { color: '#c04040' }); item('ammo', 'ammo', 10, 'ammo'); item('crank', 'crank', 1, 'crank', { yaw: .6 });\n    item('ironkey', 'ironkey', 1, 'key', { color: KEY_LOOK.ironkey, spin: .3, bob: 1, z: 3 }); item('brasskey', 'brasskey', 1, 'key', { color: KEY_LOOK.brasskey, spin: .3, bob: 1, z: 3 });\n    enemies = [];\n    const spawn = (type, m, i) => {\n      const id = type + i; if (flags.dead.includes(id)) return; const k = KIND[type];\n      const e = type === 'dog' ? world.mob({ x: m.x, y: m.y, r: k.r, half: 0, mass: 1.2, visible: false, pose: false })\n        : world.mob({ x: m.x, y: m.y, r: k.r, half: k.half, mass: type === 'boss' ? 8 : 1.4, rig: type === 'boss' ? new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.8, build: 'bulky', weapon: null, hunch: .35, lean: .15, hair: 'long', sleeves: 'long', colors: BOSS_COLORS, eyeGlow: '#ff3a2a', speedRef: 40 })\n          : new E.Humanoid({ weapon: null, hunch: .3 + rnd() * .2, lean: .12, stride: 5, speedRef: 30, colors: ZOMBIE_COLORS[(rnd() * ZOMBIE_COLORS.length) | 0], eyeGlow: '#d8e0a0' }) });\n      Object.assign(e, { id, type, k, hp: k.hp, max: k.hp, room: roomAt(m.x, m.y), state: 'idle', t: rnd() * 2, stun: 0, speed: k.speed[0] + rnd() * (k.speed[1] - k.speed[0]), facing: rnd() * TAU, head: k.head, phase: rnd() * TAU, px: m.x, py: m.y, moan: 2 + rnd() * 6, atk: null });\n      enemies.push(e);\n    };\n    for (const t of ['zombie', 'dog', 'boss']) (world.marks[t] || []).forEach((m, i) => spawn(t, m, i));\n    shots.length = 0; mode = 'play'; menu = null; msg = null; ended = 0; song = null;\n    world.camera.set('view'); world.camera.set('zones'); world.camera.follow(hero);\n  }\n  const say = (text, t = 2.6) => { msg = { text, t }; };\n  const alive = () => enemies.filter(e => e.alive && e.hp > 0);\n  const awake = () => alive().filter(e => e.room === H.room);\n\n  /* ---- THE HERO: the controls (ctl: move, the buttons this step), then what it does ---- */\n  function heroStep(dt, ctl) {\n    const h = hero, S = H;\n    S.cool -= dt; S.fireT -= dt; S.hurtT -= dt; S.inv -= dt; h.flash -= dt;\n    S.room = roomAt(h.x, h.y) || S.room;\n    if (S.dead) { S.deadT += dt; h.vx = h.vy = 0; h.anim = { pose: 'die' }; return; }\n    if (S.grabbed) {   // held by the dead: tap the button to shake free; a bite halfway\n      const z = S.grabbed; S.grabT -= dt * (ctl.pressed('act') ? 6 : 1); h.vx = h.vy = 0; h.facing = Math.atan2(z.y - h.y, z.x - h.x);\n      if (!z.bit && S.grabT < .55) { z.bit = true; hurtHero(z.type === 'boss' ? 30 : 16, h.facing + PI, true); A.sfx('bite'); }\n      if (S.grabT <= 0 || !z.alive) { S.grabbed = null; const a = Math.atan2(h.y - z.y, h.x - z.x); h.push(Math.cos(a) * 140, Math.sin(a) * 140); z.push(-Math.cos(a) * 90, -Math.sin(a) * 90); z.state = 'recoil'; z.t = 1; }\n      h.anim = { hurt: true, expr: 'wince', point: false };\n      return;\n    }\n    if (S.crankT > 0) {   // turning the crank: the grille rises\n      S.crankT -= dt; socket.turn = (socket.turn || 0) + dt * 6; gate.open = clamp(1 - S.crankT / 2.2, 0, 1); h.vx = h.vy = 0; h.anim = { pose: 'cast' };\n      if (S.crankT <= 0) { world.setSolid(gate, false); flags.crank = true; say('The grille rose. Something gleams behind it.'); A.sfx('secret'); }\n      return;\n    }\n    if (S.hurtT > 0) { h.vx = approach(h.vx, 0, 400 * dt); h.vy = approach(h.vy, 0, 400 * dt); h.anim = { hurt: true, expr: 'wince' }; return; }\n    // aim: held, it stands still and locks on what is in front; up and down aim high and low, left and right pick another\n    const wasAim = S.aim; S.aim = ctl.down('aim') && S.reloadT <= 0;\n    const cam = world.camera, targets = awake();\n    if (S.aim && !wasAim) { S.aimLv = 0; const t = cam.lock(h, targets); if (t && t.type === 'dog') S.aimLv = -1; }\n    if (!S.aim && wasAim) cam.unlock();\n    if (S.reloadT > 0) { S.reloadT -= dt; if (S.reloadT <= 0) { const n = Math.min(CLIP - S.clip, inv.count('ammo')); inv.remove('ammo', n); S.clip += n; } }\n    if (S.aim) {\n      h.vx = approach(h.vx, 0, 600 * dt); h.vy = approach(h.vy, 0, 600 * dt);\n      if (ctl.pressed('up')) S.aimLv = Math.min(1, S.aimLv + 1); if (ctl.pressed('down')) S.aimLv = Math.max(-1, S.aimLv - 1);\n      const L = cam.lockOn;\n      if (L) { if (ctl.pressed('left')) cam.cycle(targets, -1); if (ctl.pressed('right')) cam.cycle(targets, 1); const T2 = cam.lockOn; h.facing = E.approachAng(h.facing, Math.atan2(T2.y - h.y, T2.x - h.x), dt * 9); }\n      else { if (!cam.lock(h, targets)) h.facing += (ctl.move[0] ? Math.sign(ctl.move[0]) : 0) * 2.6 * dt; }\n      if (ctl.pressed('act') && S.fireT <= 0) { ctl.use('act'); S.gun ? fire() : slash(); }\n    } else {\n      // walk or run: the camera's way, or tank controls (Settings)\n      const mv = ctl.move, ml = Math.hypot(mv[0], mv[1]), sp = (ctl.down('run') ? RUN : WALK) * (S.hp <= 33 ? .7 : 1), acc = 500 * dt;\n      h.vx = approach(h.vx, mv[0] * sp, acc); h.vy = approach(h.vy, mv[1] * sp, acc);\n      if (ml > .1 && !ctl.tank) h.facing = E.approachAng(h.facing, Math.atan2(mv[1], mv[0]), dt * 9);\n      if (ctl.pressed('swap')) { ctl.use('swap'); S.gun = !S.gun; h.rig.o.weapon = S.gun ? 'gun' : 'sword'; h.rig.o.bladeLen = 5; A.sfx('select'); say(S.gun ? 'Handgun.' : 'Knife.', 1); }\n      if (ctl.pressed('act')) { ctl.use('act'); check(); }\n    }\n    if (S.knife) { S.knife.update(dt); if (S.knife.state && S.knife.phase === 'active') S.knife.hits(targets, e => Math.abs(e.z - h.z) < 24 && E.inArc(h, h.facing, e, 22 + e.k.r, .9), e => hurt(e, KNIFE_DMG, h.facing, 50)); if (!S.knife.busy) S.knife = null; }\n    h.anim = { point: S.aim && S.gun, aim: S.aim ? AIM_A[S.aimLv + 1] : 0, attack: S.knife && S.knife.state, hurt: false, crouch: S.aim && S.aimLv < 0 && !S.gun, expr: S.hp <= 33 ? 'wince' : null };\n  }\n  /** the handgun: a shot along the aim (world.ray), the first body it meets hurt; a high shot at a head hurts more */\n  function fire() {\n    const h = hero, S = H;\n    if (S.clip <= 0) { if (inv.count('ammo') > 0) { S.reloadT = 1.1; S.aim = false; world.camera.unlock(); A.sfx('reload'); } else { A.sfx('dry'); say('Out of bullets.', 1.2); } S.fireT = .4; return; }\n    S.clip--; S.fireT = .42; S.shots++; A.sfx('gun'); game.shake(1.5);\n    const a = h.facing, va = AIM_A[S.aimLv + 1], ca = Math.cos(va), x = h.x + Math.cos(a) * 7, y = h.y + Math.sin(a) * 7, z = h.z + 19;\n    const hit = world.ray(x, y, z, Math.cos(a) * ca, Math.sin(a) * ca, Math.sin(va), 300, { skip: h });\n    shots.push({ x, y, z, x1: hit ? hit.x : x + Math.cos(a) * ca * 300, y1: hit ? hit.y : y + Math.sin(a) * ca * 300, z1: hit ? hit.z : z + Math.sin(va) * 300, t: .06 });\n    muzzle.x = x; muzzle.y = y; muzzle.z = z; muzzle.power = 26; muzzle.on = true; P.sparks(x, y, z, 3, a, { color: '#ffe0a0' });\n    if (!hit) return;\n    const e = hit.actor && enemies.includes(hit.actor) ? hit.actor : null;\n    if (e && e.alive) { const head = e.type !== 'dog' && hit.z > e.z + e.head * .8; hurt(e, head ? HEAD_DMG : GUN_DMG, a, e.type === 'boss' ? 20 : 70); if (head) P.bits(hit.x, hit.y, hit.z, 6, ['#6a1a1a', '#9a2a2a', '#c8b0a0']); }\n    else { P.sparks(hit.x, hit.y, hit.z, 5, Math.atan2(hit.ny, hit.nx)); P.dust(hit.x, hit.y, hit.z, 2); }\n  }\n  function slash() { H.knife = new E.Attack('slash', { reach: 5 }); H.knife.start(); H.fireT = .45; A.sfx('stab'); }\n  function hurtHero(dmg, ang, held = false) {\n    const h = hero, S = H; if (S.dead || (S.inv > 0 && !held)) return false;\n    S.hp -= dmg; S.inv = .6; h.flash = .08; if (!held) { S.hurtT = .35; h.push(Math.cos(ang) * 110, Math.sin(ang) * 110); }\n    game.shake(3); game.flash('#7a0000', .12, .35); A.sfx('hurt'); P.bits(h.x, h.y, h.z + 16, 6, ['#7a1010', '#a02020']);\n    world.camera.unlock(); S.aim = false;\n    if (S.hp <= 0) { S.hp = 0; S.dead = true; S.deadT = 0; S.grabbed = null; A.music(null); A.sfx('die'); }\n    return true;\n  }\n  function hurt(e, dmg, ang, kb) {\n    e.hp -= dmg; e.flash = .06; e.stun = e.type === 'boss' ? (e.hp % 60 < dmg ? .7 : 0) : .35; e.push(Math.cos(ang) * kb, Math.sin(ang) * kb);\n    if (e.state === 'lunge' || e.state === 'pounce') e.state = 'chase';\n    P.bits(e.x, e.y, e.z + e.head * .6, 4, ['#5a1414', '#8a2020']); A.sfx('hit');\n    if (e.hp > 0) return;\n    e.alive = false; flags.dead.push(e.id); e.setSolid(false); e.deadT = 0; A.sfx(e.type === 'dog' ? 'bark' : 'moan');\n    if (world.camera.lockOn === e) world.camera.unlock();\n    if (e.type === 'boss') { flags.boss = true; doors.exit.locked = null; game.flash('#ffffff', .3, .5); A.sfx('roar'); say('It is over. The way out is open.', 4); }\n  }\n  /** J in front of something: a door, a thing to take, the item box, the typewriter, the socket */\n  function check() {\n    const t = world.reach(hero, 16); if (!t) return;\n    const d = t.data || {};\n    if (t.kind === 'door' && d.id === 'gate') { say(flags.crank ? 'The grille is up.' : 'An iron grille. A key gleams behind it, out of reach.'); return; }\n    if (t.kind === 'door') {\n      if (d.id === 'exit') { if (t.locked) { say('Sealed with heavy chains. Something holds them from the far side.'); return; } win(); return; }\n      if (t.locked) {\n        const was = t.locked, r = world.unlock(t, inv);\n        if (r === 'locked') { say('It is locked. ' + (was === 'ironkey' ? 'An iron lock.' : 'A brass lock.')); A.sfx('bump'); return; }\n        flags.open.push(d.id); say('You used the ' + rpg.items[was].name.toUpperCase() + '.'); A.sfx('key'); return;\n      }\n      if (world.through(t, hero, { then: () => { autosave(); } })) A.sfx('door');\n      return;\n    }\n    if (d.item) {\n      if (!inv.add(d.item, d.n)) { say('No room. Leave something in the item box.'); A.sfx('bump'); return; }\n      flags.taken.push(d.key); world.remove(t); items.splice(items.indexOf(t), 1); A.sfx(d.item.endsWith('key') ? 'key' : 'pickup');\n      say('Took the ' + rpg.items[d.item].name.toUpperCase() + (d.n > 1 ? ' x' + d.n : '') + '.'); return;\n    }\n    if (t.kind === 'trunk') { openBox(); return; }\n    if (t.kind === 'typewriter') { saveGame(); return; }\n    if (t === socket) {\n      if (flags.crank) { say('The crank is fixed in place.'); return; }\n      if (!inv.has('crank')) { say('A mechanism with a square socket. A crank would fit it.'); return; }\n      inv.remove('crank'); socket.on = true; H.crankT = 2.2; A.sfx('crank'); return;\n    }\n  }\n\n  /* ---- THE DEAD, THE DOGS, WHAT WAITS: each wakes when you are in its room ---- */\n  const _d = [0, 0];\n  function towards(e, out) {   // straight at the hero when it sees it, else down the flow field (round the furniture)\n    const dx = hero.x - e.x, dy = hero.y - e.y, d = Math.hypot(dx, dy) || 1;\n    if (d < 60 || world.clear(e.x, e.y, e.z + 10, hero.x, hero.y, hero.z + 10)) { out[0] = dx / d; out[1] = dy / d; return out; }\n    if (flow.dir(e.x, e.y, out)) return out; out[0] = dx / d; out[1] = dy / d; return out;\n  }\n  function zombie(e, dt) {\n    const h = hero, dx = h.x - e.x, dy = h.y - e.y, d = Math.hypot(dx, dy), toH = Math.atan2(dy, dx), boss = e.type === 'boss';\n    let mx = 0, my = 0, sp = e.speed * (boss && e.hp < e.max / 2 ? 1.35 : 1);\n    e.t -= dt; e.moan -= dt;\n    if (e.moan < 0 && !boss) { e.moan = 5 + rnd() * 6; A.sfx('moan'); }\n    if (e.stun > 0) e.state = e.state === 'grab' ? 'grab' : 'chase';\n    else if (e.state === 'idle') { if (H.room === e.room && !H.dead) e.state = 'chase'; }\n    else if (e.state === 'chase') {\n      towards(e, _d); mx = _d[0]; my = _d[1]; e.facing = E.approachAng(e.facing, Math.atan2(my, mx), dt * (boss ? 3 : 2));\n      if (H.room !== e.room) e.state = 'idle';\n      else if (boss && d > 70 && d < 170 && e.t < 0 && world.clear(e.x, e.y, e.z + 20, h.x, h.y, h.z + 10)) { e.state = 'wind'; e.t = .6; A.sfx('roar'); }\n      else if (d < (boss ? 30 : 14) && e.t < 0 && !H.dead && !H.grabbed) { e.state = 'lunge'; e.t = boss ? .55 : .5; if (boss) { e.atk = new E.Attack('haymaker', { reach: 9, hold: .2 }); e.atk.start(); } }\n    }\n    else if (e.state === 'lunge') {   // arms out, a lean, then the grab (the boss: a swing)\n      e.facing = E.approachAng(e.facing, toH, dt * 3); if (!boss) { mx = Math.cos(e.facing) * .6; my = Math.sin(e.facing) * .6; }\n      if (e.atk) e.atk.update(dt);\n      if (e.t <= 0) {\n        const reach = boss ? 34 : 12, near = d < reach + 4 && Math.abs(h.z - e.z) < 12 && Math.abs(E.angDiff(e.facing, toH)) < 1;\n        if (near && !H.dead && !H.grabbed && H.crankT <= 0 && !world.passing) { if (boss) { hurtHero(26, toH); h.push(Math.cos(toH) * 120, Math.sin(toH) * 120); } else { H.grabbed = e; H.grabT = 1.25; e.bit = false; e.state = 'grab'; } }\n        if (e.state === 'lunge') { e.state = 'recoil'; e.t = boss ? .8 : .9; }\n      }\n    }\n    else if (e.state === 'grab') { e.facing = toH; if (H.grabbed !== e) { e.state = 'recoil'; e.t = 1; } }\n    else if (e.state === 'wind') { e.facing = E.approachAng(e.facing, toH, dt * 4); if (e.t <= 0) { e.state = 'rush'; e.t = .7; } }\n    else if (e.state === 'rush') {   // the boss's charge: straight on, a blow to whatever is in the way\n      mx = Math.cos(e.facing); my = Math.sin(e.facing); sp = 150;\n      if (d < 22 && !H.dead && !world.passing) { hurtHero(30, e.facing); h.push(Math.cos(e.facing) * 160, Math.sin(e.facing) * 160); e.t = 0; }\n      if (e.t <= 0) { e.state = 'recoil'; e.t = 1; }\n    }\n    else if (e.state === 'recoil') { if (e.t <= 0) { e.state = 'chase'; e.t = boss ? 2 + rnd() * 2 : .4 + rnd() * .6; e.atk = null; } }\n    if (e.atk && !e.atk.busy) e.atk = null;\n    const acc = (e.stun > 0 ? 200 : 260) * dt;\n    e.vx = approach(e.vx, e.stun > 0 ? 0 : mx * sp, acc); e.vy = approach(e.vy, e.stun > 0 ? 0 : my * sp, acc);\n    e.stun -= dt; e.flash -= dt;\n    e.anim = { pose: e.state === 'chase' || e.state === 'lunge' || e.state === 'grab' ? (boss ? null : 'cast') : null, hurt: e.stun > 0, attack: e.atk && e.atk.state, expr: 'angry', dash: e.state === 'rush' };\n  }\n  function dog(e, dt) {\n    const h = hero, dx = h.x - e.x, dy = h.y - e.y, d = Math.hypot(dx, dy) || 1, toH = Math.atan2(dy, dx);\n    e.t -= dt; e.phase += dt * Math.hypot(e.vx, e.vy) * .16; e.px = e.x; e.py = e.y;\n    let mx = 0, my = 0;\n    if (e.state === 'idle') { if (H.room === e.room && !H.dead) { e.state = 'run'; A.sfx('bark'); } }\n    else if (e.state === 'run') {   // in, weaving\n      towards(e, _d); const w = Math.sin(world.time * 3 + e.phase) * .5; mx = _d[0] - _d[1] * w; my = _d[1] + _d[0] * w; e.facing = E.approachAng(e.facing, Math.atan2(my, mx), dt * 8);\n      if (H.room !== e.room) e.state = 'idle';\n      else if (d < 38 && e.grounded && e.t < 0 && !world.passing) { e.state = 'pounce'; e.t = .5; e.vz = 120; e.vx = dx / d * (d + 4) / .5; e.vy = dy / d * (d + 4) / .5; e.facing = toH; A.sfx('bark'); }\n    }\n    else if (e.state === 'pounce') {\n      if (d < e.r + 7 && Math.abs(h.z - e.z) < 18 && !H.dead) { hurtHero(10, toH); e.state = 'off'; e.t = .9; e.vx = -dx / d * 70; e.vy = -dy / d * 70; A.sfx('bite'); }\n      else if (e.t < .1 && e.grounded) { e.state = 'off'; e.t = .6; }\n    }\n    else if (e.state === 'off') { mx = -dx / d; my = -dy / d; const s = Math.sign(Math.sin(e.phase)) || 1; mx -= my * s; my += mx * s; e.facing = E.approachAng(e.facing, Math.atan2(my, mx), dt * 6); if (e.t <= 0) { e.state = 'run'; e.t = .3 + rnd() * .5; } }\n    if (e.state !== 'pounce') { const acc = (e.stun > 0 ? 300 : 700) * dt; e.vx = approach(e.vx, e.stun > 0 ? 0 : mx * e.speed, acc); e.vy = approach(e.vy, e.stun > 0 ? 0 : my * e.speed, acc); }\n    e.stun -= dt; e.flash -= dt;\n  }\n\n  /* ---- ONE STEP: the rules, then the world ---- */\n  function step(dt, ctl) {\n    if (msg && (msg.t -= dt) <= 0) msg = null;\n    if (world.passing) { world.step(dt); return; }   // (a door between rooms: everything waits)\n    flow.to(hero.x, hero.y);\n    heroStep(dt, ctl);\n    for (const e of enemies) {\n      if (!e.alive) { e.deadT += dt; e.vx = approach(e.vx, 0, 300 * dt); e.vy = approach(e.vy, 0, 300 * dt); e.anim = { pose: 'die' }; continue; }\n      if (e.type === 'dog') dog(e, dt); else zombie(e, dt);\n    }\n    for (let i = shots.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) if ((shots[i].t -= dt) <= 0) shots.splice(i, 1);\n    if (muzzle.on && (muzzle.power -= 400 * dt) <= 0) muzzle.on = false;\n    if (H.dead && H.deadT > 2.4 && !ended) { ended = 1; game.go('over', { from: 'horror', world, lines: ['YOU DIED', flags.taken.length + ' THINGS FOUND   ' + flags.dead.length + ' OF ' + enemies.length + ' PUT DOWN'] }); }\n    world.step(dt);\n  }\n  function win() {\n    if (ended) return; ended = 1; if (scripted) return; A.music('victory');\n    game.after(1.2, () => game.go('over', { from: 'horror', world, won: true, title: 'ESCAPED', lines: ['THE WING IS QUIET', flags.dead.length + ' PUT DOWN   ' + H.shots + ' SHOTS FIRED'] }));\n  }\n  /* ---- SAVES: the typewriter writes to the 2D engine's slots (game.saves); a door passed writes the autosave ---- */\n  const state = () => ({ data: { at: [hero.x, hero.y, hero.facing], hp: H.hp, clip: H.clip, gun: H.gun, inv: inv.list().map(s => [s.id, s.n]), box: box.list().map(s => [s.id, s.n]), flags }, place: (H.room || 'foyer').toUpperCase(), level: null });\n  function saveGame() { game.saves.write = state; game.saves.read = s => reset(1, s.data); if (!game.saves.show('save')) game.saves.save(0); }\n  function autosave() { if (!H.dead && !scripted) { game.saves.write = state; game.saves.autosave(); } }   // (not in the proof or the bot)\n\n  /* ---- THE ITEMS SCREEN (I) and THE ITEM BOX: the world stands still while they are open ---- */\n  const status = () => H.hp > 66 ? ['FINE', '#5ad070'] : H.hp > 33 ? ['CAUTION', '#e8c040'] : ['DANGER', '#e8483a'];\n  function openItems() { mode = 'items'; menu = { i: 0, pick: null, sub: null }; A.sfx('select'); world.camera.unlock(); H.aim = false; }\n  function openBox() { mode = 'box'; menu = { side: 0, i: 0 }; A.sfx('door'); }\n  function useItem(id) {\n    const it = rpg.items[id];\n    if (it.heal) { if (H.hp >= HP) { say('You are fine.'); return; } inv.remove(id); H.hp = Math.min(HP, H.hp + it.heal); A.sfx('heal'); say('You feel better.'); return; }\n    say(it.info);\n  }\n  function itemsStep() {\n    const I = game.input, M = menu, list = inv.list(), n = 6;\n    if (I.pressed('items') || I.pressed('cancel')) { I.consumeAll(); if (M.sub) M.sub = null; else { mode = 'play'; menu = null; } return; }\n    if (M.sub) {   // USE, MIX, INFO\n      if (I.pressed('up')) M.sub.i = (M.sub.i + 2) % 3; if (I.pressed('down')) M.sub.i = (M.sub.i + 1) % 3;\n      if (I.pressed('act') || I.pressed('confirm')) { I.consumeAll(); const s = list[M.i], c = M.sub.i; M.sub = null; if (!s) return; if (c === 0) useItem(s.id); else if (c === 1) { M.pick = M.i; say('Mix it with what?', 2); } else say(s.item.info); A.sfx('confirm'); }\n      return;\n    }\n    if (I.pressed('left')) M.i = (M.i + n - 1) % n; if (I.pressed('right')) M.i = (M.i + 1) % n;\n    if (I.pressed('up') || I.pressed('down')) M.i = (M.i + 3) % n;\n    if (I.pressed('act') || I.pressed('confirm')) {\n      I.consumeAll(); const s = list[M.i]; if (!s) return;\n      if (M.pick !== null) { const a = list[M.pick], r = a && M.pick !== M.i && MIX[a.id + '+' + s.id]; M.pick = null; if (!r) { say('They do not mix.'); A.sfx('bump'); return; } inv.remove(a.id); inv.remove(s.id); inv.add(r); A.sfx('heal'); say('Mixed: ' + rpg.items[r].name + '.'); return; }\n      M.sub = { i: 0 }; A.sfx('select');\n    }\n  }\n  function boxStep() {\n    const I = game.input, M = menu, lists = [inv.list(), box.list()];\n    if (I.pressed('cancel') || I.pressed('items')) { I.consumeAll(); mode = 'play'; menu = null; A.sfx('door'); return; }\n    if (I.pressed('left') || I.pressed('right')) { M.side ^= 1; M.i = 0; A.sfx('select'); }\n    const L = lists[M.side], cap = M.side ? Math.max(1, L.length) : 6;\n    if (I.pressed('up')) M.i = (M.i + cap - 1) % cap; if (I.pressed('down')) M.i = (M.i + 1) % cap;\n    if (I.pressed('act') || I.pressed('confirm')) {\n      I.consumeAll(); const s = L[M.i]; if (!s) return;\n      const from = M.side ? box : inv, to = M.side ? inv : box;\n      if (!to.add(s.id, s.n)) { say('No room.'); A.sfx('bump'); return; }\n      from.remove(s.id, s.n); A.sfx('pickup'); M.i = Math.max(0, Math.min(M.i, lists[M.side].length - 2));\n    }\n  }\n\n  /* ---- THE DOGS DRAWN WITH THE PEN: a body, a head, four legs at a gallop (part way between steps) ---- */\n  function drawDog(e) {\n    const k = game.paused ? 1 : clamp(game.alpha, 0, 1), x = lerp(e.px, e.x, k), y = lerp(e.py, e.y, k), z = e.z, pen = world.pen, run = Math.min(1, Math.hypot(e.vx, e.vy) / 60), ph = e.phase, dead = !e.alive;\n    const c = '#4a3c36', dk = '#2e2622', raw = '#8a3a34';\n    pen.at(x, y, z + (dead ? -3 : 0), e.facing); if (e.flash > 0) pen.flash = true;\n    const bob = dead ? 0 : Math.abs(Math.sin(ph)) * 1.2 * run, tilt = dead ? 0 : Math.sin(ph) * .06 * run;\n    pen.ball(0, 0, 9 + bob, 7.2, 3.2, 3.6, c).ball(3.2, 0, 10 + bob, 3.2, 3.4, 3.6, dk).ball(-1, 1.8, 9.6 + bob, 2.2, 1.2, 1.6, raw);\n    const hz = 12.5 + bob + (dead ? -6 : 0) - tilt * 10;\n    pen.ball(7.6, 0, hz, 2.8, 2.4, 2.4, c).cone(9.4, 0, hz - .6, 13, 0, hz - 1.4, 1.5, dk).cone(7, -1.4, hz + 1.4, 6.4, -1.8, hz + 4.4, .9, dk).cone(7, 1.4, hz + 1.4, 6.4, 1.8, hz + 4.4, .9, dk);\n    pen.glow(9.2, -1.1, hz + .8, .45, '#ff3a2a').glow(9.2, 1.1, hz + .8, .45, '#ff3a2a');\n    pen.tube(-6.6, 0, 10 + bob, -10, 0, 12 + bob + Math.sin(ph * 2) * 1.5, .8, dk);\n    for (const [lx, ly, o] of [[4.6, -2, 0], [4.6, 2, PI], [-4.6, -2, PI * .6], [-4.6, 2, PI * 1.6]]) {\n      const s = dead ? .4 : Math.sin(ph + o), fx = lx + s * 3.4 * run, fz = dead ? 2 : Math.max(0, Math.cos(ph + o)) * 2.4 * run;\n      pen.tube(lx, ly, 8 + bob, (lx + fx) / 2 + 1, ly, 4 + fz, 1.1, c).tube((lx + fx) / 2 + 1, ly, 4 + fz, fx, ly, fz + .4, .8, dk);\n    }\n    pen.flash = false; pen.at();\n  }\n\n  /* ---- THE HUD: little in play (as in the games it follows): a message, the gun when aiming, the status in a corner;\n   * the items screen and the item box over the picture ---- */\n  function ecg(g, x, y, w, color, t) {   // a heartbeat line, faster as it gets worse\n    const rate = H.hp > 66 ? 1.2 : H.hp > 33 ? 1.8 : 2.6;\n    for (let i = 0; i < w; i++) { const u = (i / w + t * rate * .5) % 1, v = u > .42 && u < .46 ? -6 : u > .46 && u < .5 ? 5 : u > .5 && u < .53 ? -2 : 0; E.px.rect(g, x + i, y + v, 1, 1, color); }\n  }\n  function hud(g, r) {\n    const [word, col] = status();\n    if (mode === 'play') {\n      E.font.text(g, word, 6, 6, col, { outline: '#000', font: 'tiny' }); ecg(g, 6, 18, 40, col, game.real);\n      if (H.aim) E.font.text(g, (H.gun ? 'HANDGUN ' + H.clip + ' / ' + inv.count('ammo') : 'KNIFE') + (H.aimLv ? H.aimLv > 0 ? '  HIGH' : '  LOW' : ''), r.W - 6, 6, '#e8e0d0', { align: 'right', outline: '#000', font: 'tiny' });\n      if (H.reloadT > 0) E.font.text(g, 'RELOADING', r.W - 6, 6, '#e8c040', { align: 'right', outline: '#000', font: 'tiny' });\n      if (H.grabbed) E.font.text(g, (touch() ? 'TAP ACT' : 'TAP ' + game.input.label('act')) + ' TO SHAKE FREE', r.W / 2, r.H / 2 + 30, '#ff8a7a', { align: 'center', outline: '#000' });\n    }\n    // (the message: above the touch buttons on a phone)\n    if (msg) { const w = Math.min(r.W - 20, 300), ta = game.input.touchArea(), y = ta && ta.y0 < r.H - 24 ? Math.min(r.H - 46, ta.y0 - 28) : r.H - 46; E.ui.box(g, (r.W - w) / 2, y, w, 22, { bg: '#08060a', border: '#5a5060' }); E.font.text(g, msg.text, r.W / 2, y + 7, '#e8e0d0', { align: 'center', outline: false, font: msg.text.length * 6 > w - 12 ? 'tiny' : undefined }); }\n    if (mode === 'items') {\n      const M = menu, list = inv.list(), w = Math.min(r.W - 16, 330), x0 = (r.W - w) / 2, y0 = Math.max(8, r.H / 2 - 90);\n      g.save(); g.fillStyle = '#000'; g.globalAlpha = .7; g.fillRect(0, 0, r.bw, r.bh); g.restore(); g._c = null;\n      E.ui.box(g, x0, y0, w, 160, { bg: '#0c0a10', border: '#6a6070' });\n      E.font.text(g, 'CONDITION', x0 + 10, y0 + 8, '#a8a0b0', { font: 'tiny', outline: false }); E.font.text(g, word, x0 + 10, y0 + 20, col, { outline: false }); ecg(g, x0 + 10, y0 + 40, 90, col, game.real);\n      E.font.text(g, H.gun ? 'HANDGUN  ' + H.clip + ' / ' + inv.count('ammo') : 'KNIFE', x0 + 10, y0 + 54, '#e8e0d0', { font: 'tiny', outline: false });\n      for (let i = 0; i < 6; i++) {\n        const s = list[i], cx = x0 + w - 186 + (i % 3) * 60, cy = y0 + 10 + Math.floor(i / 3) * 52, sel = i === M.i, pk = M.pick === i;\n        E.ui.box(g, cx, cy, 54, 46, { bg: sel ? '#2a2234' : '#16121c', border: pk ? '#e8c040' : sel ? '#e8e0d0' : '#4a4250' });\n        if (s) { E.px.sprite(g, ICONS[s.id], cx + 17, cy + 7, { scale: 2 }); if (s.n > 1) E.font.text(g, String(s.n), cx + 50, cy + 34, '#e8e0d0', { align: 'right', font: 'tiny', outline: '#000' }); }\n      }\n      const s = list[M.i]; E.font.text(g, s ? s.item.name : '', x0 + 10, y0 + 120, '#ffe0a0', { outline: false }); E.font.text(g, s ? s.item.info : '', x0 + 10, y0 + 134, '#c8c0d0', { font: 'tiny', outline: false });\n      if (M.sub) { const sx = x0 + w - 186 + (M.i % 3) * 60 + 30, sy = y0 + 10 + Math.floor(M.i / 3) * 52 + 26; E.ui.box(g, sx, sy, 50, 40, { bg: '#08060a', border: '#e8e0d0' }); ['USE', 'MIX', 'INFO'].forEach((t, k) => E.font.text(g, (k === M.sub.i ? '▸' : ' ') + t, sx + 5, sy + 5 + k * 11, k === M.sub.i ? '#ffd36a' : '#e8e0d0', { font: 'tiny', outline: false })); }\n    }\n    if (mode === 'box') {\n      const M = menu, w = Math.min(r.W - 16, 330), x0 = (r.W - w) / 2, y0 = Math.max(8, r.H / 2 - 90), L = [inv.list(), box.list()];\n      g.save(); g.fillStyle = '#000'; g.globalAlpha = .7; g.fillRect(0, 0, r.bw, r.bh); g.restore(); g._c = null;\n      ['YOURS', 'THE ITEM BOX'].forEach((t, side) => {\n        const x = x0 + side * (w / 2 + 2), ww = w / 2 - 2; E.ui.box(g, x, y0, ww, 170, { bg: '#0c0a10', border: M.side === side ? '#e8e0d0' : '#4a4250' });\n        E.font.text(g, t, x + 8, y0 + 7, '#a8a0b0', { font: 'tiny', outline: false });\n        const rows = side ? Math.max(1, L[1].length) : 6;\n        for (let i = 0; i < Math.min(rows, 12); i++) { const s = L[side][i], sel = M.side === side && M.i === i; E.font.text(g, (sel ? '▸ ' : '  ') + (s ? s.item.name + (s.n > 1 ? ' x' + s.n : '') : '-'), x + 6, y0 + 20 + i * 12, sel ? '#ffd36a' : '#e8e0d0', { font: 'tiny', outline: false }); }\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\n  /* ---- the controls this step: the stick by the player's setting (camera.steer), the buttons ---- */\n  const KEYS = { up: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'Pad12'], down: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'Pad13'], left: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'Pad14'], right: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'Pad15'],\n    act: ['KeyJ', 'Space', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0'], aim: ['KeyK', 'Mouse2', 'Pad6', 'Pad4'], run: ['ShiftLeft', 'ShiftRight', 'Pad1'], swap: ['KeyQ', 'Pad3'], items: ['KeyI', 'Tab', 'Pad2'],\n    start: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Pad9'], pause: ['Escape', 'KeyP', 'Pad9'], confirm: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Pad0'], cancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'Pad1'] };\n  const TOUCH = ['items', 'run', 'aim', 'act'], TOUCH_LABELS = { items: 'ITEMS', run: 'RUN', aim: 'AIM', act: 'ACT' };\n  const ctl = { move: [0, 0], tank: false, down: a => game.input.down(a), pressed: a => game.input.pressed(a), use: a => game.input.consume(a) };\n  function controls(dt) { ctl.tank = world.camera.tank; world.camera.steer(hero, game.input.move(), H.aim || H.grabbed || H.dead ? 0 : dt, ctl.move); if (H.aim) ctl.move[0] = game.input.move()[0]; return ctl; }\n\n  /** the proof: a scripted walk from the foyer, the stick held up across a cut (it keeps its way, as a player's does),\n   *  to the west door (the door between rooms), then aim at the dead in the hall (the lock) and shoot; n steps of 1/120\n   *  s. The world's hash with the camera's cuts and zone and the lock's target: the same on WebGPU, WebGL 2 and run\n   *  again */\n  function run(n = 600) {\n    reset(3); scripted = true; const keys = new Set(), c = { move: [0, 0], tank: false, down: a => keys.has(a), pressed: a => keys.has('tap:' + a), use() {} }, door = doors.west;\n    const toward = (x, y) => { const dx = x - hero.x, dy = y - hero.y, d = Math.hypot(dx, dy); c.move[0] = d > 3 ? dx / d : 0; c.move[1] = d > 3 ? dy / d : 0; return d; };\n    let phase = 0;\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n      keys.clear(); keys.add('run'); c.move[0] = c.move[1] = 0;\n      if (phase === 0) { world.camera.steer(hero, [0, -1], 1 / 120, c.move, { tank: false }); if (world.camera.cuts) phase = 1; }   // up, held across the foyer's cut\n      else if (phase === 1) { if (toward(door.x + 15, door.y) < 4) { phase = 2; hero.facing = PI; } }\n      else if (phase === 2) { keys.add('tap:act'); phase = 3; }\n      else if (phase === 3) { if (!world.passing && H.room === 'west') phase = 4; }\n      else { keys.add('aim'); if (i % 40 === 0) keys.add('tap:act'); }\n      step(1 / 120, c);\n    }\n    scripted = false; const L = world.camera.lockOn, Z = world.camera.zone;\n    return world.hash([H.hp, H.clip, world.camera.cuts, ZONES.indexOf(Z), L ? enemies.indexOf(L) : -1, phase, enemies.filter(e => !e.alive).length]);\n  }\n\n  /** the bot: plays the wing through to what waits in the gallery and fights it, by the game's own rules (each step a\n   *  stick and buttons, as a player gives them): walk the flow field to each thing it needs, opening (and unlocking)\n   *  the doors in its way, fight what comes (aim, shoot, low at dogs; the knife when the gun is dry), heal, crank the\n   *  grille. Returns what it did: { reached, boss, won, rooms, took, opened, killed, shots, hp, steps, errors } */\n  function bot(max = 120 * 60 * 12) {\n    reset(5); scripted = true; const seen = new Set(['foyer']), keys = new Set(), c = { move: [0, 0], tank: false, down: a => keys.has(a), pressed: a => keys.has('tap:' + a), use: a => keys.delete('tap:' + a) };\n    const GOALS = [['take', 'herbG1'], ['take', 'crank0'], ['take', 'ammo3'], ['take', 'ironkey0'], ['take', 'herbG0'], ['take', 'ammo1'], ['take', 'ammo2'], ['take', 'herbG2'],\n      ['take', 'ammo0'], ['use', 'socket'], ['take', 'brasskey0'], ['take', 'herbR0'], ['fight', 'boss'], ['door', 'exit']];\n    let g = 0, steps = 0, errors = 0, stuck = 0, lastD = 1e9, saved = false; const f = world.flow(), dt = 1 / 120;\n    const where = () => { const [k, id] = GOALS[g] || []; if (k === 'door') return doors[id]; if (k === 'take') return items.find(t => t.data.key === id); if (k === 'use') return flags.crank ? null : socket; if (k === 'fight') return enemies.find(e => e.type === 'boss' && e.alive); return null; };\n    const face = a => { hero.facing = E.approachAng(hero.facing, a, dt * 12); return Math.abs(E.angDiff(hero.facing, a)) < .1; };\n    try {\n      for (; steps < max && g < GOALS.length && !ended && !H.dead; steps++) {\n        keys.clear(); c.move[0] = c.move[1] = 0;\n        if (world.passing || H.crankT > 0) { step(dt, c); continue; }\n        if (H.grabbed) { if (steps % 6 === 0) keys.add('tap:act'); step(dt, c); continue; }\n        if (H.hp < 50) { const herb = inv.list().find(s => rpg.items[s.id].heal); if (herb) useItem(herb.id); }\n        seen.add(H.room);\n        // a threat in sight: aim (low at a dog), shoot; the knife up close when the gun is dry\n        const foes = awake().filter(e => Math.hypot(e.x - hero.x, e.y - hero.y) < (e.type === 'boss' ? 200 : 120) && world.clear(hero.x, hero.y, hero.z + 16, e.x, e.y, e.z + 10));\n        if (foes.length) {\n          const dry = H.clip === 0 && !inv.count('ammo'); if (H.gun === dry) keys.add('tap:swap');\n          const L = world.camera.lockOn, d = L ? Math.hypot(L.x - hero.x, L.y - hero.y) : 0;\n          if (!H.gun && L && d > 18) { const a = Math.atan2(L.y - hero.y, L.x - hero.x); c.move[0] = Math.cos(a); c.move[1] = Math.sin(a); }\n          else { keys.add('aim'); if (L && L.type === 'dog' && H.aimLv > -1) keys.add('tap:down'); if (L && L.type !== 'dog' && H.aimLv < 0) keys.add('tap:up');\n            if (L && Math.abs(E.angDiff(hero.facing, Math.atan2(L.y - hero.y, L.x - hero.x))) < .12 && H.fireT <= 0) keys.add('tap:act'); }\n          step(dt, c); continue;\n        }\n        const goal = GOALS[g], tgt = where(); if (!tgt) { g++; continue; }\n        const d = Math.hypot(tgt.x - hero.x, tgt.y - hero.y);\n        // there: face it and check it (a door: open it; the exit: out)\n        if (goal[0] !== 'fight' && d < (goal[0] === 'door' ? 22 : 18)) {\n          if (face(Math.atan2(tgt.y - hero.y, tgt.x - hero.x))) { keys.add('tap:act'); step(dt, c); if (goal[0] !== 'door' && (!items.includes(tgt) || flags.crank || H.crankT > 0)) g++; } else step(dt, c);\n          if (inv.has('brasskey') && !saved) saved = game.saves.save(2, state());   // (a save on the way, loaded back at the end)\n          continue;\n        }\n        // on the way: the flow field; a closed door in the way is opened (unlocked first, with the key it takes)\n        f.to(tgt.x, tgt.y); const dir = f.dir(hero.x, hero.y, [0, 0]) || [(tgt.x - hero.x) / (d || 1), (tgt.y - hero.y) / (d || 1)];\n        const door = world.reach(hero, 10, ['door']);\n        if (door && door !== tgt && door !== gate && (door.x - hero.x) * dir[0] + (door.y - hero.y) * dir[1] > 0) { if (face(Math.atan2(door.y - hero.y, door.x - hero.x) + (door.yaw ? 0 : 0))) keys.add('tap:act'); step(dt, c); continue; }\n        c.move[0] = dir[0]; c.move[1] = dir[1]; keys.add('run');\n        stuck = d < lastD - .01 ? 0 : stuck + 1; lastD = d; if (stuck > 240) { c.move[0] = -dir[1]; c.move[1] = dir[0]; if (stuck > 330) stuck = 0; }\n        step(dt, c);\n      }\n    } catch (e) { errors++; console.error(e); }\n    scripted = false; const boss = enemies.find(e => e.type === 'boss');\n    const r = { reached: seen.has('gallery'), boss: !!boss && !boss.alive, won: ended === 1 && !H.dead, dead: H.dead, rooms: [...seen], took: flags.taken.length, opened: flags.open.slice(), killed: flags.dead.length, shots: H.shots, hp: H.hp, goal: g, of: GOALS.length, steps, errors, saved };\n    // the save made on the way, loaded back: the wing as it stood then (the crank turned, the brass key in hand, in the library)\n    game.saves.read = s => reset(1, s.data); const back = saved && game.saves.load(2);\n    if (back) r.loaded = { room: roomAt(hero.x, hero.y), crank: flags.crank, brass: inv.has('brasskey'), dead: flags.dead.length, gate: !gate.solid };\n    game.saves.erase(2); ended = 0; return r;\n  }\n\n  return {\n    view: 'iso', input: KEYS, pausable: true, touch: TOUCH, camera: { zoom: [.6, 2] },\n    enter() {\n      game.settings.define(W3.CONTROLS); reset(1); active = world; A.music(null); game.input.touchButtons(TOUCH, { labels: TOUCH_LABELS });\n      game.saves.write = state; game.saves.read = s => reset(1, s.data);\n      if (game.saves.any) { mode = 'intro'; menu = new E.Menu(game, ['CONTINUE', 'NEW GAME'], { y: 'center', onPick: i => { mode = 'play'; menu = null; if (i === 0) game.saves.load(game.saves.latest().slot); } }); }\n      say('The east and west wings. Find a way out.', 3.5);\n    },\n    update(dt) {\n      if (mode === 'intro') { menu.update(dt); world.step(0); return; }\n      if (mode === 'items') { itemsStep(); world.step(0); return; }\n      if (mode === 'box') { boxStep(); world.step(0); return; }\n      if (game.input.pressed('items') && !H.dead && !world.passing && !H.grabbed) { openItems(); return; }\n      step(dt, controls(dt));\n      const want = H.room === 'gallery' && enemies.some(e => e.type === 'boss' && e.alive) ? DREAD : H.room === 'foyer' ? SAFE : HALL;\n      if (want !== song && !ended && !H.dead) { song = want; A.music(want); }\n      const inp = game.input; inp.touchSet('act', H.aim ? 'FIRE' : null, true);\n    },\n    draw(r) {\n      world.draw(r);\n      r.overlay(g => hud(g, r));\n      if (mode === 'intro') menu.draw(r);\n    },\n    get world() { return world; }, get hero() { return hero; }, get state() { return H; }, get enemies() { return enemies; }, get inv() { return inv; }, get flags() { return flags; },\n    get mode() { return mode; }, reset, run, bot, ZONES, ROOMS\n  };\n})();\nscenes.horror = HORROR;\n","numLines":603,"startLine":1,"totalLines":603}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019sPnFS8fHmLPS4n8ouDH