{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VrGuCMDhQBboQQJihG5LFH","type":"tool_result","content":"5://   dist/my-3d2dge.html          readable engine + API card + every starter slice (the reference)\n6://   dist/my-3d2dge-compact.html  same, with the engine minified (fewer tokens)\n7://   dist/kits/my-3d2dge-<genre>.html  minified engine + API card + ONE slice: the smallest file to\n10://   dist/my-3d2dge.js / .min.js  the engine alone, for multi-file projects: the core and every module (engine/modules/) in\n12://   dist/my-3d2dge-3d.html       the 3D starter: the engine and the 3D engine (engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js: three.js r182 and\n14://                                the API card and every 3D slice (src/starter3d/)\n15://   dist/kits/my-3d2dge-3d-<genre>.html  the same with ONE 3D slice: a 3D genre kit\n16://   dist/my-3d2dge-3d.js         the 3D engine alone (an ES module), readable\n17://   dist/my-3d2dge-agent.js      the agent edition: the essential engine plus its manual in one readable file,\n18://                                for AI coding agents (source: engine/my-3d2dge-agent.js; test: node tools/agent-test.mjs)\n34:const ENGINE = 'engine/my-3d2dge.js';\n35:const STARTER = 'src/starter', STARTER3D = 'src/starter3d', ENGINE3D = 'engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js';\n36:const SLICES = { adventure: 'ADVENTURE (a top-down action adventure: a village, ruins and a shrine, a sword, a key and a great door, talk with portraits; Zelda and Secret of Mana)', platformer: 'PLATFORMER (a side-scr\n41:// shell, slice, sets, modules and, in 3D, the 3D engine), and what each of the core's statements needs. A part the kit\n71:// THE 3D DIET: the 3D engine's sections a 3D kit's game never calls, left out as the kit diet leaves out the core's\n72:// (tools/diet.mjs, reading the 3D engine as the ES module it is): what the kit calls is its shell, slice and modules\n73:const DIET3D = [\n82:const PARTS = partsOf(STARTER), PARTS3D = partsOf(STARTER3D);\n90:  ENGINE: '\\n       Every module follows it, each a script marked \"inlined from engine/modules/<name>.js\" that starts with its manual.',\n94:// a kit's line on its modules (the scripts marked \"inlined from engine/modules/...\", after the engine), when it has any\n95:const modLine = mods => mods.length ? '\\n       ' + wrapHead('Its modules follow it, each a script marked \"inlined from engine/modules/<name>.js\" that starts with its manual: ' + resolveModules(mods, MODS).map(m => m.\n98:  CONTENTS: 'a title menu plus the ' + SLICES[id] + ' slice.\\n       This is a genre kit: dist/my-3d2dge.html has every slice (my-3d2dge.vercel.app/dist/my-3d2dge.html), and the\\n       handoff package every kit reada\n101:// the 3D slices: their ids and what each is (the kit's header names it)\n102:const SLICES3D = { action: 'ACTION (a 3D arena: combos, dashes and waves, Zelda 64 and Diablo by way of the stress test)', platformer: 'PLATFORMER (a 3D course of islands, platforms and coins, Mario 64 and Spyro)', s\n103:const ALL3D = { EDITION: '3D edition', GAMES: 'the 3D starter games', ENGINE: '', CONTENTS: 'a title menu plus every 3D slice (' + Object.keys(SLICES3D).map(k => k.toUpperCase()).join(', ') + ').', LINKS: links(Objec\n104:const kit3d = (id, mods = []) => ({ EDITION: '3D ' + id + ' kit', GAMES: 'one 3D game to copy', ENGINE: modLine(mods), CONTENTS: 'a title menu plus the ' + SLICES3D[id] + ' slice.\\n       This is a 3D genre kit: dist\n111:  { template: 'src/arena.template.html', out: 'examples/arena.html', vars: { VIEW: 'iso', TITLE: 'Emberwell · my-3D2dge' } },\n116:  // every entry of the asset store (src/assets/sets/, inlined) and the core library, to browse, search and copy\n118:  // a Temporary prototype (src/labs.json): the 3D engine's vehicles two ways, side by side on one track\n120:  // one page that links to every lab, test page and demo, from the list in src/labs.json (my-3d2dge.vercel.app/labs)\n125:  { template: 'src/starter.template.html', out: 'dist/