{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015yJG2cPc3nhQKCrC7kU8qU","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# my-3D2dge guide for AI models\n7:## North star\n17:## The mental model\n29:## Remake workflow (port, remaster, reimagine, remix)\n44:## Visual craft: aim for PS1 / N64 era 2D, not NES\n64:## Animation: fluid, varied, readable\n72:## Hard rules\n82:## Standard features (built in: adjust them, don't rebuild them)\n120:## Frame order\n140:## Systems in more depth\n142:### Views and resolution\n150:### Scenes\n155:### Camera\n163:### Players (two to four on one machine)\n169:### Motion and timing (tweens, scripts, paths)\n178:### TileMap (ground-plane levels)\n190:### Heights: roofs, ledges, sight and reach\n222:### PlatformMap (side-scrolling levels)\n242:### Platformer (side-scroller controller)\n249:### Body (ground-plane physics)\n255:### Mover and actions (third-person ground controller)\n267:### Perception (sight, hearing, suspicion)\n273:### Attack (melee timing)\n280:### Bullets and patterns\n286:### Humanoid\n297:### Audio\n305:### Text and UI\n311:### Shell (an HTML interface: screens and HUD)\n319:### Lighting\n328:### Errors and warnings\n338:### Testing without a browser\n357:### The handoff package\n360:### Modules (general systems in files of their own)\n367:### Kits and the diet (which file for which game)\n374:### Recorded sessions (a bug from a phone, replayed exactly)\n402:## Genre recipes\n606:## Building a big game: lessons from Emberdeep\n631:## Where to find more: animation and examples\n648:## Performance\n656:## Checklist before handing a game back\n----\n2: * SLICE 3  SHOOTER  (Apex Legends' movement and gunplay, without the multiplayer; first or third person). A badlands\n8: * the drop point has a firing range. T switches first and third person.\n652:   * third person, the raiders and the range's dummies are all soldiers\n679:  /** two-bone IK: the joint between a (a hip, a shoulder) and the end b, bending toward hint; b pulled in if too far */\n842:  /** where the gun is: low and across the chest at a sprint, at the shoulder (the cheek on the stock down the sights),\n846:    let F = { o: add(add(add(N, fC, 3.1 * k), rtT, 3 * k), upC, -3 * k), f: aim.f, u: aim.u, r: aim.r };   // (the stock in the right shoulder's pocket)\n848:    if (b.lowB > .01) { const lo = turn(F, -.32 * b.lowB, .16 * b.lowB, .12 * b.lowB); lo.o = mixv(F.o, add(add(add(C, fC, 2.4 * k), rtT, 4.3 * k), upC, -1.8 * k), b.lowB); F = lo; }   // (the low ready: at the right\n849:    if (b.spB > .01) {   // a sprint at port arms: the rifle across the chest, muzzle up past the left shoulder, swinging with the stride\n1156:   * (first person at the eyes, third over the shoulder). All in the game's steps: a replay is exact\n1400:    if (I.pressed('view')) { I.use('view'); S.view = S.view === 'first' ? 'third' : 'first'; game.note(S.view === 'first' ? 'FIRST PERSON' : 'THIRD PERSON', 1.2); }\n1402:  /** where a shot leaves from in third person: the camera's ray, begun level with the player (nothing behind them hit) */\n1404:  /** the muzzle in the world (tracers start there): the view model's in first person, the body's gun in third */\n1406:    if (S.view === 'third' && pb.G) return at(pb.G, S.cur === 'rifle' ? 12.6 : 14, S.cur === 'rifle' ? .55 : .95);\n1418:    // overlay over the fist (behind it in the world, the glove hid it); in third person on the body, chest high\n1435:  /* ---- the camera: the eyes (bob-free: the view model carries the motion), or over the right shoulder, pulled in\n1449:      const c = thirdCam(h.x, h.y, h.z, S.eye, S.adsB, S.stepPh, yaw, pitch, S.camClr); S.camClr = approach(S.camClr, c.need, dt * (c.need > S.camClr ? 90 : 40));\n1457:  /** the camera over the shoulder: beside and above the head, back along the view (closer down the sights) less clr (what\n1459:  function thirdCam(x, y, z, eye, adsB, ph, yaw, pitch, clr) {\n1592:    if (S.hp <= 0) { S.hp = 0; S.alive = false; S.lost = true; pb.move = 'dead'; pb.dead = { t: 0, dir: Math.atan2(hero.y - fy, hero.x - fx), g: hero.z }; S.view = 'third'; game.after(2.6, () => game.go('over', { fr\n1720:    spring(vm.kick, 0, 300, 26, dt); spring(vm.kp, 0, 240, 22, dt); spring(vm.kr, 0, 220, 20, dt);   // (two thirds back by the next shot: at 13 a second the gun chatters) spring(vm.dip, 0, 150, 13, dt);\n1763:    const jab = S.act === 'melee' ? win(t, 0, .05) * (1 - win(t, .2, .32)) : 0, shL = add(SH[0], [-1.5, -1.2, -2.6], jab);   // (a jab drops the shoulder: the upper arm stays under the picture)\n1964:    // (a shot from the hip shoulders the gun for a moment, so the gun and its flash are seen in third person)\n1965:    Object.assign(b, { x: hp[0], y: hp[1], z: hp[2], vx: h.vx, vy: h.vy, vz: h.vz, grounded: h.grounded, sprint: S.sprint, ads: S.ads || S.time - S.lastShot < .5, low: S.view === 'third', weapon: S.cur, act: S.act, \n1967:    const want = S.sprint && Math.hypot(h.vx, h.vy) > 40 && S.view === 'third' ? Math.atan2(h.vy, h.vx) : S.yaw; b.yaw = E.approachAng(b.yaw, want, dt * 10);\n1992:      if (S.view === 'third' && live) p = thirdCam(hp[0], hp[1], hp[2], lerp(ip.eye, S.eye, al), lerp(ip.adsB, S.adsB, al), lerp(ip.ph, S.stepPh, al), yaw, pitch, lerp(ip.clr, S.camClr, al)).p;\n1999:    if (S.view === 'third' || !S.alive) { pose(w, pb, dt); if (pb.gun.mag === 1) pb.gun.magP = add(pb.J.hands[0], pb.G.u, 2.1); drawSoldier(pen, pb); }\n2008:    Object.assign(L.muzzle, { x: mz[0], y: mz[1], z: mz[2], on: S.flash > .6, power: (S.view === 'third' ? 11 : 6) * S.flash, reach: S.view === 'third' ? 160 : 100 });   // (the shot's own frame only: no strobe)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23de6e6b-3ae6-4bf5-9764-44b18bb5857c","uuid":"27f7b8fc-cf2b-4a46-abc5-d81515f26696","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:27:21.280Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1:# my-3D2dge guide for AI models\n7:## North star\n17:## The mental model\n29:## Remake workflow (port, remaster, reimagine, remix)\n44: