{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013Gda19sgp3nEoc2Jz86UJB","type":"tool_result","content":"8:textures pixel by pixel, characters by the 2D engine's rigs (as cards, or as 3D puppets on the same joints), props and\n108:and its look: ground ('flagstone' 'grass' 'dirt' 'sand' 'snow' 'planks' 'tiles' 'plain' 'water' 'lava', or (x, y) =>\n114:o: { level, look: 'card' | 'puppet', res: 'pixels' | 'balanced' | 'full', gravity: 480, sky: '#06050b' or [top,\n143:the rig's weapon trail), look ('card' | 'puppet' for this one), shadow, pose: false (you pose it yourself) }\n146:a blob's { squash, look: [dx, dy], squint, flap }); world.step moves it, reads back a.x, a.y, a.z (its feet), a.vx,\n149:  a.resize(half) (a crouch, a slide: the capsule shorter, the feet kept; look up with world.ray before standing)\n191:  'zones' (Resident Evil's: camera.zones = [{ box: [x0, y0, x1, y1], at: [x, y, z], look: [x, y, z] (fixed) | follow:\n246:## The look\n247:  world.look = 'card' | 'puppet'; world.res = 'pixels' | 'balanced' | 'full'; world.shadows; world.outlines\n248:  world.filter = { look: 'clean' | 'cel' (Comic cel: flat bands of light, ink) | 'pixel' (big dithered pixels), apply:\n250:  E.World3D.SETTINGS in the game's menu lets the player pick the look, the picture, shadows and the filter.\n442:/* the puppets' toon look: three bands of light (shadow, base, lit), like the engine's tones */\n678: *      per look, walls and pillars instanced (cut low or to stumps by the view camera), stairs, platforms, braziers ---- */\n731:   * on that edge from the neighbour's height (a pit: 80 units down) up to its own, in the floor's side look */\n1066:  // frame: what this frame built or showed is never taken for another node in it; pass: what the last look showed\n1108: * 4. PARTS DRAWN BY CODE  instanced batches of four shapes (tube, ball, box, cone) in a toon look with outlines, and\n1484:  const look = b.look || [Math.cos(a.facing), Math.sin(a.facing)], 