{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjANFeSvL9Hn4Z3dfRhS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EAnqiR6wKQpR3SuekFzJkU","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211953__xee4d12/work/_research/engine; sed -n 1,40p engine/modules/story.js | cut -c1-280; echo ...ARCADE; grep -n \"attract\" engine/modules/arcade.js | cut -c1-240 | head -14; echo ...VOICE; grep -n \"voice\" dist/my-3d2dge.js | cut -c1-230 | head -24; echo ...CAT; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nfor name in ['mesh2motion','cmu','quaternius']:\n    c = json.load(open(f'src/mocap/catalogs/{name}.json'))\n    items = c.get('clips', c) if isinstance(c, dict) else c\n    keys = list(items.keys()) if isinstance(items, dict) else items\n    print(name, len(keys))\n    want = ['zombie','stagger','shamble','kick','suplex','throw','grab','limp','crawl','fall','get up','climb','ladder','stumble','hit','axe','pick','carry','push','reload','aim','death','crouch','rifle','pistol','gun','wounded','drag']\n    shown = 0\n    for k in keys:\n        v = items[k] if isinstance(items, dict) else k\n        s = json.dumps(v)\n        if any(w in (k + ' ' + s).lower() for w in want):\n            d = v.get('desc', '') if isinstance(v, dict) else ''\n            print('  ', k, '-', d[:70])\n            shown += 1\n            if shown > 45: break\nEOF","description":"Read story and arcade manuals, voice hooks and useful motion clips"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13575,"cache_read_input_tokens":241689,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13575},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23de6e6b-3ae6-4bf5-9764-44b18bb5857c","uuid":"6d6299b9-b089-422a-9b7d-54ade4f84e18","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:38:12.668Z","request_id":"req_011CgjANFN5q8ziCVDTZWC67","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01EAnqiR6wKQpR3SuekFzJkU":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211953__xee4d12/work/_research/engine; sed -n 1,40p engine/modules/story.js | cut -c1-280; echo ...ARCADE; grep -n \"attract\" engine/modules/arcade.js | cut -c1-240 | head -14; echo ...VOICE; grep -n \"voice\" dist/my-3d2dge.js | cut -c1-230 | head -24; echo ...CAT; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nfor name in ['mesh2motion','cmu','quaternius']:\n    c = json.load(open(f'src/mocap/catalogs/{name}.json'))\n    items = c.get('clips', c) if isinstance(c, dict) else c\n    keys = list(items.keys()) if isinstance(items, dict) else items\n    print(name, len(keys))\n    want = ['zombie','stagger','shamble','kick','suplex','throw','grab','limp','crawl','fall','get up','climb','ladder','stumble','hit','axe','pick','carry','push','reload','aim','death','crouch','rifle','pistol','gun','wounded','drag']\n    shown = 0\n    for k in keys:\n        v = items[k] if isinstance(items, dict) else k\n        s = json.dumps(v)\n        if any(w in (k + ' ' + s).lower() for w in want):\n            d = v.get('desc', '') if isinstance(v, dict) else ''\n            print('  ', k, '-', d[:70])\n            shown += 1\n            if shown > 45: break\nEOF","description":"Read story and arcade manuals, voice hooks and useful motion clips"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EAnqiR6wKQpR3SuekFzJkU","type":"tool_result","content":"/*!\nmy-3D2dge module STORY v0.88.0: dialogue as data, flags and values, a quest log and emote balloons\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nA JRPG's or an adventure's talk (Dragon Quest, Chrono Trigger, Zelda): conversations written as data and run through an\nE.Dialog (its markup and portraits), remembering what was said and done.\n- const story = new E.Story(game, { people: { elder: { name: 'ELDER', portrait: rig, at: npc } }, nodes, vars, on:\n  { gift(story, step) {...} }, dialog }). people: who speaks (portrait, full engine: a Humanoid or a function (g, x, y, size); at:\n  anything with x, y, z, and h its height, a balloon floats over); dialog: the E.Dialog it talks through (else its own:\n  story.talk); on: the game's handlers for events.\n- nodes: { id: [step, ...] }: the steps run in order, and a step with if runs only when its condition holds.\n  - { who, say: 'text' | [pages], choices: [{ text, if, goto, ...actions }] }: a line in the box (markup, {$name}\n    from vars); a choice's actions run when it is picked, then its goto, else the next step.\n  - { goto: 'id' } jumps; { end: true } stops; { wait: seconds } pauses.\n  - actions, on any step or choice: set: 'flag' | { key: value }; add: { gold: -50 }; quest: [id, title, text]; done:\n    id; emote: '!' | '?' | 'heart' | 'dots' | 'note' (over who's at); event: 'name' (calls on[name](story, step), after\n    the line on a step that speaks; with wait: true the story holds until story.resume(): the game's scene, a shop).\n  - conditions: 'flag' (set and truthy), '!flag', 'gold >= 50' (== != < <= > >=, a number or a word), 'quest:id'\n    (taken), 'done:id' (finished), an array (all of them), or a function (story) => true or false.\n- story.run(id, { onDone }) starts a node (stopping any other). In update: if (story.update(dt)) return; (true while it\n  runs: play waits); in draw: story.draw(r) (the box and the balloons). story.running; story.node: the node's id.\n- story.vars: every flag and value ({$name} in a line reads them); story.set(key, value = true), get(key) (a dotted\n  path), test(condition).\n- Quests: story.quest(id, title, text), story.done(id); story.quests: [{ id, title, text, done }] in the order taken.\n- story.emote(target, kind, seconds = 1.5): a balloon over anything with x, y, z (h: its height).\n- A visual novel: story.log (what was said and chosen: { who, name, text }, for a backlog), story.auto (seconds a page\n  stays before it turns), story.skip (pages type and turn at once; choices wait).\n- story.state() and story.restore(state): its vars and quests as JSON, for a save (game.saves' data, full engine).\n\n```js story\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true });\nconst story = new E.Story(game, { vars: { gold: 30, hero: 'ROWAN' }, nodes: {\n  elder: [{ if: 'helping', goto: 'thanks' }, { who: 'elder', say: 'Will you help us, {$hero}?', choices: [\n    { text: 'Yes', set: 'helping', quest: ['cave', 'The cave', 'Clear the cave north of town'] }, { text: 'No', goto: 'bye' }] },\n    { add: { gold: 20 } }],\n  thanks: [{ say: 'Thank you!' }, { if: 'gold >= 50', done: 'cave' }],\n  bye: [{ say: 'Farewell.' }] } });\ngame.start({ update(dt) { story.update(dt); }, draw(r) { story.draw(r); } });\nconst press = n => { for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { game.input.tap('confirm'); game.advance(.5); } };\n...ARCADE\n2:my-3D2dge module ARCADE v0.88.0: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode\n17:- The attract mode, on the title: cab.attract(dt) -> 'title', then 'demo' once o.idle seconds (20) pass without any player's input\n38: * ARCADE  scores, tables, initials, lives, credits, turns, cards and the attract mode\n45:   *  credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds),\n54:    /** mode: 'title' | 'play' | 'over'; demo: a demo is playing (no table); phase: the attract mode's, 'title' | 'demo' |\n61:  /** begin a game for 1 or 2 players (taking turns), o: { demo: true } for the attract mode's; spends the credits a\n114:  /** the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or\n116:  attract(dt) {\n124:  /** the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does) */\n126:  /** the demo is over (a demo in a scene of its own: call it on the way back): the attract mode shows the scores */\n203:  /** a table as a screen (the attract mode's, or after a game), its title at y: rank, name, score */\n...VOICE\n7617: *    saw, sine and noise voices, ready-made sound effects and a step sequencer.\n7630:/** built-in sound effects. A voice is { wave, freq, to, dur, vol, arp, step, vib: [rate, depth], filter, delay } */\n7680:     *  is none); volume: master volume 0..1; sfxVolume, musicVolume, voiceVolume: 0..1 for effects, music and the voice\n7681:     *  bus (bus('voice')); muted: true while mute() is on */\n7682:    this._game = game; this._signal = signal; this.ctx = null; this.volume = .7; this.sfxVolume = 1; this.musicVolume = .5; this.voiceVolume = 1; this.muted = false;\n7683:    /** presets: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one; song: the music\n7703:      this._voiceBus = c.createGain(); this._voiceBus.connect(this._master);   // (bus('voice'): a game's babble or speech)\n7716:  applyVolume() { if (!this.ctx) return; this._master.gain.value = this.muted ? 0 : this.volume; this._sfxBus.gain.value = this.sfxVolume; this._musBus.gain.value = this.musicVolume * (this._ducked || this.ducked ? .35 : 1); \n7717:  /** a bus for a sound of the game's own (Web Audio nodes it makes on audio.ctx: a babble voice, a loop, an instrument)\n7718:   *  to connect to, so it follows the volume, the mute and the player's settings: 'sfx', 'music', 'voice' (its level is\n7719:   *  voiceVolume) or 'master'. Returns a GainNode, or null where there is no sound (headless, no Web Audio) */\n7721:    if (!['sfx', 'music', 'voice', 'master'].includes(name)) warn('bus:' + name, 'audio.bus(\"' + name + '\"): no such bus (sfx, music, voice, master): the sfx bus');\n7723:    return name === 'master' ? this._master : name === 'music' ? this._musBus : name === 'voice' ? this._voiceBus : this._sfxBus;\n7740:  _voice(p, bus, t0, mul = 1) {\n7764:   * Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices.\n7771:    if (!p) { warn('sfx:' + what, 'unknown sound \"' + what + '\". Presets: ' + Object.keys(this.presets).join(', ') + ' (or audio.define(name, voice))'); return; }\n7777:    try { for (const v of Array.isArray(p) ? p : [p]) this._voice(o.vol === undefined ? v : Object.assign({}, v, { vol: (v.vol === undefined ? .3 : v.vol) * o.vol }), this._sfxBus, at, mul); }\n7781:  define(name, voice) { this.presets[name] = voice; }\n7947:      for (const v of kit) this._voice(Object.assign({}, v, { vol: v.vol * vol / .18 }), bus, time);\n7952:    this._voice({ wave: t.wave || 'square', freq: f * Math.pow(2, t.octave || 0), dur: n * spb * (t.gate || .9), vol, hold: true, attack: .006, vib: t.vib }, bus, time);\n9030:  /** new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, width, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types\n9036:     *  text's color; nameColor: the speaker's name's color; voice: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null\n9037:     *  for silence), or a function (letter, index, dialog) called once for each letter as it types (a babble voice:\n9040:    Object.assign(this, { speed: 50, lines: 3, place: 'bottom', color: '#ffffff', nameColor: '#ffd36a', voice: 'text', width: 0, bg: '#141a3a', border: '#e8e4ff', vars: null }, o);\n...CAT\nmesh2motion 180\n   Chop_Tree - \n   ClimbUp_1m_RM - \n   Crouch_Idle - \n   Crouch_Walk - \n   Hit_Head - \n   Hit_Knockback - \n   Hit_Knockback_RM - \n   Jump_air - \n   Jump_Land - \n   Jump_Start - \n   NinjaJump_Land - \n   NinjaJump_Start - \n   OverhandThrow - \n   PickUp_Table - \n   Pistol_Aim_Down - \n   Pistol_Aim_Neutral - \n   Pistol_Aim_Up - \n   Pistol_Idle - \n   Pistol_Reload - \n   Pistol_Shoot - \n   Push - \n   Sword_Regular_A - \n   Walk - \n   Walk_Carry - \n   Zombie_Idle - \n   Zombie_Scratch - \n   Zombie_Walk - \n   Death_D - \n   Hit_Chest - \n   Attack_Ground_Pound - \n   Backflip - \n   Bow - \n   Bow Pull Hold - \n   Climb Ladder - \n   Climb Wall - \n   Crawl - \n   Crawl RM - \n   Death_A - \n   Death_B - \n   Death_C - \n   Defend - \n   Dodge_left - \n   Dodge_left_RM - \n   Dodge_right - \n   Dodge_right_RM - \n   Jump_2 - \ncmu 62\n   $pick - \n   Zombie_Walk_Loop - \n   Jump_Kick - \n   Climb_Ladder - \n   Sneak_Loop - \n   Wounded_Walk_Loop - \n   Crouch_Walk_Loop - \n   Duck_Under - \n   Front_Kick - \n   Roundhouse_Kick - \n   Side_Kick - \n   Fall_On_Face - \n   Get_Up_Face_Down - \n   Duck_Thrown_Object - \n   Chop_Wood - \n   Pick_Up_Box - \n   Carry_Heavy_Box - \n   Search_Ground - \n   Frankenstein_Walk_Loop - \n   Dragon - \nquaternius 89\n   Walk_Loop - \n   Crouch_Idle_Loop - \n   Crouch_Fwd_Loop - \n   Jump_Start - \n   Jump_Loop - \n   Jump_Land - \n   Pistol_Idle_Loop - \n   Pistol_Aim_Neutral - \n   Pistol_Aim_Up - \n   Pistol_Aim_Down - \n   Pistol_Shoot - \n   Pistol_Reload - \n   Hit_Chest - \n   Hit_Head - \n   Death01 - \n   PickUp_Table - \n   Push_Loop - \n   Walk_Carry_Loop - \n   Zombie_Idle_Loop - \n   Zombie_Walk_Fwd_Loop - \n   Zombie_Scratch - \n   NinjaJump_Start - \n   NinjaJump_Land - \n   ClimbUp_1m_RM - \n   Sword_Regular_A - \n   OverhandThrow - \n   Hit_Knockback - \n   Hit_Knockback_RM - \n   TreeChopping_Loop -","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23de6e6b-3ae6-4bf5-97