{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tc9UvW9E4jGGbVPwP4iGuB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# PLAN: an over-the-shoulder action-horror game inspired by the source\n2\t\n3\tYou build this alone, from this plan and TASK.md. Nobody can answer questions, so where this plan leaves something open, decide and move on.\n4\t\n5\t## 0. How to use this plan\n6\t\n7\t- **TASK.md is the authority** on rules, deliverables and file names. This plan makes the creative and technical choices TASK.md leaves open, so you don't have to debate them again. If you find something better, change it, but keep the pillars (§1) and everything TASK.md requires.\n8\t- **The title is yours.** TASK.md says how to pick it. Nothing in this plan depends on it: the world, story and code read one title file (`src/title.txt`) and name the title nowhere else. Riffs that suit a wine-country setting are welcome in your brainstorm.\n9\t- **Paths** are relative to your dev folder. \"The single HTML file\" and \"the exit interview\" are the deliverables TASK.md names.\n10\t- **[verified]** means the plan's author ran it on this computer on 2026-11-04 against my-3D2dge v0.88.0 and AI Hub client 1.4.0, and it worked as written. Don't re-investigate those; build on them.\n11\t- **Read in this order:** TASK.md, this plan, then the header of `engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js` (the 3D manual, 260 lines) and `engine/API.md`. Search `engine/API-INDEX.md` for names; don't read it whole.\n12\t- **Keep `NOTES.md`** in the dev folder as you go: issues your tests caught (count them, and mark the game-breaking ones), where you got stuck, what you changed in the engine and why. TASK.md asks for these at the end, and you won't remember them.\n13\t\n14\t## 1. The game\n15\t\n16\t**Pitch.** Days before a state dinner, the President's personal sommelier is kidnapped on a buying trip. Special Agent Vera Cask of the U.S. Excise Bureau goes in alone, on a regional train, to a valley in the Grand Duchy of Vaudrenia, where the harvest has gone wrong: a fungus called the Noble Bloom got into the grapes, and then into the people. She shoots, kicks and haggles her way through a village, a château and a bottling plant, keeping a fearless, insufferable 71-year-old snob alive, to stop the Last Pressing: a vintage that would carry the Bloom to every state dinner on Earth.\n17\t\n18\t**Pillars.** When a choice is unclear, the one that serves these wins.\n19\t\n20\t1. **Every shot is a decision.** Feet planted, a laser dot that wobbles. Head, knee and arm each do something different, and each opens a different follow-up.\n21\t2. **Crowds, not waves.** Enemies come on slowly, spread out, surround you and cut you off. Space is the resource you spend.\n22\t3. **Protect the worst person you've ever met.** Ambrose is useful, brave, fragile and rude. The player should want to save him and want to strangle him.\n23\t4. **Greed between the terror.** Crates, treasure, a duty-free trolley that shouldn't exist, upgrades, arranging your case. Neon means safe.\n24\t5. **Deadpan pulp.** Scary for twenty seconds, then someone says something stupid with total sincerity.\n25\t6. **Keep escalating.** Something new every five minutes: a toy, an enemy, a set piece.\n26\t\n27\t**What we take from the source, and how we make it our own.** TASK.md asks for what makes the source distinctive, turned into an *original* game. Mechanics and genre conventions are fair game. Its specifics are not.\n28\t\n29\t| What makes the source distinctive | Our original version |\n30\t|---|---|\n31\t| A lone agent, a rescue, a remote Old World backwater | A federal excise agent, the President's sommelier, a wine valley in a fictional duchy |\n32\t| Possessed rural folk, then aristocrats, then a militarised finale | The Pressed (vineyard folk), the Confraternity of the Last Pressing at Château Rémuage, Vane Beverages' bottling plant and private security |\n33\t| Over-the-shoulder aim with planted feet; body-part hits open melee | The same genre mechanics with our own moves and numbers: KICK, SLAM, FRISK |\n34\t| A parasite that bursts out when the host \"dies\" | The Noble Bloom: magenta fungal growths, with our own variants (tendril, puffball, crawler) |\n35\t| An escort who can wait, hide and get carried off | Ambrose Pell: his Nose finds hidden enemies and weak points, and he tastes his way through puzzles |\n36\t| A wandering merchant, weapon tuning, a grid case, treasure sets | The Duty-Free Man and his neon-lit trolley, an evidence case, wine treasures you combine |\n37\t| Save points as a ritual | Passport stamps at old customs desks |\n38\t| Button prompts in the middle of the action | Prompts everywhere, and one set piece built on them: The Toast |\n39\t| Cheesy one-liners, operatic villains on the radio | §11, written fresh |\n40\t\n41\t**Must stay original (hard rule).** No character, place, organisation, item name, enemy design, boss design, line of dialogue, tune, level layout or logo from the source or its series. Don't echo its famous lines, even as a wink. Don't recreate its specific rooms or set pieces beat for beat: if a scene feels like a copy of a remembered one, change the place, the trigger and the payoff. The source's name appears only where TASK.md asks: the title riff and the Source Information. Lay out levels from §12, not from memory of any game.\n42\t\n43\t## 2. Decisions at a glance\n44\t\n45\t| TASK.md item | Decision |\n46\t|---|---|\n47\t| Genre | Over-the-shoulder action horror: a third-person shooter with a survival-horror economy, escort, puzzles and set pieces. A co-op score-attack mode, Last Stand, sits beside the campaign. |\n48\t| Perspective | Third person, over the right shoulder (swappable), tighter when aiming. |\n49\t| Title | Yours: 50 riffs in your head, then a real RNG (`node -e \"console.log(require('crypto').randomInt(50))\"`). Write the winner to `src/title.txt`. |\n50\t| Research | Done for you here for engine, hub and design. Do more only if you hit a gap, and report what you actually did. |\n51\t| Package | One self-contained HTML file: both engines, three.js, Rapier, clips and game inlined, about 6 to 9 MB. No CDN and no downloads, so it runs offline from `file://` and inside the hub. **[verified]** |\n52\t| Tech stack | my-3D2dge v0.88.0: the 2D engine from the handoff package plus its **real-3D add-on `E.World3D`** (three.js r182, Rapier 0.19.3), bundled with esbuild. The handoff README itself sends real-3D games to this add-on. Do not build this on the 2D views. |\n53\t| Art direction | The engine's own look: code-drawn, toon-banded low-poly, chunky pixel textures at 16 pixels a metre, a pixel-font HUD, fog and strong lighting. New shapes, materials and bodies for the wine country; store and core props for generic things (§10). |\n54\t| Animation | The engine's own systems: its procedural soldier skeleton (IK feet, hands on gun) and its motion-clip store in readable key poses, drawn as pen bodies. New clips and poses for our signature moves (§5). |\n55\t| Audio | All Web Audio from code, on the engine's buses. Music slider defaults to 10% **[verified recipe]**. Gibberish voices per speaker (§14). |\n56\t| Online | AI Hub Session Protocol v1, `shared-world`, 1 to 4 players: the Last Stand round. On its own: solo Last Stand and 2-player couch split-screen (§16). |\n57\t| Performance | Out of scope. Add the detail, enemies, effects, lights and shadows the scene needs. The one exception: a hub round must become ready inside the hub's load limit (§16). |\n58\t| Testing | One command, failures and a one-line count only (§17). |\n59\t| Effort | Spend it where §18 says it shows. |\n60\t\n61\t**Working rules from TASK.md, applied.** Everything stays in your own folder (not `/tmp`, not a parent). Read only what you need; other agents work beside you and share the machine's ports and processes. One or two browsers at once. Prefer `file://`. The only server you need is for the hub suite (§17): `127.0.0.1`, a port the OS picks, confirm the page is yours, stop it by its own PID. Never `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`. Extra Python packages only via `uv` as TASK.md describes.\n62\t\n63\t## 3. Tech setup (all [verified])\n64\t\n65\t### 3.1 Get the engine (2 seconds, 16 MB; a full clone takes minutes and 150 MB)\n66\t\n67\tRun from the dev folder. The `engine/` tree mirrors the repository's so that the tools' relative paths still work.\n68\t\n69\t```sh\n70\tgit clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --no-checkout https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git .repo\n71\tgit -C .repo sparse-checkout set --no-cone '/dist/handoff/' '/dist/my-3d2dge-3d.js' '/vendor/' '/src/starter3d/' '/src/mocap/' '/tools/anim-set.mjs' '/tools/mocap-lib.mjs' '/tools/kit3d-test.mjs' '/docs/MOCAP.md' '/docs/ENGINE-3D.md'\n72\tgit -C .repo checkout -q main\n73\tmkdir -p engine lib/hub tools src assets tests\n74\tcp -r .repo/dist/handoff/. engine/\n75\tcp .repo/dist/my-3d2dge-3d.js engine/\n76\tcp -r .repo/vendor engine/vendor\n77\tcp -r .repo/src/starter3d .repo/src/mocap engine/src/\n78\tcp .repo/tools/anim-set.mjs .repo/tools/mocap-lib.mjs .repo/tools/kit3d-test.mjs engine/tools/\n79\tcp .repo/docs/MOCAP.md .repo/docs/ENGINE-3D.md engine/docs/\n80\trm -rf .repo\n81\tnpm init -y >/dev/null && npm install --no-audit --no-fund playwright@1.63.0\n82\tfor f in session.js harness.html bridge.js round.js README.md; do curl -fsSL \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f\" -o \"lib/hub/$f\"; done\n83\t```\n84\t\n85\tNever run `npx playwright install`, even though the handoff README says to: the browsers are already on this computer, and TASK.md forbids it. You may edit anything under `engine/`.\n86\t\n87\tFiles to copy from, not read whole:\n88\t\n89\t- `engine/src/starter3d/30-shooter.js`: the over-the-shoulder camera, look, gunplay, soldier skeleton, tracers, decals, ladders, mantles, gunmen's AI.\n90\t- `engine/src/starter3d/40-horror.js`: doors, keys, item box, saves, grabs, flow-field AI, and a bot that plays a whole game.\n91\t- `engine/src/starter3d/00-shell.js`: what those two expect around them.\n92\t\n93\t### 3.2 Folder layout\n94\t\n95\t```\n96\tengine/   the engine, its docs, tools and asset store     lib/hub/  session client and test harness, unmodified\n97\tassets/   clips.js (cut clips), sets.js (cut asset sets)  tools/    build.mjs, patch-engine.mjs, level-check.mjs\n98\ttests/    run.mjs, suites/                                .build/   bundler output (not a deliverable)\n99\tsrc/      title.txt, main.js, and:\n100\t  core/    config, Tune table, Run state, registry (def), events, FEATURES, about data\n101\t  body/    soldier pose, clip pose, looks, drawers, hit zones\n102\t  player/  controller, camera, weapons, melee, grenades, traversal\n103\t  ai/      director, one file per enemy, bosses/, ally (Ambrose)\n104\t  world/   materials, shapes, legend, zone loader, doors, links, barricades, pickups, encounters\n105\t  zones/   one data file per zone (pure data, so Node tests can import them)\n106\t  ui/      prompts, focus, hud, case, trolley, map, passport, results, title, about, dev, gameover\n107\t  story/   dialog, voices, cutscene helpers, qte, lines/\n108\t  audio/   sfx, music engine, songs/\n109\t  modes/   campaign, laststand, net (hub), attract, bots\n110\t```\n111\t\n112\t### 3.3 The build\n113\t\n114\t**`tools/build.mjs`**\n115\t\n116\t```js\n117\t// node tools/build.mjs <path of the single HTML file>   (run from the dev folder)\n118\timport { readFileSync as read, writeFileSync as write, mkdirSync } from 'node:fs';\n119\timport { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';\n120\timport { resolve } from 'node:path';\n121\tconst out = process.argv[2], V = resolve('engine/vendor'), T3 = V + '/three-0.182.0', txt = f => read(f, 'utf8');\n122\tconst esc = s => s.replace(/<\\/script/gi, '<\\\\/script');   // a script's text must not close its tag early\n123\tmkdirSync('.build', { recursive: true });\n124\texecFileSync('esbuild', ['src/main.js', '--bundle', '--format=esm', '--target=es2022', '--legal-comments=none', '--minify-syntax', '--minify-whitespace', '--loader:.txt=text',\n125\t  `--alias:three/webgpu=${T3}/three.webgpu.min.js`, `--alias:three/tsl=${T3}/three.tsl.min.js`, `--alias:three=${T3}/three.webgpu.min.js`,\n126\t  `--alias:@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat=${V}/rapier3d-simd-compat-0.19.3/rapier.js`, '--outfile=.build/game.js', '--log-level=warning'], { stdio: 'inherit' });\n127\tconst classic = ['engine/my-3d2dge.js', 'engine/src/mocap/readable.js', 'engine/src/mocap/mocap.js', 'assets/clips.js'];   // cut asset sets go here too\n128\tconst html = `<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n129\t<script>${txt('lib/hub/session.js')}</script>\n130\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"><meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\"><meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\"><meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"4\">\n131\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Survive the harvest and outscore your crew\">\n132\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move WASD/stick, aim right click/L2, fire left click/R2, kick E/Cross\">\n133\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\"><title>${txt('src/title.txt').trim()}</title>\n134\t<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; overflow: hidden; background: #000 }</style></head><body>\n135\t<div id=\"stage\" style=\"position:relative;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:hidden\"><canvas id=\"view\"></canvas><canvas id=\"screen\" style=\"position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%\"></canvas></div>\n136\t${classic.map(f => `<script>${esc(txt(f))}</script>`).join('\\n')}\n137\t<script>if (!self.GPUShaderStage) self.GPUShaderStage = { VERTEX: 1, FRAGMENT: 2, COMPUTE: 4 };</script>\n138\t<script type=\"module\">${esc(txt('.build/game.js'))}</script></body></html>`;\n139\twrite(out, html); console.log('wrote ' + out + ' ' + (html.length / 1e6).toFixed(1) + ' MB');\n140\t```\n141\t\n142\tWhy it looks like this:\n143\t\n144\t- `session.js` must be the first script, right after `<meta charset>`, pasted unmodified. The hub swaps in new versions by matching it.\n145\t- The `GPUShaderStage` line is required. Without it, three's WebGPU build crashes on load in browsers with no WebGPU, such as Firefox on Linux.\n146\t- Inline module scripts run fine on `file://`. Rapier's wasm is embedded as base64, so nothing is fetched.\n147\t- The kit's determinism hash came out **identical on Chromium (WebGL 2 and WebGPU), WebKit and Firefox** from a file built this way.\n148\t\n149\t### 3.4 Two engine patches: apply once, right after §3.1\n150\t\n151\t**Without the first patch the game crashes on every zone change on real players' machines.** `world.dispose()` throws inside three on WebGPU, which is what Chromium uses on any machine with a GPU, and WebGL-only tests never see it. The second patch lets the attract mode show behind the touch-only notice, as TASK.md wants. Record both in `NOTES.md`: TASK.md asks what you changed in the engine.\n152\t\n153\t**`tools/patch-engine.mjs`**\n154\t\n155\t```js\n156\t// node tools/patch-engine.mjs   (run once from the dev folder, right after getting the engine)\n157\timport { readFileSync as read, writeFileSync as write } from 'node:fs';\n158\tconst patch = (file, from, to) => { const s = read(file, 'utf8'); if (!s.includes(from)) throw new Error(`patch: not found in ${file}: ${from.slice(0, 60)}`); write(file, s.replace(from, to)); };\n159\t// 1. world.dispose() throws inside three on WebGPU: dispose each thing once, and let one failure not stop the rest\n160\tpatch('engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js',\n161\t`    this.scene.traverse(o => { if (o.isMesh) { o.geometry && o.geometry.dispose(); } });\n162\t    for (const x of this._owned) if (x && x.dispose) x.dispose();`,\n163\t`    const gone = new Set(), safely = x => { if (!x || !x.dispose || gone.has(x)) return; gone.add(x); try { x.dispose(); } catch (e) { /* WebGPU: nothing was uploaded to destroy */ } };\n164\t    this.scene.traverse(o => { if (o.isMesh) safely(o.geometry); });\n165\t    for (const x of this._owned) safely(x);`);\n166\t// 2. the touch-only notice hid the attract mode behind 88% black: make it lighter, and put it at the bottom\n167\tpatch('engine/my-3d2dge.js',\n168\t  'display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:24px;text-align:center;background:rgba(5,3,12,.88)',\n169\t  'display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:center;padding:24px;text-align:center;background:rgba(5,3,12,.35)');\n170\tconsole.log('engine patched');\n171\t```\n172\t\n173\t### 3.5 First boot: start from this\n174\t\n175\tPaste it into `src/main.js`, put any title in `src/title.txt`, run the patch, cut the clips, build, and open the file. You get a dusk village in real 3D, an over-the-shoulder camera with mouse and right stick, planted-feet aiming with a laser, a crowd that comes on by flow field, and a hub round that passes all four harness cases. **Grow this into the game; don't start again from an empty file.** Its look (sky, fog, sun, `outlines: false`, `res: 'balanced'`) is the agreed starting point.\n176\t\n177\t```sh\n178\tnode tools/patch-engine.mjs\n179\techo 'ANY TITLE FOR NOW' > src/title.txt\n180\t(cd engine && node tools/anim-set.mjs src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js src/mocap/sets/mesh2motion.js src/mocap/sets/cmu.js --name CLIPS --out ../assets/clips.js --clips \"QUATERNIUS:Idle_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Walk_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Walk_Formal_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Jog_Fwd_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Sprint_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Idle_FoldArms_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Idle_Talking_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Idle_Lantern_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Idle_Rail_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Sitting_Idle_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Sitting_Talking_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Zombie_Idle_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Zombie_Walk_Fwd_Loop,CMU:Zombie_Walk_Loop,CMU:Wounded_Walk_Loop,CMU:Hurt_Stomach_Walk_Loop,CMU:Looking_Around,QUATERNIUS:Zombie_Scratch,CMU:Chop_Wood,QUATERNIUS:Melee_Hook,QUATERNIUS:OverhandThrow,QUATERNIUS:Sword_Dash_RM,QUATERNIUS:Idle_Shield_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Idle_Shield_Break,QUATERNIUS:Hit_Chest,QUATERNIUS:Hit_Head,MESH2MOTION:Dizzy,MESH2MOTION:Kneeling Tired,QUATERNIUS:Hit_Knockback,QUATERNIUS:LayToIdle,CMU:Fall_On_Face,CMU:Get_Up_Face_Down,QUATERNIUS:Death01,MESH2MOTION:Death_A,MESH2MOTION:Death_B,MESH2MOTION:Death_C,MESH2MOTION:Defend,CMU:Duck_Thrown_Object,MESH2MOTION:Crawl,MESH2MOTION:Climb Ladder,QUATERNIUS:ClimbUp_1m_RM,CMU:Run_Jump_Over,MESH2MOTION:Land_Three_Point,QUATERNIUS:Push_Loop,CMU:Roundhouse_Kick,CMU:Side_Kick,CMU:Front_Kick,QUATERNIUS:Consume,CMU:Drink_Water,QUATERNIUS:PickUp_Table,QUATERNIUS:Walk_Carry_Loop,CMU:Carry_Heavy_Box,MESH2MOTION:Greeting\")\n181\t```\n182\t\n183\tThat is 53 clips and 350 KB. Add more whenever you need them (`engine/src/mocap/catalogs/*.json` describes every clip).\n184\t\n185\t**`src/main.js`**\n186\t\n187\t```js\n188\t// The first boot: real 3D on one file, an over-the-shoulder camera, a clip-driven pen body, the hub's round. Grow it into the game.\n189\timport '../engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js';   // first: it adds E.World3D to the 2D engine\n190\timport GAME_TITLE from './title.txt';\n191\tconst E = My3D2dge, W3 = E.World3D, PI = Math.PI, hubOn = AIHub.active;\n192\t\n193\tconst KEYS = { up: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'Pad12'], down: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'Pad13'], left: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'Pad14'], right: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'Pad15'],\n194\t  aim: ['Mouse2', 'Pad6'], fire: ['Mouse0', 'Pad7'], act: ['KeyE', 'Space', 'Pad0'], sprint: ['ShiftLeft', 'Pad1'],\n195\t  start: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Pad9'], pause: ['Escape', 'KeyP', 'Pad9'], confirm: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Pad0'], cancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'Pad1'] };\n196\tconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, bg: null, input: KEYS, touch: 'never', autoPause: !hubOn, live: hubOn, menu: { quit: false, settings: [\n197\t  ...W3.SETTINGS.filter(s => s.key !== 'look3d').map(s => s.key === 'picture3d' ? { ...s, value: 'balanced' } : s),\n198\t  { key: 'music', value: .1 },   // the Music slider starts at 10%\n199\t  { key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['xbox', 'Xbox']] }] } });\n200\t\n201\t/* ---- materials and shapes of our own: a material's fn returns [r, g, b] (a hex string bakes black) ---- */\n202\tconst hx = E.hex;\n203\tW3.SIDE.plaster = { w: 32, h: 48, fn(x, y) {   // lime plaster over timber, a rubble course below\n204\t  const z = 47 - y; if (x % 16 < 2 || z > 44 || (z > 14 && z < 17)) return hx(E.hash2(x, y) < .2 ? '#3a2616' : '#4c3220');\n205\t  if (z < 14) { const r = Math.floor(z / 5), off = r % 2 ? 3 : 0; return hx((x + off) % 7 === 0 || z % 5 === 0 ? '#3a3630' : E.hash2(((x + off) / 7) | 0, r) < .4 ? '#6e675a' : '#7f7768'); }\n206\t  return hx(E.hash2(x * 3, y * 7) < .07 ? '#a89a7c' : E.hash2(x, y) < .15 ? '#d6c8a4' : '#c8bb96'); } };\n207\tW3.GROUND.cobble = (x, y) => { const h = E.hash2(Math.floor(x / 5), Math.floor(y / 5)), k = 70 + h * 34; return x % 5 < 1 || y % 5 < 1 ? [46, 40, 34] : [k + 8, k, k - 8]; };\n208\tE.SHAPES.roofA = { about: 'gable roof', mats: { r: 'shingle' }, parts: [['prism', 'r', [0, 0, 0], [[-50, -1], [50, -1], [0, 44]], 131, { axis: 'x' }]] };\n209\tE.SHAPES.vinerow = { about: 'trained vines on posts and wire, heavy with fruit', mats: { p: 'walnut', l: 'leaves', g: '#4a2348 glaze' }, parts: [['row', 5, [16, 0, 0], ['box', 'p', [0, 0, 0], [1.5, 1.5, 26]]], ['box', 'l', [0, 0, 11], [68, 6, 15]], ['row', 9, [8, 0, 0], ['ball', 'g', [0, 3.6, 12], 2.1]], ['row', 9, [8, 0, 0], ['ball', 'g', [4, -3.6, 13], 2]]] };\n210\tE.SHAPES.press = { about: 'a great wooden wine press: slatted basket, iron screw, beam', mats: { w: 'oak', i: 'iron', d: 'walnut' }, parts: [['cyl', 'w', [0, 0, 0], 22, 22], ['ring', 12, 22.5, ['box', 'd', [0, 0, 0], [3, 2, 23]]], ['cyl', 'i', [0, 0, 14], 3, 56], ['box', 'd', [0, 0, 56], [64, 7, 7]], ['mirror', 'x', ['box', 'd', [30, 0, 0], [7, 7, 62]]], ['cyl', 'i', [0, 0, 22], 21, 2]] };\n211\t\n212\t/* ---- a level is text, one character a metre. W: a window (sill and lintel, an opening you see and shoot through) ---- */\n213\tconst LEVEL = { rows: [\n214\t  'vvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv',\n215\t  'v......................................................v',\n216\t  'v..V.......V.......V......................V.......V....v',\n217\t  'v......,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,.........v',\n218\t  'v...HHWHHHHW,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,HHHWHH.......v',\n219\t  'v...H......H,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,H.....H......v',\n220\t  'v...H......W,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,W.....H......v',\n221\t  'v...H......H,,,,,,,z,,,,,,,,,,,,,z,,,,,,,,H.....W......v',\n222\t  'v...H.......,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,.....H......v',\n223\t  'v...H......H,,,,z,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,z,,,,,,H.....H......v',\n224\t  'v...HHHHHHHH,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,HHHHHHH......v',\n225\t  'v......,,,,,,,,,,z,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,z,,,,,,,,,,,,.........v',\n226\t  'v...B..,,,,c,,,,,,z,,,,,,,,,,,,z,,,,,,,,c,,,,,..B......v',\n227\t  'v......,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,.........v',\n228\t  'v......,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,@,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,.........v',\n229\t  'v......,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,.........v',\n230\t  'v..V.......V.......V......................V.......V....v',\n231\t  'v......................................................v',\n232\t  'vvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv'],\n233\t  ground: 'dirt', colors: { base: '#4c4a2c', dark: '#3e3f26', light: '#5a5632' }, legend: {\n234\t    v: { wall: 96, side: 'earth', color: '#2a2a24', top: '#20261c' }, ',': { ground: 'cobble' }, H: { wall: 48, side: 'plaster', top: '#5a3a2a' },\n235\t    W: { wall: 14, side: 'plaster', platform: 48, thick: 16 }, V: { shape: 'vinerow', solid: true }, B: { shape: 'barrel' }, c: { shape: 'cart', facing: .6, ground: 'cobble' },\n236\t    z: { mark: 'z', ground: 'cobble' }, '@': { mark: 'start', ground: 'cobble' } } };\n237\t\n238\t/* ---- a body: motion clips drive body points (millimetres, forward/right/up), the pen draws limbs over them ---- */\n239\tconst lib = Mocap.load(MOCAP.CLIPS), MM = .016, buf = new Float32Array(lib.P * 3);   // 16 units a metre\n240\tconst add = (a, b, k = 1) => [a[0] + b[0] * k, a[1] + b[1] * k, a[2] + b[2] * k], sub = (a, b) => [a[0] - b[0], a[1] - b[1], a[2] - b[2]], nrm = a => { const l = Math.hypot(...a) || 1; return [a[0] / l, a[1] / l, a[2] / l]; };\n241\tfunction drawBody(pen, a, X, c) {\n242\t  const co = Math.cos(a.facing), si = Math.sin(a.facing), P = n => { const i = lib.idx[n] * 3, f = X[i] * MM, r = X[i + 1] * MM; return [a.x + co * f - si * r, a.y + si * f + co * r, a.z + X[i + 2] * MM]; };\n243\t  const tube = (p, q, r, col) => pen.tube(p[0], p[1], p[2], q[0], q[1], q[2], r, col), ball = (p, r, col) => pen.ball(p[0], p[1], p[2], r, r, r, col), slab = (p, q, ac, w, t, col) => pen.slab(p[0], p[1], p[2], q[0], q[1], q[2], ac[0], ac[1], ac[2], w, t, col);\n244\t  const pel = P('pelvis'), che = P('chest'), nek = P('neck'), hed = P('head'), top = P('headTop'), face = nrm(sub(P('faceF'), hed)), rt = nrm(sub(P('shR'), P('shL'))), rtP = nrm(sub(P('hipR'), P('hipL'))), up = nrm(sub(top, hed));\n245\t  for (const s of 'LR') { const kn = P('knee' + s), an = P('ankle' + s); tube(P('hip' + s), kn, 2, c.pants); tube(kn, an, 1.4, c.pants); ball(kn, 1.5, c.pants); slab(add(an, [0, 0, -.6]), add(P('toe' + s), [0, 0, .3]), rt, 2.3, 1.6, c.boot); }\n246\t  slab(add(pel, [0, 0, .4]), che, rtP, 6.6, 4.2, c.shirt); slab(che, nek, rt, 7, 3.9, c.shirt); slab(add(pel, rtP, -3.1), add(pel, rtP, 3.1), face, 3.4, 4.3, c.belt);\n247\t  for (const s of 'LR') { const sh = P('sh' + s), el = P('elbow' + s), wr = P('wrist' + s); ball(sh, 1.9, c.shirt); tube(sh, el, 1.35, c.shirt); tube(el, wr, 1.1, c.skin); ball(P('fist' + s), 1.1, c.skin); }\n248\t  tube(nek, hed, 1, c.skin); const hc = add(hed, sub(top, hed), .45); pen.ball(hc[0], hc[1], hc[2], 2.2, 2.2, 2.5, c.skin); const cap = add(hc, up, .9); pen.ball(cap[0], cap[1], cap[2], 2.45, 2.45, 1.9, c.hair);\n249\t  if (c.eyes) for (const k of [-1, 1]) { const e = add(add(hc, face, 2.05), rt, k * .85); pen.glow(e[0], e[1], e[2], .34, c.eyes); }\n250\t}\n251\tconst VERA = { skin: '#d8ae8c', hair: '#2a1c14', shirt: '#2e3e58', pants: '#23242c', boot: '#17140f', belt: '#3a2a1a' }, PICKER = { skin: '#b89a80', hair: '#4a3a24', shirt: '#7a6a4c', pants: '#3a3430', boot: '#231f1b', belt: '#2a2018', eyes: '#ff5a2a' };\n252\t\n253\t/* ---- the world and one scene: over the shoulder, feet planted to aim, the crowd comes on ---- */\n254\tlet world, flow, hero, crowd = [], yaw = -PI / 2, pitch = -.05, aimK = 0, heroT = 0, sendT = 0, info = null;\n255\tconst mouse = [0, 0], dir = [0, 0], focus = { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 };\n256\tfunction buildWorld() {\n257\t  world = new W3(game, { level: LEVEL, res: 'balanced', outlines: false, sky: ['#27284a', '#e8955a'], fog: { color: '#b07a5a', near: 180, far: 900 }, ambient: ['#a4a8d0', '#6a5038', 2.1],\n258\t    sun: { color: '#ffb070', intensity: 2.6, dir: [.72, .42, -.45], area: 900, shadow: true, map: 2048 }, lights: 2, camera: { mode: 'fixed', capture: true }, onDraw: w => {\n259\t      for (const e of crowd) { lib.sample(lib.clip(Math.hypot(e.vx, e.vy) > 4 ? 'Zombie_Walk_Loop' : 'Zombie_Idle_Loop'), e.data.t, buf); drawBody(w.pen, e, buf, PICKER); }\n260\t      if (!hero) return; lib.sample(lib.clip(aimK > .5 ? 'Idle_Loop' : Math.hypot(hero.vx, hero.vy) > 8 ? 'Jog_Fwd_Loop' : 'Idle_Loop'), heroT, buf); drawBody(w.pen, hero, buf, VERA);\n261\t      if (aimK > .5) { const cp = Math.cos(pitch), d = [Math.cos(yaw) * cp, Math.sin(yaw) * cp, Math.sin(pitch)], o = [hero.x + d[0] * 8, hero.y + d[1] * 8, hero.z + 21], hit = w.ray(o[0], o[1], o[2], d[0], d[1], d[2], 600, { skip: hero }), L = hit ? hit.dist : 600, p = add(o, d, L); w.pen.bar(o[0], o[1], o[2], p[0], p[1], p[2], .3, .3, '#ff2a1a'); w.pen.glow(p[0], p[1], p[2], 1, '#ff3a2a'); }\n262\t    } });\n263\t  world.prepare();\n264\t}\n265\tconst play = { pausable: true, view: 'iso',\n266\t  enter() {\n267\t    world.reset(); flow = world.flow(); world.shape('press', 27.5 * 16, 7.5 * 16, 0, { solid: true }); world.shape('roofA', 8 * 16, 7.5 * 16, 48, { facing: 0 });   // (world.reset takes these away: place them again)\n268\t    const s = world.marks.start[0]; hero = info && info.server ? null : world.hero({ x: s.x, y: s.y, r: 4.5, half: 9, visible: false, shadow: false });\n269\t    crowd = world.marks.z.map((m, i) => { const e = world.mob({ x: m.x, y: m.y, r: 5, half: 8, visible: false, shadow: false }); e.data.t = i * .37; return e; });\n270\t    world.camera.set('fixed'); world.camera.follow(hero || crowd[0]); world.camera.target = focus;\n271\t  },\n272\t  update(dt) {\n273\t    const I = game.input, h = hero;\n274\t    if (h) {\n275\t      world.camera.takeMouse(mouse); yaw += mouse[0] * .0021; pitch = E.clamp(pitch - mouse[1] * .0021, -1.2, 1.2);\n276\t      const a = I.padAim; if (a) { yaw += a[0] * 2.4 * dt; pitch = E.clamp(pitch - a[1] * 1.8 * dt, -1.2, 1.2); }\n277\t      aimK = E.approach(aimK, I.down('aim') ? 1 : 0, dt * 6); heroT += dt;\n278\t      const m = I.move(), fx = Math.cos(yaw), fy = Math.sin(yaw), sp = aimK > .05 ? 0 : I.down('sprint') ? 88 : 52, mx = fx * -m[1] - fy * m[0], my = fy * -m[1] + fx * m[0];\n279\t      h.vx = E.approach(h.vx, mx * sp, 700 * dt); h.vy = E.approach(h.vy, my * sp, 700 * dt);\n280\t      if (aimK > .05) h.facing = yaw; else if (Math.hypot(mx, my) > .1) h.facing = E.approachAng(h.facing, Math.atan2(my, mx), dt * 10);\n281\t      const cp = Math.cos(pitch), f = [fx * cp, fy * cp, Math.sin(pitch)], piv = [h.x - fy * 12, h.y + fx * 12, h.z + 31], want = E.lerp(42, 30, aimK), ray = world.ray(piv[0], piv[1], piv[2], -f[0], -f[1], -f[2], want + 4, { skip: h, level: true }), d = ray ? Math.max(6, ray.dist - 3) : want;\n282\t      world.camera.fixed = { x: piv[0] - f[0] * d, y: piv[1] - f[1] * d, z: piv[2] - f[2] * d, yaw, pitch, roll: 0, fov: E.lerp(60, 46, aimK), near: 2 };\n283\t      focus.x = h.x + fx * 320; focus.y = h.y + fy * 320; focus.z = h.z + 10;\n284\t    } else world.camera.fixed = { x: 400, y: 500, z: 200, yaw: -PI / 2, pitch: -.5, roll: 0, fov: 60, near: 2 };\n285\t    if (!info || info.isHost) { flow.to(h ? h.x : 400, h ? h.y : 200); for (const e of crowd) { e.data.t += dt; const near = h && Math.hypot(h.x - e.x, h.y - e.y) < 26; if (!near && flow.dir(e.x, e.y, dir)) { e.vx = dir[0] * 24; e.vy = dir[1] * 24; e.facing = E.approachAng(e.facing, Math.atan2(dir[1], dir[0]), dt * 4); } else e.vx = e.vy = 0; } }\n286\t    if (info && AIHub.time() > -3000 && (sendT -= dt) <= 0) { sendT = 1 / 12; AIHub.send(info.isHost ? { t: 's', e: crowd.map(e => [Math.round(e.x), Math.round(e.y)]) } : { t: 'i', x: h ? Math.round(h.x) : 0, y: h ? Math.round(h.y) : 0 }, info.isHost ? { reliable: false } : { to: info.host, reliable: false }); }\n287\t    world.step(dt);\n288\t  },\n289\t  draw(r) { world.draw(r); r.overlay(g => E.font.text(g, GAME_TITLE.trim(), 8, r.H - 16, '#e8e0d0', { outline: '#000' })); }\n290\t};\n291\tasync function main() {\n292\t  info = hubOn ? await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4] }) : null;\n293\t  if (info) {\n294\t    AIHub.on('message', (d, from) => { if (d.t === 's' && !info.isHost) d.e.forEach(([x, y], i) => crowd[i] && crowd[i].place(x, y, crowd[i].z)); });\n295\t    AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (info.isHost) AIHub.finish({ standings: [info.players.map(p => p.id)] }); });\n296\t    AIHub.on('end', () => game.audio.mute());\n297\t  }\n298\t  game.start({ scenes: { play }, scene: 'play', boot: { title: GAME_TITLE.trim(), steps: [['The 3D engine', () => W3.init(game)], ['The valley', buildWorld]] } });\n299\t  if (info) { await game.booted; AIHub.ready(); }\n300\t  window.__game = { game, get world() { return world; }, get hero() { return hero; } };"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23de6e6b-3ae6-4bf5-9764-44b18bb5857c","uuid":"20280a5e-ebb6-4bab-be81-30779bf8216b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:28:51.720Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211953__xee4d12/work/PLAN.md","content":"# PLAN: an over-the-shoulder action-horror game inspired by the source\n\nYou build this alone, from this plan and TASK.md. Nobody can answer questions, so where this plan leaves something open, decide and move on.\n\n## 0. How to use this plan\n\n- **TASK.md is the authority** on rules, deliverables and file names. This plan makes the creative and technical choices TASK.md leaves open, so you don't have to debate them again. If you find something better, change it, but keep the pillars (§1) and everything TASK.md requires.\n- **The title is yours.** TASK.md says how to pick it. Nothing in this plan depends on it: the world, story and code read one title file (`src/title.txt`) and name the title nowhere else. Riffs that suit a wine-country setting are welcome in your brainstorm.\n- **Paths** are relative to your dev folder. \"The single HTML file\" and \"the exit interview\" are the deliverables TASK.md names.\n- **[verified]** means the plan's author ran it on this computer on 2026-11-04 against my-3D2dge v0.88.0 and AI Hub client 1.4.0, and it worked as written. Don't re-investigate those; build on them.\n- **Read in this order:** TASK.md, this plan, then the header of `engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js` (the 3D manual, 260 lines) and `engine/API.md`. Search `engine/API-INDEX.md` for names; don't read it whole.\n- **Keep `NOTES.md`** in the dev folder as you go: issues your tests caught (count them, and mark the game-breaking ones), where you got stuck, what you changed in the engine and why. TASK.md asks for these at the end, and you won't remember them.\n\n## 1. The game\n\n**Pitch.** Days before a state dinner, the President's personal sommelier is kidnapped on a buying trip. Special Agent Vera Cask of the U.S. Excise Bureau goes in alone, on a regional train, to a valley in the Grand Duchy of Vaudrenia, where the harvest has gone wrong: a fungus called the Noble Bloom got into the grapes, and then into the people. She shoots, kicks and haggles her way through a village, a château and a bottling plant, keeping a fearless, insufferable 71-year-old snob alive, to stop the Last Pressing: a vintage that would carry the Bloom to every state dinner on Earth.\n\n**Pillars.** When a choice is unclear, the one that serves these wins.\n\n1. **Every shot is a decision.** Feet planted, a laser dot that wobbles. Head, knee and arm each do something different, and each opens a different follow-up.\n2. **Crowds, not waves.** Enemies come on slowly, spread out, surround you and cut you off. Space is the resource you spend.\n3. **Protect the worst person you've ever met.** Ambrose is useful, brave, fragile and rude. The player should want to save him and want to strangle him.\n4. **Greed between the terror.** Crates, treasure, a duty-free trolley that shouldn't exist, upgrades, arranging your case. Neon means safe.\n5. **Deadpan pulp.** Scary for twenty seconds, then someone says something stupid with total sincerity.\n6. **Keep escalating.** Something new every five minutes: a toy, an enemy, a set piece.\n\n**What we take from the source, and how we make it our own.** TASK.md asks for what makes the source distinctive, turned into an *original* game. Mechanics and genre conventions are fair game. Its specifics are not.\n\n| What makes the source distinctive | Our original version |\n|---|---|\n| A lone agent, a rescue, a remote Old World backwater | A federal excise agent, the President's sommelier, a wine valley in a fictional duchy |\n| Possessed rural folk, then aristocrats, then a militarised finale | The Pressed (vineyard folk), the Confraternity of the Last Pressing at Château Rémuage, Vane Beverages' bottling plant and private security |\n| Over-the-shoulder aim with planted feet; body-part hits open melee | The same genre mechanics with our own moves and numbers: KICK, SLAM, FRISK |\n| A parasite that bursts out when the host \"dies\" | The Noble Bloom: magenta fungal growths, with our own variants (tendril, puffball, crawler) |\n| An escort who can wait, hide and get carried off | Ambrose Pell: his Nose finds hidden enemies and weak points, and he tastes his way through puzzles |\n| A wandering merchant, weapon tuning, a grid case, treasure sets | The Duty-Free Man and his neon-lit trolley, an evidence case, wine treasures you combine |\n| Save points as a ritual | Passport stamps at old customs desks |\n| Button prompts in the middle of the action | Prompts everywhere, and one set piece built on them: The Toast |\n| Cheesy one-liners, operatic villains on the radio | §11, written fresh |\n\n**Must stay original (hard rule).** No character, place, organisation, item name, enemy design, boss design, line of dialogue, tune, level layout or logo from the source or its series. Don't echo its famous lines, even as a wink. Don't recreate its specific rooms or set pieces beat for beat: if a scene feels like a copy of a remembered one, change the place, the trigger and the payoff. The source's name appears only where TASK.md asks: the title riff and the Source Information. Lay out levels from §12, not from memory of any game.\n\n## 2. Decisions at a glance\n\n| TASK.md item | Decision |\n|---|---|\n| Genre | Over-the-shoulder action horror: a third-person shooter with a survival-horror economy, escort, puzzles and set pieces. A co-op score-attack mode, Last Stand, sits beside the campaign. |\n| Perspective | Third person, over the right shoulder (swappable), tighter when aiming. |\n| Title | Yours: 50 riffs in your head, then a real RNG (`node -e \"console.log(require('crypto').randomInt(50))\"`). Write the winner to `src/title.txt`. |\n| Research | Done for you here for engine, hub and design. Do more only if you hit a gap, and report what you actually did. |\n| Package | One self-contained HTML file: both engines, three.js, Rapier, clips and game inlined, about 6 to 9 MB. No CDN and no downloads, so it runs offline from `file://` and inside the hub. **[verified]** |\n| Tech stack | my-3D2dge v0.88.0: the 2D engine from the handoff package plus its **real-3D add-on `E.World3D`** (three.js r182, Rapier 0.19.3), bundled with esbuild. The handoff README itself sends real-3D games to this add-on. Do not build this on the 2D views. |\n| Art direction | The engine's own look: code-drawn, toon-banded low-poly, chunky pixel textures at 16 pixels a metre, a pixel-font HUD, fog and strong lighting. New shapes, materials and bodies for the wine country; store and core props for generic things (§10). |\n| Animation | The engine's own systems: its procedural soldier skeleton (IK feet, hands on gun) and its motion-clip store in readable key poses, drawn as pen bodies. New clips and poses for our signature moves (§5). |\n| Audio | All Web Audio from code, on the engine's buses. Music slider defaults to 10% **[verified recipe]**. Gibberish voices per speaker (§14). |\n| Online | AI Hub Session Protocol v1, `shared-world`, 1 to 4 players: the Last Stand round. On its own: solo Last Stand and 2-player couch split-screen (§16). |\n| Performance | Out of scope. Add the detail, enemies, effects, lights and shadows the scene needs. The one exception: a hub round must become ready inside the hub's load limit (§16). |\n| Testing | One command, failures and a one-line count only (§17). |\n| Effort | Spend it where §18 says it shows. |\n\n**Working rules from TASK.md, applied.** Everything stays in your own folder (not `/tmp`, not a parent). Read only what you need; other agents work beside you and share the machine's ports and processes. One or two browsers at once. Prefer `file://`. The only server you need is for the hub suite (§17): `127.0.0.1`, a port the OS picks, confirm the page is yours, stop it by its own PID. Never `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`. Extra Python packages only via `uv` as TASK.md describes.\n\n## 3. Tech setup (all [verified])\n\n### 3.1 Get the engine (2 seconds, 16 MB; a full clone takes minutes and 150 MB)\n\nRun from the dev folder. The `engine/` tree mirrors the repository's so that the tools' relative paths still work.\n\n```sh\ngit clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --no-checkout https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git .repo\ngit -C .repo sparse-checkout set --no-cone '/dist/handoff/' '/dist/my-3d2dge-3d.js' '/vendor/' '/src/starter3d/' '/src/mocap/' '/tools/anim-set.mjs' '/tools/mocap-lib.mjs' '/tools/kit3d-test.mjs' '/docs/MOCAP.md' '/docs/ENGINE-3D.md'\ngit -C .repo checkout -q main\nmkdir -p engine lib/hub tools src assets tests\ncp -r .repo/dist/handoff/. engine/\ncp .repo/dist/my-3d2dge-3d.js engine/\ncp -r .repo/vendor engine/vendor\ncp -r .repo/src/starter3d .repo/src/mocap engine/src/\ncp .repo/tools/anim-set.mjs .repo/tools/mocap-lib.mjs .repo/tools/kit3d-test.mjs engine/tools/\ncp .repo/docs/MOCAP.md .repo/docs/ENGINE-3D.md engine/docs/\nrm -rf .repo\nnpm init -y >/dev/null && npm install --no-audit --no-fund playwright@1.63.0\nfor f in session.js harness.html bridge.js round.js README.md; do curl -fsSL \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f\" -o \"lib/hub/$f\"; done\n```\n\nNever run `npx playwright install`, even though the handoff README says to: the browsers are already on this computer, and TASK.md forbids it. You may edit anything under `engine/`.\n\nFiles to copy from, not read whole:\n\n- `engine/src/starter3d/30-shooter.js`: the over-the-shoulder camera, look, gunplay, soldier skeleton, tracers, decals, ladders, mantles, gunmen's AI.\n- `engine/src/starter3d/40-horror.js`: doors, keys, item box, saves, grabs, flow-field AI, and a bot that plays a whole game.\n- `engine/src/starter3d/00-shell.js`: what those two expect around them.\n\n### 3.2 Folder layout\n\n```\nengine/   the engine, its docs, tools and asset store     lib/hub/  session client and test harness, unmodified\nassets/   clips.js (cut clips), sets.js (cut asset sets)  tools/    build.mjs, patch-engine.mjs, level-check.mjs\ntests/    run.mjs, suites/                                .build/   bundler output (not a deliverable)\nsrc/      title.txt, main.js, and:\n  core/    config, Tune table, Run state, registry (def), events, FEATURES, about data\n  body/    soldier pose, clip pose, looks, drawers, hit zones\n  player/  controller, camera, weapons, melee, grenades, traversal\n  ai/      director, one file per enemy, bosses/, ally (Ambrose)\n  world/   materials, shapes, legend, zone loader, doors, links, barricades, pickups, encounters\n  zones/   one data file per zone (pure data, so Node tests can import them)\n  ui/      prompts, focus, hud, case, trolley, map, passport, results, title, about, dev, gameover\n  story/   dialog, voices, cutscene helpers, qte, lines/\n  audio/   sfx, music engine, songs/\n  modes/   campaign, laststand, net (hub), attract, bots\n```\n\n### 3.3 The build\n\n**`tools/build.mjs`**\n\n```js\n// node tools/build.mjs <path of the single HTML file>   (run from the dev folder)\nimport { readFileSync as read, writeFileSync as write, mkdirSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';\nimport { resolve } from 'node:path';\nconst out = process.argv[2], V = resolve('engine/vendor'), T3 = V + '/three-0.182.0', txt = f => read(f, 'utf8');\nconst esc = s => s.replace(/<\\/script/gi, '<\\\\/script');   // a script's text must not close its tag early\nmkdirSync('.build', { recursive: true });\nexecFileSync('esbuild', ['src/main.js', '--bundle', '--format=esm', '--target=es2022', '--legal-comments=none', '--minify-syntax', '--minify-whitespace', '--loader:.txt=text',\n  `--alias:three/webgpu=${T3}/three.webgpu.min.js`, `--alias:three/tsl=${T3}/three.tsl.min.js`, `--alias:three=${T3}/three.webgpu.min.js`,\n  `--alias:@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat=${V}/rapier3d-simd-compat-0.19.3/rapier.js`, '--outfile=.build/game.js', '--log-level=warning'], { stdio: 'inherit' });\nconst classic = ['engine/my-3d2dge.js', 'engine/src/mocap/readable.js', 'engine/src/mocap/mocap.js', 'assets/clips.js'];   // cut asset sets go here too\nconst html = `<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<script>${txt('lib/hub/session.js')}</script>\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"><meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\"><meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\"><meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Survive the harvest and outscore your crew\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move WASD/stick, aim right click/L2, fire left click/R2, kick E/Cross\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\"><title>${txt('src/title.txt').trim()}</title>\n<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; overflow: hidden; background: #000 }</style></head><body>\n<div id=\"stage\" style=\"position:relative;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:hidden\"><canvas id=\"view\"></canvas><canvas id=\"screen\" style=\"position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%\"></canvas></div>\n${classic.map(f => `<script>${esc(txt(f))}</script>`).join('\\n')}\n<script>if (!self.GPUShaderStage) self.GPUShaderStage = { VERTEX: 1, FRAGMENT: 2, COMPUTE: 4 };</script>\n<script type=\"module\">${esc(txt('.build/game.js'))}</script></body></html>`;\nwrite(out, html); console.log('wrote ' + out + ' ' + (html.length / 1e6).toFixed(1) + ' MB');\n```\n\nWhy it looks like this:\n\n- `session.js` must be the first script, right after `<meta charset>`, pasted unmodified. The hub swaps in new versions by matching it.\n- The `GPUShaderStage` line is required. Without it, three's WebGPU build crashes on load in browsers with no WebGPU, such as Firefox on Linux.\n- Inline module scripts run fine on `file://`. Rapier's wasm is embedded as base64, so nothing is fetched.\n- The kit's determinism hash came out **identical on Chromium (WebGL 2 and WebGPU), WebKit and Firefox** from a file built this way.\n\n### 3.4 Two engine patches: apply once, right after §3.1\n\n**Without the first patch the game crashes on every zone change on real players' machines.** `world.dispose()` throws inside three on WebGPU, which is what Chromium uses on any machine with a GPU, and WebGL-only tests never see it. The second patch lets the attract mode show behind the touch-only notice, as TASK.md wants. Record both in `NOTES.md`: TASK.md asks what you changed in the engine.\n\n**`tools/patch-engine.mjs`**\n\n```js\n// node tools/patch-engine.mjs   (run once from the dev folder, right after getting the engine)\nimport { readFileSync as read, writeFileSync as write } from 'node:fs';\nconst patch = (file, from, to) => { const s = read(file, 'utf8'); if (!s.includes(from)) throw new Error(`patch: not found in ${file}: ${from.slice(0, 60)}`); write(file, s.replace(from, to)); };\n// 1. world.dispose() throws inside three on WebGPU: dispose each thing once, and let one failure not stop the rest\npatch('engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js',\n`    this.scene.traverse(o => { if (o.isMesh) { o.geometry && o.geometry.dispose(); } });\n    for (const x of this._owned) if (x && x.dispose) x.dispose();`,\n`    const gone = new Set(), safely = x => { if (!x || !x.dispose || gone.has(x)) return; gone.add(x); try { x.dispose(); } catch (e) { /* WebGPU: nothing was uploaded to destroy */ } };\n    this.scene.traverse(o => { if (o.isMesh) safely(o.geometry); });\n    for (const x of this._owned) safely(x);`);\n// 2. the touch-only notice hid the attract mode behind 88% black: make it lighter, and put it at the bottom\npatch('engine/my-3d2dge.js',\n  'display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:24px;text-align:center;background:rgba(5,3,12,.88)',\n  'display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:center;padding:24px;text-align:center;background:rgba(5,3,12,.35)');\nconsole.log('engine patched');\n```\n\n### 3.5 First boot: start from this\n\nPaste it into `src/main.js`, put any title in `src/title.txt`, run the patch, cut the clips, build, and open the file. You get a dusk village in real 3D, an over-the-shoulder camera with mouse and right stick, planted-feet aiming with a laser, a crowd that comes on by flow field, and a hub round that passes all four harness cases. **Grow this into the game; don't start again from an empty file.** Its look (sky, fog, sun, `outlines: false`, `res: 'balanced'`) is the agreed starting point.\n\n```sh\nnode tools/patch-engine.mjs\necho 'ANY TITLE FOR NOW' > src/title.txt\n(cd engine && node tools/anim-set.mjs src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js src/mocap/sets/mesh2motion.js src/mocap/sets/cmu.js --name CLIPS --out ../assets/clips.js --clips \"QUATERNIUS:Idle_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Walk_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Walk_Formal_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Jog_Fwd_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Sprint_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Idle_FoldArms_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Idle_Talking_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Idle_Lantern_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Idle_Rail_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Sitting_Idle_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Sitting_Talking_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Zombie_Idle_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Zombie_Walk_Fwd_Loop,CMU:Zombie_Walk_Loop,CMU:Wounded_Walk_Loop,CMU:Hurt_Stomach_Walk_Loop,CMU:Looking_Around,QUATERNIUS:Zombie_Scratch,CMU:Chop_Wood,QUATERNIUS:Melee_Hook,QUATERNIUS:OverhandThrow,QUATERNIUS:Sword_Dash_RM,QUATERNIUS:Idle_Shield_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Idle_Shield_Break,QUATERNIUS:Hit_Chest,QUATERNIUS:Hit_Head,MESH2MOTION:Dizzy,MESH2MOTION:Kneeling Tired,QUATERNIUS:Hit_Knockback,QUATERNIUS:LayToIdle,CMU:Fall_On_Face,CMU:Get_Up_Face_Down,QUATERNIUS:Death01,MESH2MOTION:Death_A,MESH2MOTION:Death_B,MESH2MOTION:Death_C,MESH2MOTION:Defend,CMU:Duck_Thrown_Object,MESH2MOTION:Crawl,MESH2MOTION:Climb Ladder,QUATERNIUS:ClimbUp_1m_RM,CMU:Run_Jump_Over,MESH2MOTION:Land_Three_Point,QUATERNIUS:Push_Loop,CMU:Roundhouse_Kick,CMU:Side_Kick,CMU:Front_Kick,QUATERNIUS:Consume,CMU:Drink_Water,QUATERNIUS:PickUp_Table,QUATERNIUS:Walk_Carry_Loop,CMU:Carry_Heavy_Box,MESH2MOTION:Greeting\")\n```\n\nThat is 53 clips and 350 KB. Add more whenever you need them (`engine/src/mocap/catalogs/*.json` describes every clip).\n\n**`src/main.js`**\n\n```js\n// The first boot: real 3D on one file, an over-the-shoulder camera, a clip-driven pen body, the hub's round. Grow it into the game.\nimport '../engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js';   // first: it adds E.World3D to the 2D engine\nimport GAME_TITLE from './title.txt';\nconst E = My3D2dge, W3 = E.World3D, PI = Math.PI, hubOn = AIHub.active;\n\nconst KEYS = { up: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'Pad12'], down: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'Pad13'], left: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'Pad14'], right: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'Pad15'],\n  aim: ['Mouse2', 'Pad6'], fire: ['Mouse0', 'Pad7'], act: ['KeyE', 'Space', 'Pad0'], sprint: ['ShiftLeft', 'Pad1'],\n  start: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Pad9'], pause: ['Escape', 'KeyP', 'Pad9'], confirm: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Pad0'], cancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'Pad1'] };\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, bg: null, input: KEYS, touch: 'never', autoPause: !hubOn, live: hubOn, menu: { quit: false, settings: [\n  ...W3.SETTINGS.filter(s => s.key !== 'look3d').map(s => s.key === 'picture3d' ? { ...s, value: 'balanced' } : s),\n  { key: 'music', value: .1 },   // the Music slider starts at 10%\n  { key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['xbox', 'Xbox']] }] } });\n\n/* ---- materials and shapes of our own: a material's fn returns [r, g, b] (a hex string bakes black) ---- */\nconst hx = E.hex;\nW3.SIDE.plaster = { w: 32, h: 48, fn(x, y) {   // lime plaster over timber, a rubble course below\n  const z = 47 - y; if (x % 16 < 2 || z > 44 || (z > 14 && z < 17)) return hx(E.hash2(x, y) < .2 ? '#3a2616' : '#4c3220');\n  if (z < 14) { const r = Math.floor(z / 5), off = r % 2 ? 3 : 0; return hx((x + off) % 7 === 0 || z % 5 === 0 ? '#3a3630' : E.hash2(((x + off) / 7) | 0, r) < .4 ? '#6e675a' : '#7f7768'); }\n  return hx(E.hash2(x * 3, y * 7) < .07 ? '#a89a7c' : E.hash2(x, y) < .15 ? '#d6c8a4' : '#c8bb96'); } };\nW3.GROUND.cobble = (x, y) => { const h = E.hash2(Math.floor(x / 5), Math.floor(y / 5)), k = 70 + h * 34; return x % 5 < 1 || y % 5 < 1 ? [46, 40, 34] : [k + 8, k, k - 8]; };\nE.SHAPES.roofA = { about: 'gable roof', mats: { r: 'shingle' }, parts: [['prism', 'r', [0, 0, 0], [[-50, -1], [50, -1], [0, 44]], 131, { axis: 'x' }]] };\nE.SHAPES.vinerow = { about: 'trained vines on posts and wire, heavy with fruit', mats: { p: 'walnut', l: 'leaves', g: '#4a2348 glaze' }, parts: [['row', 5, [16, 0, 0], ['box', 'p', [0, 0, 0], [1.5, 1.5, 26]]], ['box', 'l', [0, 0, 11], [68, 6, 15]], ['row', 9, [8, 0, 0], ['ball', 'g', [0, 3.6, 12], 2.1]], ['row', 9, [8, 0, 0], ['ball', 'g', [4, -3.6, 13], 2]]] };\nE.SHAPES.press = { about: 'a great wooden wine press: slatted basket, iron screw, beam', mats: { w: 'oak', i: 'iron', d: 'walnut' }, parts: [['cyl', 'w', [0, 0, 0], 22, 22], ['ring', 12, 22.5, ['box', 'd', [0, 0, 0], [3, 2, 23]]], ['cyl', 'i', [0, 0, 14], 3, 56], ['box', 'd', [0, 0, 56], [64, 7, 7]], ['mirror', 'x', ['box', 'd', [30, 0, 0], [7, 7, 62]]], ['cyl', 'i', [0, 0, 22], 21, 2]] };\n\n/* ---- a level is text, one character a metre. W: a window (sill and lintel, an opening you see and shoot through) ---- */\nconst LEVEL = { rows: [\n  'vvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv',\n  'v......................................................v',\n  'v..V.......V.......V......................V.......V....v',\n  'v......,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,.........v',\n  'v...HHWHHHHW,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,HHHWHH.......v',\n  'v...H......H,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,H.....H......v',\n  'v...H......W,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,W.....H......v',\n  'v...H......H,,,,,,,z,,,,,,,,,,,,,z,,,,,,,,H.....W......v',\n  'v...H.......,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,.....H......v',\n  'v...H......H,,,,z,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,z,,,,,,H.....H......v',\n  'v...HHHHHHHH,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,HHHHHHH......v',\n  'v......,,,,,,,,,,z,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,z,,,,,,,,,,,,.........v',\n  'v...B..,,,,c,,,,,,z,,,,,,,,,,,,z,,,,,,,,c,,,,,..B......v',\n  'v......,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,.........v',\n  'v......,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,@,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,.........v',\n  'v......,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,.........v',\n  'v..V.......V.......V......................V.......V....v',\n  'v......................................................v',\n  'vvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv'],\n  ground: 'dirt', colors: { base: '#4c4a2c', dark: '#3e3f26', light: '#5a5632' }, legend: {\n    v: { wall: 96, side: 'earth', color: '#2a2a24', top: '#20261c' }, ',': { ground: 'cobble' }, H: { wall: 48, side: 'plaster', top: '#5a3a2a' },\n    W: { wall: 14, side: 'plaster', platform: 48, thick: 16 }, V: { shape: 'vinerow', solid: true }, B: { shape: 'barrel' }, c: { shape: 'cart', facing: .6, ground: 'cobble' },\n    z: { mark: 'z', ground: 'cobble' }, '@': { mark: 'start', ground: 'cobble' } } };\n\n/* ---- a body: motion clips drive body points (millimetres, forward/right/up), the pen draws limbs over them ---- */\nconst lib = Mocap.load(MOCAP.CLIPS), MM = .016, buf = new Float32Array(lib.P * 3);   // 16 units a metre\nconst add = (a, b, k = 1) => [a[0] + b[0] * k, a[1] + b[1] * k, a[2] + b[2] * k], sub = (a, b) => [a[0] - b[0], a[1] - b[1], a[2] - b[2]], nrm = a => { const l = Math.hypot(...a) || 1; return [a[0] / l, a[1] / l, a[2] / l]; };\nfunction drawBody(pen, a, X, c) {\n  const co = Math.cos(a.facing), si = Math.sin(a.facing), P = n => { const i = lib.idx[n] * 3, f = X[i] * MM, r = X[i + 1] * MM; return [a.x + co * f - si * r, a.y + si * f + co * r, a.z + X[i + 2] * MM]; };\n  const tube = (p, q, r, col) => pen.tube(p[0], p[1], p[2], q[0], q[1], q[2], r, col), ball = (p, r, col) => pen.ball(p[0], p[1], p[2], r, r, r, col), slab = (p, q, ac, w, t, col) => pen.slab(p[0], p[1], p[2], q[0], q[1], q[2], ac[0], ac[1], ac[2], w, t, col);\n  const pel = P('pelvis'), che = P('chest'), nek = P('neck'), hed = P('head'), top = P('headTop'), face = nrm(sub(P('faceF'), hed)), rt = nrm(sub(P('shR'), P('shL'))), rtP = nrm(sub(P('hipR'), P('hipL'))), up = nrm(sub(top, hed));\n  for (const s of 'LR') { const kn = P('knee' + s), an = P('ankle' + s); tube(P('hip' + s), kn, 2, c.pants); tube(kn, an, 1.4, c.pants); ball(kn, 1.5, c.pants); slab(add(an, [0, 0, -.6]), add(P('toe' + s), [0, 0, .3]), rt, 2.3, 1.6, c.boot); }\n  slab(add(pel, [0, 0, .4]), che, rtP, 6.6, 4.2, c.shirt); slab(che, nek, rt, 7, 3.9, c.shirt); slab(add(pel, rtP, -3.1), add(pel, rtP, 3.1), face, 3.4, 4.3, c.belt);\n  for (const s of 'LR') { const sh = P('sh' + s), el = P('elbow' + s), wr = P('wrist' + s); ball(sh, 1.9, c.shirt); tube(sh, el, 1.35, c.shirt); tube(el, wr, 1.1, c.skin); ball(P('fist' + s), 1.1, c.skin); }\n  tube(nek, hed, 1, c.skin); const hc = add(hed, sub(top, hed), .45); pen.ball(hc[0], hc[1], hc[2], 2.2, 2.2, 2.5, c.skin); const cap = add(hc, up, .9); pen.ball(cap[0], cap[1], cap[2], 2.45, 2.45, 1.9, c.hair);\n  if (c.eyes) for (const k of [-1, 1]) { const e = add(add(hc, face, 2.05), rt, k * .85); pen.glow(e[0], e[1], e[2], .34, c.eyes); }\n}\nconst VERA = { skin: '#d8ae8c', hair: '#2a1c14', shirt: '#2e3e58', pants: '#23242c', boot: '#17140f', belt: '#3a2a1a' }, PICKER = { skin: '#b89a80', hair: '#4a3a24', shirt: '#7a6a4c', pants: '#3a3430', boot: '#231f1b', belt: '#2a2018', eyes: '#ff5a2a' };\n\n/* ---- the world and one scene: over the shoulder, feet planted to aim, the crowd comes on ---- */\nlet world, flow, hero, crowd = [], yaw = -PI / 2, pitch = -.05, aimK = 0, heroT = 0, sendT = 0, info = null;\nconst mouse = [0, 0], dir = [0, 0], focus = { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 };\nfunction buildWorld() {\n  world = new W3(game, { level: LEVEL, res: 'balanced', outlines: false, sky: ['#27284a', '#e8955a'], fog: { color: '#b07a5a', near: 180, far: 900 }, ambient: ['#a4a8d0', '#6a5038', 2.1],\n    sun: { color: '#ffb070', intensity: 2.6, dir: [.72, .42, -.45], area: 900, shadow: true, map: 2048 }, lights: 2, camera: { mode: 'fixed', capture: true }, onDraw: w => {\n      for (const e of crowd) { lib.sample(lib.clip(Math.hypot(e.vx, e.vy) > 4 ? 'Zombie_Walk_Loop' : 'Zombie_Idle_Loop'), e.data.t, buf); drawBody(w.pen, e, buf, PICKER); }\n      if (!hero) return; lib.sample(lib.clip(aimK > .5 ? 'Idle_Loop' : Math.hypot(hero.vx, hero.vy) > 8 ? 'Jog_Fwd_Loop' : 'Idle_Loop'), heroT, buf); drawBody(w.pen, hero, buf, VERA);\n      if (aimK > .5) { const cp = Math.cos(pitch), d = [Math.cos(yaw) * cp, Math.sin(yaw) * cp, Math.sin(pitch)], o = [hero.x + d[0] * 8, hero.y + d[1] * 8, hero.z + 21], hit = w.ray(o[0], o[1], o[2], d[0], d[1], d[2], 600, { skip: hero }), L = hit ? hit.dist : 600, p = add(o, d, L); w.pen.bar(o[0], o[1], o[2], p[0], p[1], p[2], .3, .3, '#ff2a1a'); w.pen.glow(p[0], p[1], p[2], 1, '#ff3a2a'); }\n    } });\n  world.prepare();\n}\nconst play = { pausable: true, view: 'iso',\n  enter() {\n    world.reset(); flow = world.flow(); world.shape('press', 27.5 * 16, 7.5 * 16, 0, { solid: true }); world.shape('roofA', 8 * 16, 7.5 * 16, 48, { facing: 0 });   // (world.reset takes these away: place them again)\n    const s = world.marks.start[0]; hero = info && info.server ? null : world.hero({ x: s.x, y: s.y, r: 4.5, half: 9, visible: false, shadow: false });\n    crowd = world.marks.z.map((m, i) => { const e = world.mob({ x: m.x, y: m.y, r: 5, half: 8, visible: false, shadow: false }); e.data.t = i * .37; return e; });\n    world.camera.set('fixed'); world.camera.follow(hero || crowd[0]); world.camera.target = focus;\n  },\n  update(dt) {\n    const I = game.input, h = hero;\n    if (h) {\n      world.camera.takeMouse(mouse); yaw += mouse[0] * .0021; pitch = E.clamp(pitch - mouse[1] * .0021, -1.2, 1.2);\n      const a = I.padAim; if (a) { yaw += a[0] * 2.4 * dt; pitch = E.clamp(pitch - a[1] * 1.8 * dt, -1.2, 1.2); }\n      aimK = E.approach(aimK, I.down('aim') ? 1 : 0, dt * 6); heroT += dt;\n      const m = I.move(), fx = Math.cos(yaw), fy = Math.sin(yaw), sp = aimK > .05 ? 0 : I.down('sprint') ? 88 : 52, mx = fx * -m[1] - fy * m[0], my = fy * -m[1] + fx * m[0];\n      h.vx = E.approach(h.vx, mx * sp, 700 * dt); h.vy = E.approach(h.vy, my * sp, 700 * dt);\n      if (aimK > .05) h.facing = yaw; else if (Math.hypot(mx, my) > .1) h.facing = E.approachAng(h.facing, Math.atan2(my, mx), dt * 10);\n      const cp = Math.cos(pitch), f = [fx * cp, fy * cp, Math.sin(pitch)], piv = [h.x - fy * 12, h.y + fx * 12, h.z + 31], want = E.lerp(42, 30, aimK), ray = world.ray(piv[0], piv[1], piv[2], -f[0], -f[1], -f[2], want + 4, { skip: h, level: true }), d = ray ? Math.max(6, ray.dist - 3) : want;\n      world.camera.fixed = { x: piv[0] - f[0] * d, y: piv[1] - f[1] * d, z: piv[2] - f[2] * d, yaw, pitch, roll: 0, fov: E.lerp(60, 46, aimK), near: 2 };\n      focus.x = h.x + fx * 320; focus.y = h.y + fy * 320; focus.z = h.z + 10;\n    } else world.camera.fixed = { x: 400, y: 500, z: 200, yaw: -PI / 2, pitch: -.5, roll: 0, fov: 60, near: 2 };\n    if (!info || info.isHost) { flow.to(h ? h.x : 400, h ? h.y : 200); for (const e of crowd) { e.data.t += dt; const near = h && Math.hypot(h.x - e.x, h.y - e.y) < 26; if (!near && flow.dir(e.x, e.y, dir)) { e.vx = dir[0] * 24; e.vy = dir[1] * 24; e.facing = E.approachAng(e.facing, Math.atan2(dir[1], dir[0]), dt * 4); } else e.vx = e.vy = 0; } }\n    if (info && AIHub.time() > -3000 && (sendT -= dt) <= 0) { sendT = 1 / 12; AIHub.send(info.isHost ? { t: 's', e: crowd.map(e => [Math.round(e.x), Math.round(e.y)]) } : { t: 'i', x: h ? Math.round(h.x) : 0, y: h ? Math.round(h.y) : 0 }, info.isHost ? { reliable: false } : { to: info.host, reliable: false }); }\n    world.step(dt);\n  },\n  draw(r) { world.draw(r); r.overlay(g => E.font.text(g, GAME_TITLE.trim(), 8, r.H - 16, '#e8e0d0', { outline: '#000' })); }\n};\nasync function main() {\n  info = hubOn ? await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4] }) : null;\n  if (info) {\n    AIHub.on('message', (d, from) => { if (d.t === 's' && !info.isHost) d.e.forEach(([x, y], i) => crowd[i] && crowd[i].place(x, y, crowd[i].z)); });\n    AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (info.isHost) AIHub.finish({ standings: [info.players.map(p => p.id)] }); });\n    AIHub.on('end', () => game.audio.mute());\n  }\n  game.start({ scenes: { play }, scene: 'play', boot: { title: GAME_TITLE.trim(), steps: [['The 3D engine', () => W3.init(game)], ['The valley', buildWorld]] } });\n  if (info) { await game.booted; AIHub.ready(); }\n  window.__game = { game, get world() { return world; }, get hero() { return hero; } };","numLines":300,"startLine":1,"totalLines":994}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Tc9UvW9E4jGGbVPwP4iGuB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
