{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016LLR91bEd1t6zxZbEKS4Gy","type":"tool_result","content":"686:      // o.expand: the resolution is the least the screen shows, and the picture grows on both sides to fill the window\n725:  // the screen filter over the canvas: a dark line under each of the game's rows (a third of it), and for 'crt' each\n740:  /** browser client coords -> projected screen pixels (same space as view.p) */\n1121:  /** a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false,\n1159:  /** browser client coords -> screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space, with no camera), or null without a canvas */\n2314:   * - expand: true makes res the least the screen shows and grows the picture to fill the window, any shape, no bars\n2565:    on(window, 'pointerup', e => {   // (a browser goes full screen only from a tap: this one, or a game started by it)\n3051:  filter: { group: 'Display', label: 'Screen filter', type: 'select', value: 'clean', options: [['clean', 'Clean'], ['scanlines', 'Scanlines'], ['crt', 'CRT']], help: 'Scanlines: the dark lines between a TV\\'s rows. CRT: those, its colored stripes and its\n3149:  /** game.fullscreen: the whole page full screen (the game, its menus and buttons), where the browser can */\n3159:  /** true when the page was opened from a home screen as an app (no browser bars: nothing to go full screen from) */\nevalmachine.<anonymous>:1374\n  _glyph(f, ch) { return f.glyphs[f.upper ? ch.toUpperCase() : ch] || f.glyphs[ch.toUpperCase()] || f.glyphs['?']; },\n                           ^\n\nTypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'glyphs')\n    at Object._glyph (evalmachine.<anonymous>:1374:28)\n    at [eval]:4:60\n    at runScriptInThisContext (node:internal/vm:219:10)\n    at node:internal/process/execution:451:12\n    at [eval]-wrapper:6:24\n    at runScriptInContext (node:internal/process/execution:449:60)\n    at evalFunction (node:internal/process/execution:283:30)\n    at evalTypeScript (node:internal/process/execution:295:3)\n    at node:internal/main/eval_string:71:3\n\nNode.js v24.22.1\n    only 2 distinct colors on screen (PS1-era scenes use 100+) in \"after play\": shade with E.tones, add a backdrop, textured tiles and props\n    100% of the screen is one flat color in \"after play\": fill it with an E.Backdrop, textured tiles or props\n    low contrast in \"after play\" (luma spread 0): darker shadows, brighter highlights\n  1 error(s):\n    After pressing start, the screen stayed one flat color the whole time: nothing is drawn where the camera looks (check game.focus, level.draw / map.drawFloor, and that the play scene draws).\n  screenshots and report.json in /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211953__xee4d12/work/_research/dryrun/run2/dev/.build/check","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23de6e6b-3ae6-4bf5-9764-44b18bb5857c","uuid":"a81ed37c-4c2a-4063-9281-c17764867717","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:32:28.953Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"686:      // o.expand: the resolution is the least the screen shows, and the picture grows on both sides to fill the window\n725:  // the screen filter over the canvas: a dark line under each of the game's rows (a third of it), and for 'crt' each\n740:  /** browser client coords -> projected screen pixels (same space as view.p) */\n1121:  /** a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false,\n1159:  /** browser client coords -> screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space, with no camera), or null without a canvas */\n2314:   * - expand: true makes res the least the screen shows and grows the picture to fill the window, any shape, no bars\n2565:    on(window, 'pointerup', e => {   // (a browser goes full screen only from a tap: this one, or a game started by it)\n3051:  filter: { group: 'Display', label: 'Screen filter', t