{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjEeEqFQUwQXzkptDvmr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012SnvjSRHbdm2Y2rUWky8rD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211953__xee4d12/work/_research/dryrun/plan-files; cat > apply1.py <<'PY'\nplan = '../../../PLAN.md'\ns = open(plan, encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(old, new, count=1):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old) >= 1, 'not found: ' + old[:70]\n    s = s.replace(old, new) if count == 0 else s.replace(old, new, count)\n# versions\nrep(\"against my-3D2dge v0.88.0 and AI Hub client 1.4.0, and it worked as written.\", \"against my-3D2dge v0.89.1 and AI Hub client 1.4.0, and it worked as written.\")\nrep(\"my-3D2dge v0.88.0: the 2D engine from the handoff package plus its\", \"my-3D2dge (v0.89.1 when this was written): the 2D engine from the handoff package plus its\")\nrep(\"- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.88.0 with World3D,\", \"- **Tech:** my-3D2dge (the version on `engine/API.md`'s first line) with World3D,\")\n# setup: the changelog too, and main moves\nrep(\"'/tools/kit3d-test.mjs' '/docs/MOCAP.md' '/docs/ENGINE-3D.md'\", \"'/tools/kit3d-test.mjs' '/docs/MOCAP.md' '/docs/ENGINE-3D.md' '/CHANGELOG.md'\")\nrep(\"cp .repo/docs/MOCAP.md .repo/docs/ENGINE-3D.md engine/docs/\", \"cp .repo/docs/MOCAP.md .repo/docs/ENGINE-3D.md .repo/CHANGELOG.md engine/docs/\")\nrep(\"Never run `npx playwright install`, even though the handoff README says to: the browsers are already on this computer, and TASK.md forbids it. You may edit anything under `engine/`.\",\n\"Never run `npx playwright install`, even though the handoff README says to: the browsers are already on this computer, and TASK.md forbids it. You may edit anything under `engine/`.\\n\\n**The setup takes `main`, as TASK.md links, and `main` moves:** it gained TV menus and sound loops while this plan was being written. `engine/API.md`'s first line says what you got, and the top of `engine/docs/CHANGELOG.md` says what changed since v0.89.1. If a recipe here breaks and you can't quickly see why, go back to the commit it was verified on: after the `sparse-checkout` line, run `git -C .repo fetch -q --depth 1 --filter=blob:none origin 8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691` and check out `FETCH_HEAD` instead of `main`.\")\n# patch tool: never blocks\nrep(\"const patch = (file, from, to) => { const s = read(file, 'utf8'); if (!s.includes(from)) throw new Error(`patch: not found in ${file}: ${from.slice(0, 60)}`); write(file, s.replace(from, to)); };\",\n    \"const patch = (file, from, to) => { const s = read(file, 'utf8'); if (s.includes(from)) write(file, s.replace(from, to)); else console.log(`patch skipped, the engine has changed here (fixed upstream? the webgpu suite will say): ${from.slice(0, 60)}`); };\")\nrep(\"console.log('engine patched');\\n\", \"\")\n# first boot: TV menus, and the settings' short pages\nrep(\"autoPause: !hubOn, live: hubOn, menu: { quit: false, settings: [\", \"autoPause: !hubOn, live: hubOn, menu: { quit: false, items: [['Sound', () => ui.show('sound')], ['Controller', () => ui.show('pad')]], settings: [\")\nrep(\"\"\"  { key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['xbox', 'Xbox']] }] } });\n\"\"\", \"\"\"  { key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['xbox', 'Xbox']] }] } });\n// Ten feet: the engine's menus at TV size (14 px text without this), without their small print, and settings on short pages\nconst ui = new E.Shell(game, { tv: true, screens: { sound: { title: 'Sound', rows: ['sound', 'volume', 'music', 'effects'] }, pad: { title: 'Controller', rows: ['glyphs', 'invertY', 'deadzone', 'rumble'] } } });\ndocument.head.appendChild(Object.assign(document.createElement('style'), { textContent: '.esh-row small{display:none}' }));\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"You get a dusk village in real 3D, an over-the-shoulder camera with mouse and right stick, planted-feet aiming with a laser, a crowd that comes on by flow field, and a hub round that passes all four harness cases.\",\n    \"You get a dusk village in real 3D, an over-the-shoulder camera with mouse and right stick, planted-feet aiming with a laser, a crowd that comes on by flow field, the engine's menus at TV size, and a hub round that passes all four harness cases.\")\n# barks: the font has no guillemets\nrep(\"Show them on screen rarely, in invented words: «Vendanj!» «Pressho, pressho!» «Ombrelu!»\", \"Show them on screen rarely, in invented words: \\\"Vendanj!\\\", \\\"Pressho, pressho!\\\", \\\"Ombrelu!\\\"\")\n# 10-foot rules\nrep(\"- Everything is canvas pixel UI (`E.font`, `E.ui`, sprites, `r.overlay`) in game pixels. At 1080p that is **[verified]** 480×270, so one default font row is about 2.6% of the screen height, which reads at 10 feet.\\n\",\n\"\"\"- The game's own screens and HUD are canvas pixel UI (`E.font`, `E.ui`, sprites, `r.overlay`) in game pixels. At 1080p that is **[verified]** 480×270, so one default font row is about 2.6% of the screen height, which reads at 10 feet.\n- The engine's menus (pause, settings, controls) are HTML overlays with 14 px text and paragraphs of help: fine on a desk, unreadable on a TV. **`new E.Shell(game, { tv: true })` scales them to about 30 px at 1080p, and §3.5 also hides their small print [verified].** Colour them with its `theme` (`ink, paper, accent, muted, line, font, titleFont`). Add short pages with `screens: { sound: { title: 'Sound', rows: [...] } }` and `ui.show('sound')`. The setting keys are `fullscreen frameRate showFps filter sound volume music effects background audioOffset motion shake flashes deadzone invertY invertMoveX invertMoveY glyphs rumble picture3d shadows3d filter3d`, plus yours.\n- The pixel font draws ASCII, the face buttons, arrows, ★ ♥ ♪ ✓ … ° € £, curly quotes, dashes and accented Latin letters (Château Rémuage is fine). Anything else draws as `?`, so no « ».\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"- **Pause:** the engine's menu (`menu: { items: [['Map', ...], ['Dev mode', ...], ['About & Credits', ...]], settings: [...], controls: {...}, quit: 'title' }`).\",\n    \"- **Pause:** the engine's menu at TV size (`menu: { items: [['Map', ...], ['Sound', ...], ['Controller', ...], ['Dev mode', ...], ['About & Credits', ...]], settings: [...], controls: {...}, quit: 'title' }`).\")\nrep(\"- **Settings:** the engine's (Display, Sound, Comfort, Controller), plus yours:\", \"- **Settings:** the engine's (Display, Sound, Comfort, Controller; `tv: true`), plus yours:\")\n# audio: the engine's newer helpers\nrep(\"(original compositions; the engine's song format with `layer`, `audio.music(song, { fade })`, and your own instruments on the bus):\",\n    \"(original compositions; the engine's song format with `layer` and `audio.music(song, { fade })`, and your own instruments: `audio.instrument('fiddle', (ctx, bus, time, freq, dur, vol) => ...)` makes a `wave` a track can use):\")\nrep(\"Keep an `sfx` table so one line defines one sound. Use the engine's `A.define` where it's enough, your own nodes where it isn't.\",\n    \"Keep an `sfx` table so one line defines one sound. Use the engine's `A.define` where it's enough, your own nodes where it isn't. Loops (a motor, rain, the sign's buzz): `const h = audio.sfx(sound, { loop: true, pan })`, then `h.set({ pan, vol })` and `h.stop(.3)`. A pitch that follows the rev needs your own nodes.\")\n# attract: the idle timer\nrep(\"**Attract mode.** On the title and its menus, 10 s without input starts it. It loops\", \"**Attract mode.** On the title and its menus, 10 s without input starts it (`game.hook('input', fn)` runs every step, menus and all: a natural idle timer). It loops\")\n# ui suite\nrep(\"Every screen opens and closes by pad and by keyboard. |\", \"Every screen opens and closes by pad and by keyboard. The engine's menus are at TV scale. |\")\nopen(plan, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('applied; bytes', len(s.encode()))\nPY\npython3 apply1.py; cd ..; rm -rf run3; mkdir -p run3/dev; python3 plan-files/extract.py ../../PLAN.md run3/dev && cd run3/dev && bash .setup.sh 2>&1 | tail -1 && bash .firstboot.sh 2>&1 | tail -1 && node tools/build.mjs ../game.html; head -1 engine/API.md | cut -c1-60; ls engine/docs | tr '\\n' ' '; echo; cp ../../run2/dev/tests/verify.mjs tests/verify.mjs; python3 - <<'EOF'\ns = open('tests/verify.mjs').read()\n# add: the TV menus through the real pause menu, with hover and a click\ns = s.replace(\"await pg.waitForTimeout(800); await pg.screenshot({ path: '../shot-1080.png' });\", \"\"\"await pg.waitForTimeout(800); await pg.screenshot({ path: '../shot-1080.png' });\n  await pg.keyboard.press('Escape'); await pg.waitForTimeout(500);\n  const menu = await pg.evaluate(() => { const el = [...document.querySelectorAll('.esh-mod button')], fs = getComputedStyle(el[0]).fontSize, tr = document.querySelector('.esh').style.transform; return { labels: el.map(b => b.textContent), fs, tr }; }); console.log(JSON.stringify(menu));\n  ok(menu.labels.join(' ').toUpperCase().includes('SOUND'), 'Sound in the pause menu'); ok(/scale\\\\(2\\\\.1/.test(menu.tr), 'menus at TV scale', menu.tr);\n  const box = await pg.evaluate(() => { const b = [...document.querySelectorAll('.esh-mod button')].find(x => /sound/i.test(x.textContent)), r = b.getBoundingClientRect(); return [r.x + r.width / 2, r.y + r.height / 2]; });\n  await pg.mouse.move(box[0], box[1]); await pg.waitForTimeout(200); const hovered = await pg.evaluate(() => /sound/i.test(document.activeElement && document.activeElement.textContent || '')); ok(hovered, 'mouse hover moves the focus in the pause menu');\n  await pg.mouse.click(box[0], box[1]); await pg.waitForTimeout(400); const h2 = await pg.evaluate(() => { const hs = [...document.querySelectorAll('.esh h2')]; return hs.map(h => h.textContent).join('|'); }); ok(/Sound/.test(h2), 'click opens the Sound page', h2);\n  const music = await pg.evaluate(() => { const rows = [...document.querySelectorAll('.esh-row')].map(r => r.textContent); return rows.join(' / '); }); console.log(music.slice(0, 120)); ok(/Music\\\\s*10%/.test(music), 'Sound page shows Music 10%', music.slice(0, 80)); await pg.screenshot({ path: '../shot-sound.png' });\n  await pg.keyboard.press('Escape'); await pg.waitForTimeout(250); await pg.keyboard.press('Escape'); await pg.waitForTimeout(300);\"\"\")\nopen('tests/verify.mjs','w').write(s)\nEOF\ntimeout 500 node tests/verify.mjs 2>&1 | cut -c1-420 | tail -22","description":"Apply the plan updates and rerun the full verification from scratch","timeout":560000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3617,"cache_read_input_tokens":680694,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3617},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23de6e6b-3ae6-4bf5-9764-44b18bb5857c","uuid":"b62bc2d9-4883-4c94-8028-c96b33d99ca1","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:34:39.534Z","request_id":"req_011CgjEeEWeDXdfsrANtuqHK","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012SnvjSRHbdm2Y2rUWky8rD":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211953__xee4d12/work/_research/dryrun/plan-files; cat > apply1.py <<'PY'\nplan = '../../../PLAN.md'\ns = open(plan, encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(old, new, count=1):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old) >= 1, 'not found: ' + old[:70]\n    s = s.replace(old, new) if count == 0 else s.replace(old, new, count)\n# versions\nrep(\"against my-3D2dge v0.88.0 and AI Hub client 1.4.0, and it worked as written.\", \"against my-3D2dge v0.89.1 and AI Hub client 1.4.0, and it worked as written.\")\nrep(\"my-3D2dge v0.88.0: the 2D engine from the handoff package plus its\", \"my-3D2dge (v0.89.1 when this was written): the 2D engine from the handoff package plus its\")\nrep(\"- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.88.0 with World3D,\", \"- **Tech:** my-3D2dge (the version on `engine/API.md`'s first line) with World3D,\")\n# setup: the changelog too, and main moves\nrep(\"'/tools/kit3d-test.mjs' '/docs/MOCAP.md' '/docs/ENGINE-3D.md'\", \"'/tools/kit3d-test.mjs' '/docs/MOCAP.md' '/docs/ENGINE-3D.md' '/CHANGELOG.md'\")\nrep(\"cp .repo/docs/MOCAP.md .repo/docs/ENGINE-3D.md engine/docs/\", \"cp .repo/docs/MOCAP.md .repo/docs/ENGINE-3D.md .repo/CHANGELOG.md engine/docs/\")\nrep(\"Never run `npx playwright install`, even though the handoff README says to: the browsers are already on this computer, and TASK.md forbids it. You may edit anything under `engine/`.\",\n\"Never run `npx playwright install`, even though the handoff README says to: the browsers are already on this computer, and TASK.md forbids it. You may edit anything under `engine/`.\\n\\n**The setup takes `main`, as TASK.md links, and `main` moves:** it gained TV menus and sound loops while this plan was being written. `engine/API.md`'s first line says what you got, and the top of `engine/docs/CHANGELOG.md` says what changed since v0.89.1. If a recipe here breaks and you can't quickly see why, go back to the commit it was verified on: after the `sparse-checkout` line, run `git -C .repo fetch -q --depth 1 --filter=blob:none origin 8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691` and check out `FETCH_HEAD` instead of `main`.\")\n# patch tool: never blocks\nrep(\"const patch = (file, from, to) => { const s = read(file, 'utf8'); if (!s.includes(from)) throw new Error(`patch: not found in ${file}: ${from.slice(0, 60)}`); write(file, s.replace(from, to)); };\",\n    \"const patch = (file, from, to) => { const s = read(file, 'utf8'); if (s.includes(from)) write(file, s.replace(from, to)); else console.log(`patch skipped, the engine has changed here (fixed upstream? the webgpu suite will say): ${from.slice(0, 60)}`); };\")\nrep(\"console.log('engine patched');\\n\", \"\")\n# first boot: TV menus, and the settings' short pages\nrep(\"autoPause: !hubOn, live: hubOn, menu: { quit: false, settings: [\", \"autoPause: !hubOn, live: hubOn, menu: { quit: false, items: [['Sound', () => ui.show('sound')], ['Controller', () => ui.show('pad')]], settings: [\")\nrep(\"\"\"  { key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['xbox', 'Xbox']] }] } });\n\"\"\", \"\"\"  { key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['xbox', 'Xbox']] }] } });\n// Ten feet: the engine's menus at TV size (14 px text without this), without their small print, and settings on short pages\nconst ui = new E.Shell(game, { tv: true, screens: { sound: { title: 'Sound', rows: ['sound', 'volume', 'music', 'effects'] }, pad: { title: 'Controller', rows: ['glyphs', 'invertY', 'deadzone', 'rumble'] } } });\ndocument.head.appendChild(Object.assign(document.createElement('style'), { textContent: '.esh-row small{display:none}' }));\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"You get a dusk village in real 3D, an over-the-shoulder camera with mouse and right stick, planted-feet aiming with a laser, a crowd that comes on by flow field, and a hub round that passes all four harness cases.\",\n    \"You get a dusk village in real 3D, an over-the-shoulder camera with mouse and right stick, planted-feet aiming with a laser, a crowd that comes on by flow field, the engine's menus at TV size, and a hub round that passes all four harness cases.\")\n# barks: the font has no guillemets\nrep(\"Show them on screen rarely, in invented words: «Vendanj!» «Pressho, pressho!» «Ombrelu!»\", \"Show them on screen rarely, in invented words: \\\"Vendanj!\\\", \\\"Pressho, pressho!\\\", \\\"Ombrelu!\\\"\")\n# 10-foot rules\nrep(\"- Everything is canvas pixel UI (`E.font`, `E.ui`, sprites, `r.overlay`) in game pixels. At 1080p that is **[verified]** 480×270, so one default font row is about 2.6% of the screen height, which reads at 10 feet.\\n\",\n\"\"\"- The game's own screens and HUD are canvas pixel UI (`E.font`, `E.ui`, sprites, `r.overlay`) in game pixels. At 1080p that is **[verified]** 480×270, so one default font row is about 2.6% of the screen height, which reads at 10 feet.\n- The engine's menus (pause, settings, controls) are HTML overlays with 14 px text and paragraphs of help: fine on a desk, unreadable on a TV. **`new E.Shell(game, { tv: true })` scales them to about 30 px at 1080p, and §3.5 also hides their small print [verified].** Colour them with its `theme` (`ink, paper, accent, muted, line, font, titleFont`). Add short pages with `screens: { sound: { title: 'Sound', rows: [...] } }` and `ui.show('sound')`. The setting keys are `fullscreen frameRate showFps filter sound volume music effects background audioOffset motion shake flashes deadzone invertY invertMoveX invertMoveY glyphs rumble picture3d shadows3d filter3d`, plus yours.\n- The pixel font draws ASCII, the face buttons, arrows, ★ ♥ ♪ ✓ … ° € £, curly quotes, dashes and accented Latin letters (Château Rémuage is fine). Anything else draws as `?`, so no « ».\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"- **Pause:** the engine's menu (`menu: { items: [['Map', ...], ['Dev mode', ...], ['About & Credits', ...]], settings: [...], controls: {...}, quit: 'title' }`).\",\n    \"- **Pause:** the engine's menu at TV size (`menu: { items: [['Map', ...], ['Sound', ...], ['Controller', ...], ['Dev mode', ...], ['About & Credits', ...]], settings: [...], controls: {...}, quit: 'title' }`).\")\nrep(\"- **Settings:** the engine's (Display, Sound, Comfort, Controller), plus yours:\", \"- **Settings:** the engine's (Display, Sound, Comfort, Controller; `tv: true`), plus yours:\")\n# audio: the engine's newer helpers\nrep(\"(original compositions; the engine's song format with `layer`, `audio.music(song, { fade })`, and your own instruments on the bus):\",\n    \"(original compositions; the engine's song format with `layer` and `audio.music(song, { fade })`, and your own instruments: `audio.instrument('fiddle', (ctx, bus, time, freq, dur, vol) => ...)` makes a `wave` a track can use):\")\nrep(\"Keep an `sfx` table so one line defines one sound. Use the engine's `A.define` where it's enough, your own nodes where it isn't.\",\n    \"Keep an `sfx` table so one line defines one sound. Use the engine's `A.define` where it's enough, your own nodes where it isn't. Loops (a motor, rain, the sign's buzz): `const h = audio.sfx(sound, { loop: true, pan })`, then `h.set({ pan, vol })` and `h.stop(.3)`. A pitch that follows the rev needs your own nodes.\")\n# attract: the idle timer\nrep(\"**Attract mode.** On the title and its menus, 10 s without input starts it. It loops\", \"**Attract mode.** On the title and its menus, 10 s without input starts it (`game.hook('input', fn)` runs every step, menus and all: a natural idle timer). It loops\")\n# ui suite\nrep(\"Every screen opens and closes by pad and by keyboard. |\", \"Every screen opens and closes by pad and by keyboard. The engine's menus are at TV scale. |\")\nopen(plan, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('applied; bytes', len(s.encode()))\nPY\npython3 apply1.py; cd ..; rm -rf run3; mkdir -p run3/dev; python3 plan-files/extract.py ../../PLAN.md run3/dev && cd run3/dev && bash .setup.sh 2>&1 | tail -1 && bash .firstboot.sh 2>&1 | tail -1 && node tools/build.mjs ../game.html; head -1 engine/API.md | cut -c1-60; ls engine/docs | tr '\\n' ' '; echo; cp ../../run2/dev/tests/verify.mjs tests/verify.mjs; python3 - <<'EOF'\ns = open('tests/verify.mjs').read()\n# add: the TV menus through the real pause menu, with hover and a click\ns = s.replace(\"await pg.waitForTimeout(800); await pg.screenshot({ path: '../shot-1080.png' });\", \"\"\"await pg.waitForTimeout(800); await pg.screenshot({ path: '../shot-1080.png' });\n  await pg.keyboard.press('Escape'); await pg.waitForTimeout(500);\n  const menu = await pg.evaluate(() => { const el = [...document.querySelectorAll('.esh-mod button')], fs = getComputedStyle(el[0]).fontSize, tr = document.querySelector('.esh').style.transform; return { labels: el.map(b => b.textContent), fs, tr }; }); console.log(JSON.stringify(menu));\n  ok(menu.labels.join(' ').toUpperCase().includes('SOUND'), 'Sound in the pause menu'); ok(/scale\\\\(2\\\\.1/.test(menu.tr), 'menus at TV scale', menu.tr);\n  const box = await pg.evaluate(() => { const b = [...document.querySelectorAll('.esh-mod button')].find(x => /sound/i.test(x.textContent)), r = b.getBoundingClientRect(); return [r.x + r.width / 2, r.y + r.height / 2]; });\n  await pg.mouse.move(box[0], box[1]); await pg.waitForTimeout(200); const hovered = await pg.evaluate(() => /sound/i.test(document.activeElement && document.activeElement.textContent || '')); ok(hovered, 'mouse hover moves the focus in the pause menu');\n  await pg.mouse.click(box[0], box[1]); await pg.waitForTimeout(400); const h2 = await pg.evaluate(() => { const hs = [...document.querySelectorAll('.esh h2')]; return hs.map(h => h.textContent).join('|'); }); ok(/Sound/.test(h2), 'click opens the Sound page', h2);\n  const music = await pg.evaluate(() => { const rows = [...document.querySelectorAll('.esh-row')].map(r => r.textContent); return rows.join(' / '); }); console.log(music.slice(0, 120)); ok(/Music\\\\s*10%/.test(music), 'Sound page shows Music 10%', music.slice(0, 80)); await pg.screenshot({ path: '../shot-sound.png' });\n  await pg.keyboard.press('Escape'); await pg.waitForTimeout(250); await pg.keyboard.press('Escape'); await pg.waitForTimeout(300);\"\"\")\nopen('tests/verify.mjs','w').write(s)\nEOF\ntimeout 500 node tests/verify.mjs 2>&1 | cut -c1-420 | tail -22","description":"Apply the plan updates and rerun the full verification from scratch","timeout":560000}}}
